{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials","id":427250,"title":"Post-publishing and fan-made materials","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-03T19:39:43-08:00","id":427250,"title":"Post-publishing and fan-made materials","content":"Greetings all.<br /> I just wanted to see what resources for the trinity/continuum universe might fall out if i gave the tree a shake. My inspiration here is to track down any loose gems i may have missed myself over the years - since i have just had The New Flesh pointed out to me (fingers crossed for Bright Continent). For reference, the bits i've found for myself (in a 'completed' state) include;<br /> Note: some of these documents are fairly short, non-canon or otherwise dubiously gathered from the internet, but i've included them for completeness-sake. Apologies for the lack of credit where due, i have mostly taken anything that wasn't nailed down and spent little time reminiscing where or when precisely i obtained them.<br /> <br /> <u>Trinity</u><br /> Absolute Zero Player's Guide (discussed briefly with CHILL in another thread)<br /> Asia Ascendant<br /> Awaiting Inspiration<br /> Battleground: Players Guide (semi official, but unpublished)<br /> BioGenesis<br /> Field Report: Corporate Life (official, but only ever released online)<br /> Field Report: Noetic Science (Can't believe i forgot this one, thanks KingOfDreams)<br /> Field Report: Oceania (same as Corporate Life, above)<br /> Frantically French (authored by KingOfDreams, PM either of us for a copy of the updated version.)<br /> Hidden Between Asteroids<br /> India Underground<br /> In His Majesties Service<br /> Storyteller's Guide (.pdf assembled below, by from. Thanks again to Mr. Watson and everyone else who worked on it.)<br /> Technology Index<br /> <br /> <u>Aberrant</u><br /> <a href=\"http://www.dark-kingdom.org/Aberrant/abtoc.htm\" target=\"_blank\">1,001 Aberrant Nights</a> (Thanks One Vorlon)<br /> 3rd World War<br /> A Breed Apart<br /> Aberrant Companion<br /> Aberrant Compendium (not the same as the Companion. Thanks, Sreden)<br /> Brainwaves<br /> Forceful Personalities<br /> Nova Census<br /> Nova Tech<br /> Outbreak<br /> The New Flesh (thank you, Sreden)<br /> <br /> <u>Adventure!</u><br /> Awaiting Inspiration (also listed under Trinity, above)<br /> <a href=\"http://digital.raven.tripod.com/rp/mystics.html\" target=\"_blank\">Mystics!</a> (crossover rules for Sorcery Revised, Thanks Mythic Fox.)<br /> <br /> CHILL has made a respectable number of mixed resources available through <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B6FYbpbzU8JCfjdWVmQyQjFyaml5VVBVc2lGWGVLZEQ1YzFTbkVtN0VfUHhSLW9idl9yV0U&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the EON archive</a>, posted on the second page of this thread. Sincere thanks for the effort, CHILL.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you know anything about these creations or have more to add to the list, please, let us know in here. If any i list here have become unavailable, let me know if i can help you get a look.<br /> <br /> A few notes;<br /> JSnead made notes about Qin character generation that i've gleefully managed to fish out of my archives.<br /> I once read there was a map of the Germanic states in 2120 out there somewhere, but i've never been able to track it down.<br /> CHILL has lost his page borders, but if anyone has something similar i would be interested.<br /> Until i personally see evidence of <i>Trial by Fire</i>, i have to assume it never really got that far.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your consideration and all the contributors to this thread for assisting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  1,001 Aberrant Nights added. 03-30-2015, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T00:33:56-08:00","id":427505,"title":"","content":"I'd have to dig it up, as I think I still have a copy, but once upon a time in the distant past, someone came up with a fan-made rules hack for incorporating the hedge magic and such from Sorcery Revised (A cWoD supplement) into Adventure! for a variety of Inspired that performs a sort of spellcasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T00:52:01-08:00","id":427511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials#post427250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asia Ascendant</div> </div> </div> </div>Contracted, written, line cancelled before it was fully developed. I personally consider it canon, but YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Corporate Life </div> </div> </div>Official. Free PDF from the WW site, released between the Trinity Players Guide and Aurora Australis. <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/File:TFRCorpLife.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Hosted here</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oceania </div> </div> </div>Official. Free PDF from the WW site, released between Stellar Frontier and Alien Enounter 2. <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/93096?affiliate_id=13\" target=\"_blank\">Available on DTRPG</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Storyteller's Guide (although i can't find a handy pdf to print out) </div> </div> </div>Mine, actually. Never completed, unfortunately, so I only released a few sample snippets rather than the whole book as PDF (since the whole book doesn't exist). You can, however, view the content as-is <a href=\"http://rpgbooks.wikia.com/wiki/Trinity_Storytellers_Handbook\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. This project may be part of the reason I am where I am today.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Brainwaves </div> </div> </div>Like Asia Ascendant, contracted, but never completed. <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20050829090124/http://members.aol.com/talonstudio/brainwaves/\" target=\"_blank\">Original content here</a>, assembled by fans into a <a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/files/file/1-aberrant-brainwaves/\" target=\"_blank\">PDF here</a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T10:39:15-08:00","id":427828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials#post427250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Poor Adventure!, i didn't find any fan supplements for it over the years, although i remember reading some loose outlines for Trial by Fire, if anyone has leads on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trial by Fire was one on the list for EON - but aside from a couple paragraphs outline it never went anywhere - so that one is definitely dead.<br /> <br /> RPGPost.com has the archive of basically everything that was on EON - but its a bit difficult to use sometimes and logins can be challenging (mine refuses to work, and the password reset is hosed). I do have, I think, all of the EON stuff somewhere in a backup. <br /> <br /> I should probably dump copies of the PDFs in a Google Drive for everyone. A lot were HTML pages that are not as user friendly, but I guess I can dump them in there too. Would anyone find that useful?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T20:22:10-08:00","id":428475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=427505#post427505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to dig it up, as I think I still have a copy, but once upon a time in the distant past, someone came up with a fan-made rules hack for incorporating the hedge magic and such from Sorcery Revised (A cWoD supplement) into Adventure! for a variety of Inspired that performs a sort of spellcasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something as opposed to nothing would be better for poor Adventure!, please let me know if it ever shows up. Thanks for mentioning it, i'd never heard of that one before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=427511#post427511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mine, actually. Never completed, unfortunately, so I only released a few sample snippets rather than the whole book as PDF (since the whole book doesn't exist). You can, however, view the content as-is. This project may be part of the reason I am where I am today.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to keep the more or less official ones up there, just for completeness sake, but thinking back i remember getting CorpLife and Oceania from (i believe) the white wolf website. They weren't fan-made or post-publishing as i stipulated, but some may be unaware of their existance and the goal of the thread is to shed light on anything readers may not be aware was produced. I hope this doesn't offend anyone.<br /> Thanks for the details. Did you have to look this up or are those things just cocked and loaded, ready to go? The fact that you know all this shows there was way more information out there about this stuff. I heard rumours of a rift in the development team after Bates left too, is there somewhere the behind-the-scenes drama is detailed? Gossip really isn't in my wheelhouse, but to get the whole picture of this game, it may be required reading...<br /> What's your secret? Eidetic memory? Too much time on your hands? Being paid to do it? (so much envy, the goggles do nothing -smile-)<br /> The ST guide really is something else though - so ambitious and deeply scoped that i'm not surprised it never got finished (i knew i should have volunteered, but i never knew how -sigh-). But i'm glad someone from the online Trinity community eventually got to pick up the torch and i'm really excited to see where this Onyx Path thing goes. Even in an unfinished state, the ST guide for Trinity was one of the setting's most meaty supplements.<br /> I wish i had known there was an effort toward this going on before i randomly stumbled across it in a web-search - when everything slowed down over the last few years i took my fandom inwards, you seem to be the ultimate result of focussing the fandom outwards. So i must offer my deepest congratulations and appreciation for the efforts you've put into the setting over the years - even on the few occasions where i personally disagreed with your vision. -smile-<br /> I hope your time with Onyx Path is productive and meaningful, for both you and the setting. And know that many of us would be seething with jealousy if your grasp on the setting wasn't so complete. Thanks again for the loan of your top-down perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=427828#post427828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trial by Fire was one on the list for EON - but aside from a couple paragraphs outline it never went anywhere - so that one is definitely dead.<br /> <br /> RPGPost.com has the archive of basically everything that was on EON - but its a bit difficult to use sometimes and logins can be challenging (mine refuses to work, and the password reset is hosed). I do have, I think, all of the EON stuff somewhere in a backup.<br /> <br /> I should probably dump copies of the PDFs in a Google Drive for everyone. A lot were HTML pages that are not as user friendly, but I guess I can dump them in there too. Would anyone find that useful?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pity for TBF, but there was so little to go on with Adventure! that it was really easily interpreted differently by each reader. Same with our discussions of naked Aeon/Trinity as it was publised, prior to the universe calcifying around it, it took the individual ST/players to ultimately define it. Meaning each of the potential Fan-Authors may have had a different interpretation of the era.<br /> -shrug-<br /> Do you happen to know what became of Bright Continent? I think that was Eon's main Trinity project at the time i was there and you know how i like to try to use EVERYTHING published for that setting, however unlikely. -blush-<br /> I just took a look on RPGPost after Sreden mentioned the New Flesh was there in another thread, while it's a useful depository, i raided Eon for everything i could get my hands on. I'd always intended to start contributing art or writing to them, but real-life kept popping in to change my priorities. RPGPost messed up my login details too, but i straightened it out. I'll make note of my account details, since you have experienced trouble yourself.<br /> I would find that Google Drive an interesting browse, HTML can be loaded into a browser of even some document-creators - so there are no barriers there. I like to have hard-copies, with e-copies saved to my physical drive a close second. But a mess of pdfs and unsorted html elements could make for a confusing ftp list of assets - so a little work to make the file-structure user-friendly could make a difference if you decide to go in for this. Of course, try not to post anything that still makes a profit for this tremendous setting.<br /> If you can set up a drive that is publically available you can serve as a kind of book depository for the setting - at least for those reading this forum who have no desire to give RPGPost any personal details. I can contribute a few loose bits of b&amp;w art (see avatar), but most of my work on the setting was pre-digital. So i'm hardly original content rich here...<br /> P.S. For those interested, CHILL wrote the Absolute Zero Player's Guide. Thanks again CHILL.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T22:29:27-08:00","id":428704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428475#post428475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the details. Did you have to look this up or are those things just cocked and loaded, ready to go? The fact that you know all this shows there was way more information out there about this stuff. I heard rumours of a rift in the development team after Bates left too, is there somewhere the behind-the-scenes drama is detailed? Gossip really isn't in my wheelhouse, but to get the whole picture of this game, it may be required reading...<br /> What's your secret? Eidetic memory? Too much time on your hands? Being paid to do it? (so much envy, the goggles do nothing -smile-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sort of the unofficial White Wolf historian. I spent a long time putting together the unofficial <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\">White Wolf Wiki</a>, with a particular focus on stuff I liked: Mage: The Ascension and the Trinity Universe. I was also friends with developer Bruce Baugh at the time (still am). A lot of it is first-hand knowledge or second-hand information, which I recorded on the Wiki.<br /> <br /> There was no rift in the dev team to the best of my knowledge. Baugh and Bates co-developed Adventure!, after all, and Bates and Blackwelder co-developed Mummy: The Resurrection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ST guide really is something else though - so ambitious and deeply scoped that i'm not surprised it never got finished (i knew i should have volunteered, but i never knew how -sigh-). But i'm glad someone from the online Trinity community eventually got to pick up the torch and i'm really excited to see where this Onyx Path thing goes. Even in an unfinished state, the ST guide for Trinity was one of the setting's most meaty supplements. </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Glad you like it. Fun fact: another Trinity fan who worked on the STH is Stew Wilson, who later went on to do some writing for Werewolf: The Forsaken. He's currently developer on both Forsaken and Werewolf: The Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wish i had known there was an effort toward this going on before i randomly stumbled across it in a web-search - when everything slowed down over the last few years i took my fandom inwards, you seem to be the ultimate result of focussing the fandom outwards. So i must offer my deepest congratulations and appreciation for the efforts you've put into the setting over the years - even on the few occasions where i personally disagreed with your vision. -smile-<br /> I hope your time with Onyx Path is productive and meaningful, for both you and the setting. And know that many of us would be seething with jealousy if your grasp on the setting wasn't so complete. Thanks again for the loan of your top-down perspective. </div> </div> </div>Thanks. We're doing our best, and I hope people like what we've got in store.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you happen to know what became of Bright Continent? I think that was Eon's main Trinity project at the time i was there and you know how i like to try to use EVERYTHING published for that setting, however unlikely. -blush- </div> </div> </div>Bright Continent was a region/order book planned to follow after Asia Ascendant, detailing the United African Nations and a new psi order formed of the cast-offs of the other orders (I think the Upeo's Star-Crossed were supposed to form their nucleus). I wouldn't be surprised if EON tried to make their own version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just took a look on RPGPost after Sreden mentioned the New Flesh was there in another thread, while it's a useful depository, i raided Eon for everything i could get my hands on. I'd always intended to start contributing art or writing to them, but real-life kept popping in to change my priorities. RPGPost messed up my login details too, but i straightened it out. I'll make note of my account details, since you have experienced trouble yourself. </div> </div> </div>I can still log in with my own RPGpost account, but it's consistently denied access to even read anything, as though it's been banned. I never got a notification about it. In any case if I'm not welcome there, so be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T10:22:19-08:00","id":428951,"title":"","content":"I'll see about tracking down my EON archive and dumping it in a GDrive folder then. Leave that with me for a few days.<br /> <br /> As for Bright Continent - nope - not an EON thing. That was a planned official publication (see Ian's response). While I was managing it EON had no plans to do a 'Bright Continent'. I tried to nudge EON away from doing what could be mistaken for official publications. With India Underground the noise at the time was that Chibs / India were unlikely to get much love so IU seemed OK to run with. <br /> <br /> I handed over EON to others way back in 2003 though. I stepped back from any involvement from that point, so I have no idea if there were later plans to do something covering that topic / with the lines being cancelled. Don't recall ever seeing anything though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428704#post428704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can still log in with my own RPGpost account, but it's consistently denied access to even read anything, as though it's been banned. I never got a notification about it. In any case if I'm not welcome there, so be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's mostly the thing same thing that I see, its hit and miss. I think there's just software issues there - unless we're both blocked of course, hah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T21:14:56-08:00","id":429796,"title":"","content":"Being a member at RPGPost.com I can say you are both welcome. You could try talking to Chosen/Matt about getting the accounts fixed. Bright Continent was being worked on as a fan product (and still is sporadically) as well as the Nexus which is appears to me to be a STH for the entire continuity. Sprocket has been working to get it finished as a capstone on the old system before the new versions begin any form of open development.<br /> <br /> PS - if you are listing the Companion you might as well add <a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/files/file/5-aberrant-compendium/\" target=\"_blank\">the compendium</a> as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4074-sreden","user":"Sreden","date":". 03-06-2015, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4074-sreden","name":"Sreden","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T00:30:04-08:00","id":429931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428704#post428704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sort of the unofficial White Wolf historian. I spent a long time putting together the unofficial <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\">White Wolf Wiki</a>, with a particular focus on stuff I liked: Mage: The Ascension and the Trinity Universe. I was also friends with developer Bruce Baugh at the time (still am). A lot of it is first-hand knowledge or second-hand information, which I recorded on the Wiki.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've picked up on that in my time lurking over the years, makes sense. Bibliography leads to a unique kind of understanding. I make use of the Wiki whenever i'm writing for Trinity games, so that's an excellent resource as well - as far as i'm concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428704#post428704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was no rift in the dev team to the best of my knowledge. Baugh and Bates co-developed Adventure!, after all, and Bates and Blackwelder co-developed Mummy: The Resurrection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, your Wiki makes note of the Paramorph definition referring to two different visions between Baugh and Bates - which has lead to a lot of discussion between my players and i over the years. That's what i mean, but it's likely the proportions were exaggerated in my perspective. Out of interest, i tended toward Bates' view - just to en-richen baselines as PC choices.<br /> -shrug-<br /> As an aside, it always gives me a kick to see these guys add their $0.02 when they are about. I feel like i personally owe them something for the ungodly amount of fun i've had on their efforts over the years. Thanks for setting me straight here, Mr. Watson.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428704#post428704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! Glad you like it. Fun fact: another Trinity fan who worked on the STH is Stew Wilson, who later went on to do some writing for Werewolf: The Forsaken. He's currently developer on both Forsaken and Werewolf: The Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish i could look in on his new work, but i just don't have the available funds to collect WOD in the completeness i would like these days.<br /> I owned nearly every book i could find for oWOD, i kind of felt betrayed when all of it was rendered (partially) irrelevant and my more well off friends were picking up supplements and clan-books that were higher quality replacements for those i had dutifully purchased years earlier. But, i'm certain this is a common story among tabletop gamers, so excuse my whining.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428704#post428704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. We're doing our best, and I hope people like what we've got in store.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure it will be a welcome addition for us all regardless. I would like to make a personal plea to start with<br /> something splashy for us older players of the setting - the d20 republishing really fell down by not expanding the<br /> setting measurably when the chance availed itself. I don't blame anyone - the right sentiment was in play, but they could have forced me into buying if there was something more fresh being served up at the beginning there.<br /> Rather than single you out any more, i'd just like to spread thanks to everyone who reads this who played any part in keeping this setting going over the quiet years. It's an honour to stand with you all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428704#post428704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bright Continent was a region/order book planned to follow after Asia Ascendant, detailing the United African Nations and a new psi order formed of the cast-offs of the other orders (I think the Upeo's Star-Crossed were supposed to form their nucleus). I wouldn't be surprised if EON tried to make their own version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember seeing something, but i haven't kept anything about it, so there might not have been anything substantial. I was absolutely teeming with excitement for how the setting would fall on the future of Addis Ababa and the middle-east region, seeing how it was (still is) a political nightmare to anticipate, even a few years into the future.<br /> -distances self from middle-eastern politics-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428951#post428951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll see about tracking down my EON archive and dumping it in a GDrive folder then. Leave that with me for a few days.</div> </div> </div> </div>No rush, let me know if i can be of any assistance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428951#post428951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Bright Continent - nope - not an EON thing. That was a planned official publication (see Ian's response). While I was managing it EON had no plans to do a 'Bright Continent'. I tried to nudge EON away from doing what could be mistaken for official publications. With India Underground the noise at the time was that Chibs / India were unlikely to get much love so IU seemed OK to run with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any particular reason you preferred them not to do those those books? Just the hope that official versions would make it out eventually?<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Originally, updated rules for Inspired were going to be included as a small section of a new EON Order-Setting e-book (Bright Continent)</i>&quot;<br /> - Awaiting Inspiration, Introduction<br /> <br /> That's the only evidence i can find to support my claim. So, like i say, if anyone has any substantial samples of the actual work on BC (if any) to add to any potential depository - let us know before the information is lost to history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428951#post428951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I handed over EON to others way back in 2003 though. I stepped back from any involvement from that point, so I have no idea if there were later plans to do something covering that topic / with the lines being cancelled. Don't recall ever seeing anything though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn you are old-school.<br /> -smile-<br /> I really didn't even start looking into the TU online presence until years later - mostly inspired by the fact that the only additional content was coming from fans at that point. Which is one of the reasons why i have this thread, in case i've missed anything along the voyage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sreden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=429796#post429796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bright Continent was being worked on as a fan product (and still is sporadically) as well as the Nexus which is appears to me to be a STH for the entire continuity. Sprocket has been working to get it finished as a capstone on the old system before the new versions begin any form of open development.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's interesting, is there anywhere i can look in on this? 'Nexus' is something i've not heard of either, given how much i enjoyed the STH by Mr Watson, i'd like to see what (perhaps alternate) direction this Nexus is taking the setting. It sounds like a dangerous precedent to be working on old-system stuff when a new system is in the works. But, this is coming from someone who still breaks out some old-system writing to work on. I would be dong that right now, if this forum wasn't bleeding off my excess Trinity fandom. -blush-<br /> I'm a bit concerned about the split efforts between, but anything is better than nothing at this stage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sreden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=429796#post429796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS - if you are listing the Companion you might as well add <a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/files/file/5-aberrant-compendium/\" target=\"_blank\">the compendium</a> as well</div> </div> </div> </div>-Wonders what the difference is, goes to check.-<br /> RPGPost must have some weird coding, it sent me to the wrong page twice when i used the google link... Third time was the charm. It's a good site, but there seems to be a consensus growing here that it's unreliable.<br /> -shrug-<br /> I honestly hadn't realized these were separate documents, i think i might have combined them after i printed them out. I'll make the adjustment now, thanks for pointing that out.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the responses and tantalizing hints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Better formatted the quote from Awaiting Inspiration 03-06-2015, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:13:51-08:00","id":430232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=429931#post429931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any particular reason you preferred them not to do those those books? Just the hope that official versions would make it out eventually?<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Originally, updated rules for Inspired were going to be included as a small section of a new EON Order-Setting e-book (Bright Continent)</i>&quot;<br /> - Awaiting Inspiration, Introduction<br /> <br /> That's the only evidence i can find to support my claim. So, like i say, if anyone has any substantial samples of the actual work on BC (if any) to add to any potential depository - let us know before the information is lost to history.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Awaiting Inspiration was after I turned EON over to others, so can't really comment on that entry (I didn't even know about it until now, having never read AI). And from Sreden's comment above, it looks like the new gang decided to try and produce a version of Bright Continent. Around the time I handed over EON there was still some hope of continued support - and i'd prefered simply to avoid potentially misleading people into thinking we were doing anything that could possibly be mistaken as official. Not to mention, avoiding possibly inviting a cease-and-desist letter from the IP owners. But, after the lines were cancelled and some time had passed I can see why a version of Bright Continent might crop up from the fans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=429931#post429931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn you are old-school.<br /> -smile-<br /> I really didn't even start looking into the TU online presence until years later - mostly inspired by the fact that the only additional content was coming from fans at that point. Which is one of the reasons why i have this thread, in case i've missed anything along the voyage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha - I'm sure EON changed a lot once I'd handed it over, and even during my tenure it had.....5..... redesigns I think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Sreden</b><br /> You could try talking to Chosen/Matt about getting the accounts fixed. </div> </div> </div>Thanks Sreden, I did try PMing through RPGpost a while back, and it said I don't have permission to do that. Or search, read posts, post and a bunch of other stuff. I just kinda gave up. Would be nice if I could get back in, but is not that essential. Thanks though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T03:32:30-08:00","id":431186,"title":"","content":"So I spent most of the night doing ugly stuff to the Storyteller's Handbook. Here you go:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.megafileupload.com/en/file/616078/Trinity-Storytellers-Handbook-pdf.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.megafileupload.com/en/file/616078/Trinity-Storytellers-Handbook-pdf.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.megafileupload.com/en/file/616078/Trinity-Storytellers-Handbook-pdf.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.megafileupload.com/en/file/616078/Trinity-Storytellers-Handbook-pdf.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And my working file, ODT (OpenOffice format, though I worked in LibreOffice)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.megafileupload.com/en/file/616080/Trinity-Storytellers-Handbook-odt.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.megafileupload.com/en/file/616080/Trinity-Storytellers-Handbook-odt.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.megafileupload.com/en/file/616080/Trinity-Storytellers-Handbook-odt.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.megafileupload.com/en/file/616080/Trinity-Storytellers-Handbook-odt.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'll take them down ASAP if I ought to, but it felt somewhat helpful to present the wiki in an easily downloadable format.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5180-from","name":"from","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T09:38:07-08:00","id":431272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>from</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=431186#post431186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I spent most of the night doing ugly stuff to the Storyteller's Handbook. Here you go:</div> </div> </div> </div>-chuckle-<br /> While that would be handy, i can't seem to actually get it in an uncorrupted state - and with all the pop-ups on megafileupload i'm afraid i might catch something if i keep trying. Let me get my antivirus swinging 100% again in a few days and i may give it another shot, but if you can get it to CHILL for his proposed depository - then i'll definitely nab that like a thief in the night. Thanks from.<br /> Assuming this formatting isn't a problem for Mr. Watson. Please, stop us if you would prefer it remain solely on the wiki.<br /> <br /> Edit, 5 minutes later:<br /> No, I did get the .pdf to load up on one last attempt. So maybe i'm just using the wrong software to read the .odt file, I wouldn't put it past me.<br /> That will help, I mentioned i like to keep hard-copies of these creations to pass around when needed - although that generally doesn't apply to ST books.<br /> <br /> It does bring me back to the question in the original post, if anyone knows how some of the fan-supplements synthesized the visual styles of the series they emulated (borders, fonts, etc..)? Some were very nice and it could be something to teach myself in time, imitation as flattery and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Proved myself wrong shortly there-after. 03-07-2015, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T10:58:49-08:00","id":431502,"title":"","content":"OK, update on the EON archive. Got most of the downloads I'd retained in my archive ready to go. There seems to be some non-EON stuff in there as well that I'd saved as well........or was on EON and I've completely forgotten. There's a couple PDF's, including one I'd done a decent layout job on for Aberrant, that I can't actually even remember creating. Seriously, have no memory of it. Looks nice though O_o.<br /> <br /> I also have what looks like a fairly complete copy of EON v4 - that was the last 'black' version of the site and also the last one to be pure html. The one with the annoying flash logo / animation at the top, for those that remember (yay 90s web!). Should get that v4 ready to go in the next few days then I can open up the folder for those that want to grab copies.<br /> <br /> The V5 of EON - the white version from somewhere in mid 2002 on IIRC - is long gone from my archives. A fairly hosed version of it can be found on archive.org if you've got time to kill. A ton of stuff was in the forum though and that is what I think made it to RPGpost eventually.<br /> <br /> On the layout front Nihilist, a lot of the EON PDFs that had the visuals looks / borders etc similar to actual official books was probably done by me in InDesign and Photoshop. I spent weeks getting that stuff done and then used it everywhere (red versions, blue versions, yellow versions, green versions!). I remember re-using it so often because it took so damned long to create. Unfortunately, the original PSD and InDe files never made it to my archives. Just the PDF's remain.<br /> <br /> Will update again when the folder is ready.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T21:06:38-08:00","id":432217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=431502#post431502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will update again when the folder is ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking forward to it, it'll be interesting to see the treasures you've hoarded in your time with the Trinity online community. Pity you lost those borders, but i'm glad for everything you've managed to save.<br /> Thanks for your efforts here CHILL, sharing difficult to find information is a noble act at the least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T23:35:36-08:00","id":432340,"title":"","content":"OK. I'm finally posting something. I've been observing this forum ever since Onyx Path announced it got the rights to Trinity. I was an infrequent poster on the old EON sight right when CHILL left. There is one fan made document I know of that you did not list Nihilist. I'm pretty sure it was the first Trinity PDF that EON members produced; Trinity Field Report - Noetic Science. I thought it was awesome. I had very low expectations when I read about the work being done on it. At the time it seemed that it was just yesterday that White Wolf had announced they were no longer producing material for that line, and I was still suffering from at least one of the stages of grief. However, when I saw the finished product the first thing I thought was...Trinity Lives!<br /> <br /> Oh, and not to toot my own horn, but the Frantically French document you listed was mine and I posted it on EON.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T23:54:18-08:00","id":432364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=432340#post432340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. I'm finally posting something. I've been observing this forum ever since Onyx Path announced it got the rights to Trinity. I was an infrequent poster on the old EON sight right when CHILL left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the number of those of us who wait, KingOfDreams. -smile-<br /> Nice to have another fan author show up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=432340#post432340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one fan made document I know of that you did not list Nihilist. I'm pretty sure it was the first Trinity PDF that EON members produced; Trinity Field Report - Noetic Science. I thought it was awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gah!<br /> You're right, that was an incredible piece of writing that made the whole mess of inspiration into something i was proud to work into my (mostly) hard-science vision of the 2120s. Because of how well formatted it is and the importance i assign it's ideas, i never even considered it unofficial - which is about as much compliment as i can give. I'll add it to the list right away, thanks for pointing out that greivous oversight on my part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=432340#post432340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and not to toot my own horn, but the Frantically French document you listed was mine and I posted it on EON.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, i had hoped to lure a few a few stray authors out for comments. I am going to have to refresh my memory of what it was all about, but if i remember correctly it was an adventure based on Shattered Europe's Trauma Tours of France, yes? Posted on EON, is that where i found it? Anyway, keep an eye on this thread, I'm sure i'll have some questions about your writings once i've re-aquainted myself.<br /> <br /> That 'Trinity Lives' moment is one i've shared, in fact because i was late to the EON party, your writing actually gave that to me. Thanks for that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Oops.. 03-08-2015, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T00:18:11-08:00","id":432388,"title":"","content":"You are correct in your assumptions of the Frantically French adventure. I've edited it a lot since I posted it on EON. If there is a resurgence of fan material postings, I would be happy to re-contribute it. I just don't know if this is the place for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T00:35:22-08:00","id":432402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=432388#post432388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are correct in your assumptions of the Frantically French adventure. I've edited it a lot since I posted it on EON. If there is a resurgence of fan material postings, I would be happy to re-contribute it. I just don't know if this is the place for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wow. i look forward to seeing how it's evolved. I'll PM you a link to my email (if i can figure out how), CHILL's archive will be richer for it too. Beyond that - i have no real idea how to contribute to the RPGPost archives or anywhere else.<br /> New/Edited Trinity content to consume? You've just made my weekend.<br /> -standing ovation-<br /> <br /> The Next Day...<br /> <br /> Right, i now have a copy of the updated Frantically French. I will need to take a closer look to tell what (if anything) has changed, but it's a solid adventure into the ruins of France by proxy of the UK. I'm going to ply KingOfDreams with some questions about the adventure, but if it goes too long, i'll move the conversation into a different thread to keep the intentions of each clear...<br /> So, KingOfDreams:<br /> The title calls this &quot;1st Assignment&quot;, what happened to the 2nd? Did you have plans you could share? Colin seemed suspiciously poignant at the end there, for a character that had little actual role in the drama...<br /> The party composition seems to be locked in by the narrative, yet the story doesn't really take advantage of that expressly. Did you intend for each member to actually have been dunked by their respective orders? Was the grouping one of psionic or political consideration? Is there any reason why another group couldn't take part in the adventure? Would you say it could even be headed up by organizations other than Aeon, with a bit of re-tailoring?<br /> Why use Hector Ramirez? Was this eventually going to run into Darkness Revealed or in the midst of it (Passage Through Shadow may have room before the trial, maybe after with some adjustments...)?<br /> Did you refer to the UK Sourcebook &quot;In his Majesty's Service&quot; for your visit to London Arcology? (nice placement of the beanstalk, by the way...)<br /> Did you avoid geographic details for any reason? The Thames doesn't get mentioned at the point of departure, the arrival location is an unnamed beach, when Calais, Boulogne and Dunkirk could be used. Why do they need to do this quiet insertion as opposed to a more grand introduction to ruined France?<br /> Were you tempted to use French Flu at any point? Or any contemporary French locales as ruins?<br /> How long does it generally take you to run the scenario and how would you award experience for it?<br /> <br /> That should get me started... Thanks again for coming forward, KingOfDreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Rather than double post... 03-09-2015, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T07:08:17-07:00","id":433940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428704#post428704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was no rift in the dev team to the best of my knowledge. Baugh and Bates co-developed Adventure!, after all, and Bates and Blackwelder co-developed Mummy: The Resurrection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the idea of that comes from the differing depictions of dramatic editing within the game (as you and I have discussed); I <i>believe </i>that was popularly attributed to a development split. I'll admit, I've repeated that idea myself, without confirming it directly with either Baugh or Bates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:03:55-07:00","id":434113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=428475#post428475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something as opposed to nothing would be better for poor Adventure!, please let me know if it ever shows up. Thanks for mentioning it, i'd never heard of that one before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so I checked my assorted archives and old backups and what have you. Turns out I don't have a local copy of that anymore. So I did some digging, and was able to find the original source, on an old, more-or-less discarded site of Stew's. You'll find it at <a href=\"http://digital.raven.tripod.com/rp/mystics.html\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a> and the difficulty conversion chart it references can be found <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20030222204119/http://www.mindspring.com/~brucebaugh/trinity/charts.html\" target=\"_blank\">here, thanks to the Wayback Machine.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:48:23-07:00","id":434164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=432402#post432402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title calls this &quot;1st Assignment&quot;, what happened to the 2nd? Did you have plans you could share? Colin seemed suspiciously poignant at the end there, for a character that had little actual role in the drama...</div> </div> </div> </div>I did plan several other Assignments, but none of them got fleshed out anywhere nearly as much as Frantically French. I did plan on having Colin show up as a re-occurring NPC in some of the other Assignments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=432402#post432402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The party composition seems to be locked in by the narrative, yet the story doesn't really take advantage of that expressly. Did you intend for each member to actually have been dunked by their respective orders? Was the grouping one of psionic or political consideration? Is there any reason why another group couldn't take part in the adventure? Would you say it could even be headed up by organizations other than Aeon, with a bit of re-tailoring?</div> </div> </div> </div>The approach of the party composition was intended to be idealistic from a story perspective as well as from a game dynamic one. Trinity had a theme of unity, which I thought could be represented well by a group of psions, one from each of the Orders, working together to succeed in aiding humanity, hence the beginning narrative in the Assignment I wrote. The Assignment can be re-tooled to easily handle any mash up of psions or even normal humans for that matter. By the way, did Trinity have a term for normal humans like Aberrant did, I can't remember?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=432402#post432402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why use Hector Ramirez? Was this eventually going to run into Darkness Revealed or in the midst of it (Passage Through Shadow may have room before the trial, maybe after with some adjustments...)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did plan on running all of the printed material as well. I figured it would be best to introduce Hector right from the start to enrich the published material down the road.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=432402#post432402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you refer to the UK Sourcebook &quot;In his Majesty's Service&quot; for your visit to London Arcology? (nice placement of the beanstalk, by the way...)<br /> Did you avoid geographic details for any reason? The Thames doesn't get mentioned at the point of departure, the arrival location is an unnamed beach, when Calais, Boulogne and Dunkirk could be used. Why do they need to do this quiet insertion as opposed to a more grand introduction to ruined France?<br /> Were you tempted to use French Flu at any point? Or any contemporary French locales as ruins?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>In His Majesty's Service</i> was not written at the time I wrote and edited Frantically French, though I would have definitely tried to use material from it for my Assignment. I did try to incorporate as much of the published material as I could because I like practically all of it. Mining as much detail as possible really makes the game more of a reality for players. However, I think it is possible to include too much. Really, I just read the books, jotted down enough notes to get started and then began writing. If I didn't include something from the published material it was either because I didn't feel it was necessary, simply forgot about what I read, or I felt I already had enough material. Though I could easily see myself adjusting the Assignment with the ideas you mentioned. As for the quiet insertion, I think that fit the approach Aeon was trying to take in the Assignment. They wanted to try out something new with this team dynamic of a psion from each Order and publicize the heck out of it...if it worked. No need to make it a press release until they were confident it was a success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=432402#post432402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does it generally take you to run the scenario and how would you award experience for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I never did run Frantically French, nor have I run a Trinity game. I would hope the game would take two to three sessions, each four to five hours long, to complete. As for experience, I had planned a ton of house rules, especially when it came to character advancement. I had anticipated a run of three Assignments in Europe before reaching a milestone and moving on to a different setting. Perhaps that gives a better picture for how much experience to dole out.<br /> <br /> Again, thanks for the interest and I hope Frantically French lives on in other games!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":5273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","user":"KingOfDreams","date":". 03-09-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T22:01:41-07:00","id":435267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=433940#post433940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll admit, I've repeated that idea myself, without confirming it directly with either Baugh or Bates.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably how i picked up this meme, unconfirmed conversation pieces that never provided sources or evidence. But it made sense given the clear lack of integration of Trinity and Aberrant on release - just another example of false pattern recognition leading, i guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=434113#post434113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so I checked my assorted archives and old backups and what have you. Turns out I don't have a local copy of that anymore. So I did some digging, and was able to find the original source, on an old, more-or-less discarded site of Stew's. You'll find it at <a href=\"http://digital.raven.tripod.com/rp/mystics.html\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a> and the difficulty conversion chart it references can be found <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20030222204119/http://www.mindspring.com/~brucebaugh/trinity/charts.html\" target=\"_blank\">here, thanks to the Wayback Machine.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Finally, some fan-made material for Adventure!, it does require the Sorcery rules - so it isn't stand alone. But, it's definitely something as opposed to nothing. I have never really felt the need to cross over the WOD and TU, but if that's the prerogative of other games, i won't stand in their way. But something about Lovecraftian horror fits so well with the greater setting (in my opinion), so i'm not at all opposed to this particular one.<br /> A sincere thank you for the effort, Mythic Fox, had you not brought this to my attention it could have completely passed me by. I'm glad you maintained your memory of it well enough to guide new readers to the text itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=434164#post434164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did plan several other Assignments, but none of them got fleshed out anywhere nearly as much as Frantically French. I did plan on having Colin show up as a re-occurring NPC in some of the other Assignments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pity you never got there. Was there some kind of over-plot for the assignments that you had planned or were they going to be episodic and separate from each other? How would you suggest Colin be presented, as a villain, hero or something in-between? Would you suggest underplaying the encounter if there are no further appearances by the character? You have a talent for narrating the grey-scales of the WOD, but sometimes it helps for a ST to know these things... -taps head-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=434164#post434164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The approach of the party composition was intended to be idealistic from a story perspective as well as from a game dynamic one. Trinity had a theme of unity, which I thought could be represented well by a group of psions, one from each of the Orders, working together to succeed in aiding humanity, hence the beginning narrative in the Assignment I wrote. The Assignment can be re-tooled to easily handle any mash up of psions or even normal humans for that matter. By the way, did Trinity have a term for normal humans like Aberrant did, I can't remember?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we've all tried to wrangle that group out of our players at one stage or another - eventually i got it by allowing some players to play two PCs at once (small group, big party). As political representatives between and from their orders, such a party can be a convoluted mess of tensions and mistrust - which is exactly what the setting thrives on, if you ask me. But some players want something much more pulpy and less challenging.<br /> The glossary on p307 of the core book lists 'neutral' as a name used to describe non-psions, further stipulating the following uses; neut, normal, norm, blank and empty. But i've personally found it doesn't quite roll off the tongue like 'baseline' from Aberrant. -shrug-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=434164#post434164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did plan on running all of the printed material as well. I figured it would be best to introduce Hector right from the start to enrich the published material down the road.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, i always let Hector Ramirez step into screen during non-canon adventures too - like a dangling sky-ladder for the players to climb up into the meta-plot when they wish. It takes a few sessions before new players warm to the senior operative, but once they realize he is ultimately on their side they are generally pleased to see him show up uninvited. So, introducing him before Darkness Revealed appealed to me also.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=434164#post434164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>In His Majesty's Service</i> was not written at the time I wrote and edited Frantically French, though I would have definitely tried to use material from it for my Assignment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've managed not to stand on its toes at least, but it's been a while since i read all that through as well so i wouldn't want to assume.<br /> The customs hold-ups are great atmosphere builders at the start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=434164#post434164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did try to incorporate as much of the published material as I could because I like practically all of it. Mining as much detail as possible really makes the game more of a reality for players. However, I think it is possible to include too much. Really, I just read the books, jotted down enough notes to get started and then began writing. If I didn't include something from the published material it was either because I didn't feel it was necessary, simply forgot about what I read, or I felt I already had enough material. Though I could easily see myself adjusting the Assignment with the ideas you mentioned. As for the quiet insertion, I think that fit the approach Aeon was trying to take in the Assignment. They wanted to try out something new with this team dynamic of a psion from each Order and publicize the heck out of it...if it worked. No need to make it a press release until they were confident it was a success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your adherence to the setting is really strong, but the story doesn't suffer for your fidelity, so you found a decent balance there. The use of Mossalo and the heads of Proteus/Triton/Neptune was dry, but effective.<br /> I had assumed you were intending a low-profile for the mission, but with the media in tow - i just assumed that a more in-your-face transition into France could have made for a better book end after the London Arcology. Something as simple as road signs with ominous warnings, asking people to leave while they still can or similar, would be sufficient.<br /> -shrug-<br /> With the film crew there, a few memorable visual prompts might have sparked the PCs inner attention seeker and seen them having fun with the film crew aspect of the assignment. I have at least two player of mine in mind who would have jumped at the chance to preach at a camera, or show-off for it, given appropriate roles to do such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=434164#post434164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, I never did run Frantically French, nor have I run a Trinity game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry about that, you would have been good, simply judging from your knowledge of the setting. This story seems fun enough on paper to deserve a solid play-through to iron out the kinks. So, does anyone have a group spare? My players are currently 800km+ away...<br /> -hangs head-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=434164#post434164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would hope the game would take two to three sessions, each four to five hours long, to complete. As for experience, I had planned a ton of house rules, especially when it came to character advancement. I had anticipated a run of three Assignments in Europe before reaching a milestone and moving on to a different setting. Perhaps that gives a better picture for how much experience to dole out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think all Trinity STs eventually had at least some house-rules. -smile- Character advancement was fraught with perils if the separate systems got mixed together anyway - so you weren't alone in thinking advancement needed some in-house adjustments, if only for consistency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=434164#post434164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, thanks for the interest and I hope Frantically French lives on in other games!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank <i>you</i>, for coming forward. You spent the time to write this out and the care &amp; thought you put into it shows. I personally might have told most of this story with a flowchart, a fistful of visual aides and a few more random encounters to effect the atmosphere that you've created in your narrative. So my approach left me with little narrative to show for all the years of storytelling - played or not, Frantically French certainly preserves your ideas much better.<br /> I could see Frantically French show up alongside Hidden Agendas in a compilation of episodic adventures with a bit of work and play-testing, it's a good use of the material, i feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Incapable of posting anything without coming back and editing some minor detail... -shame- 03-10-2015, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:19:51-07:00","id":436546,"title":"","content":"OK, archive ready.<br /> <br /> Quick reminder: This includes a bunch of publications, tools, sheets and other downloads - I'm pretty sure most if not all of these were on EON, but in honesty a couple of non-EON ones may have got dropped in (my archives of EON are a mess).<br /> <br /> I've also managed to salvage a largely functioning copy of the EON site as it was when it was still 'EurOpNet' (specifically, version 4 of the site). This was the last version of EurOpNet that had a black background, was static HTML and called by the full name 'EurOpNet'. The version that came along after this (V5) was named 'EON'. V5 was the white website with the forum, launched some where in mid 2002, IIRC. I don't have a backup of V5 or any later version (see rpgpost.com for forum archives).<br /> <br /> In case there's any confusion - this stuff was all fan-made, and not in any way to be taken as canon - especially the very few files that looked half-decent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B6FYbpbzU8JCfjdWVmQyQjFyaml5VVBVc2lGWGVLZEQ1YzFTbkVtN0VfUHhSLW9idl9yV0U&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Click here for the EON archive</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:31:21-07:00","id":436553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=435267#post435267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pity you never got there. Was there some kind of over-plot for the assignments that you had planned or were they going to be episodic and separate from each other? How would you suggest Colin be presented, as a villain, hero or something in-between? Would you suggest underplaying the encounter if there are no further appearances by the character?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had about ten Assignment ideas all together. Colin was going to show up in a couple of them. One was going to include his father who was an FSA elected official in a high seat of power who was pushing anti-psion laws. Colin was kind of a wild card. His actions or position would somehow get the players into trouble, so he was kind of planned as an antagonist, but his intentions would always be harmless. Other than that, the Assignments were pretty separate from one another. Colin can be integrated or not, the Assignment's story doesn't need him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=435267#post435267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The glossary on p307 of the core book lists 'neutral' as a name used to describe non-psions, further stipulating the following uses; neut, normal, norm, blank and empty. But i've personally found it doesn't quite roll off the tongue like 'baseline' from Aberrant. -shrug-</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I remember. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=435267#post435267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had assumed you were intending a low-profile for the mission, but with the media in tow - i just assumed that a more in-your-face transition into France could have made for a better book end after the London Arcology. Something as simple as road signs with ominous warnings, asking people to leave while they still can or similar, would be sufficient.<br /> -shrug-<br /> With the film crew there, a few memorable visual prompts might have sparked the PCs inner attention seeker and seen them having fun with the film crew aspect of the assignment. I have at least two player of mine in mind who would have jumped at the chance to preach at a camera, or show-off for it, given appropriate roles to do such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was using the media NPCs as Associates of Aeon who had gained enough credibility for Aeon to trust them to submit all footage to their organization for final approval, and editing. Aeon would probably even have them sign legal binding contracts that stipulated as much. As for your suggestion to make France seem more foreboding, I like it. Maybe the Assignment could use some more writing to emphasize how much people <i>don't</i> want to visit that country anymore. As for camera hogging, Aeon operatives must adhere to strict professionalism at all times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=435267#post435267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see Frantically French show up alongside Hidden Agendas in a compilation of episodic adventures with a bit of work and play-testing, it's a good use of the material, i feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a huge compliment for me. I intended this Assignment to be a good introductory adventure. I tried to think of a scenario that would have all the right elements which would expose the players to the current atmosphere. Thanks!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:59:43-07:00","id":436590,"title":"","content":"CHILL is a godsend. When I get off work, I am raiding that archive you put up. I loved all of those books and I used most of them in my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T21:44:28-07:00","id":436681,"title":"","content":"Awesome CHILL! I actually grabbed a few tidbits that I didn't think to get years ago. Thanks so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T00:32:04-07:00","id":436804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=436546#post436546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, archive ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just fantastic, a number of things i've never seen before, a treasure of lost relics (BioGenesis and 3rdWorldWar, i forgot all about them!) and all free to whomever is interested. Let me add my gratitude to the pile CHILL, you have served these authors well by extending the lifetime of their work. I think i have to gave another...<br /> -standing ovation-<br /> <br /> I kind of want to see all of the RPGPost documents in there too now, but there is no need to step on their toes just for that convenience.<br /> How would you like to handle ongoing contributions that find their way to the community walls, are you happy to expand the archive for willing authors?<br /> Your efforts have given us all something to do this evening, at the very least.<br /> -rubs hands together-<br /> Thanks for this, you old-school boss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=436553#post436553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for camera hogging, Aeon operatives must adhere to strict professionalism at all times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, good luck with that. PCs are the very bastion of dignity and stoicism as any ST can attest. [/SARCASM] Oh, the stories i could tell...<br /> -smile-<br /> Thanks for the feedback, KingOfDreams and see if you can get Frantically French into CHILL's archive for posterity. Failing that, i can send in the copy you sent me - but that seems a bit third-wheel.<br /> There's some good swag here, now. I'm glad i shook that tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:55:33-07:00","id":437141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=436804#post436804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you like to handle ongoing contributions that find their way to the community walls, are you happy to expand the archive for willing authors?<br /> Your efforts have given us all something to do this evening, at the very least.<br /> -rubs hands together-<br /> Thanks for this, you old-school boss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure - why not, I could do that. I have a massive amount of GDrive space so yep. Kinda goes without saying but saying it anyway - I would only host fan stuff there, nothing official, nothing copyrighted etc.<br /> <br /> Best way to get anything to me is to ping me through the G+ community (see link in my sig). I've added a permanent link to that archive in that community too in case you need to retrieve the link (see panel on right when visiting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:02:02-07:00","id":437150,"title":"","content":"Also, just added the A-Z Players Guide original PDF as well as the India Underground PDF books to their respective folders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:36:18-07:00","id":437448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=437141#post437141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, sure - why not, I could do that. I have a massive amount of GDrive space so yep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good, i'm going to see what i have lying around later to see if i can come up with anything relevant and accessible enough. Although, i suspect there won't be much digitally available...<br /> <br /> Later...<br /> <br /> Okay, i've pieced together a few discoveries along with my own assorted, fever-dream dementations upon the subject matter. Including a couple of unexpected pieces from my very first Trinity game, which i've expanded on in another thread to CHILL (and anyone who read it). Showing that i was kind of headed for crossover hell even back then.<br /> I managed to find the Qin write-up i mentioned in the OP (yay, me) and a couple of other things that aren't my own creations. I'm pretty certain none of it was copyrighted or official since all of it has come from documents - but there was probably some copypasta in my recipe.<br /> Most of this crap is probably best kept secret - none of it's really in a finished state, honestly i wouldn't even be tempted to share these if not as some form of balancing out the joy other fan-authors have brought me over the years. -blush-<br /> <br /> -removed bleating-<br /> <br /> Finally figured it out, see CHILLs first post on page three for details.<br /> <br /> I've included Frantically French V2, i hope this isn't stepping on KingOfDreams toes. I'm just trying to load up the archive with more content and i don't mean to bypass your opportunity to do the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Less GDrive needed 03-12-2015, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T20:14:39-07:00","id":437953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=437448#post437448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've included Frantically French V2, i hope this isn't stepping on KingOfDreams toes. I'm just trying to load up the archive with more content and i don't mean to bypass your opportunity to do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind. Now that I think of it though, I did include a picture of a vehicle used in an old show called Damnation Alley, and I would think that is copyrighted material. It's a really old show from the 80s, so it may not matter, but I'm not up on my copyright law.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T05:56:41-07:00","id":438304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=437953#post437953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think of it though, I did include a picture of a vehicle used in an old show called Damnation Alley, and I would think that is copyrighted material. It's a really old show from the 80s, so it may not matter, but I'm not up on my copyright law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, i removed that image from the document included. But truthfully, i have no idea how visual reproductions fall under copyright law, the only safe bet is to make your own as far as i'm concerned...<br /> Onyx Path will need a lot of new art if they aren't the new owners of the reproduction rights - so hopefully that's at least is intuitive.<br /> <br /> Now, will somebody please releive my GDrive of anything worth saving - i'm not exactly comfortable with some of that crap being publically posted. I can see myself reducing or denying access pretty soon for one reason or another (any would do at this point).<br /> The sunlight.. It burns.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:40:14-07:00","id":438379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=437448#post437448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright... I think i have the items hosted on <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B43PeIDH5JjySE1NQWFQQ0oyNDQ&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">my own GDrive</a>. But i'd prefer it be moved elsewhere, something about google touching my private datas gives me the willies. Excuse any failed earlier attempts... I hope i didn't make a mess on your end CHILL.<br /> I've included Frantically French V2, i hope this isn't stepping on KingOfDreams toes. I'm just trying to load up the archive with more content and i don't mean to bypass your opportunity to do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Nihilist. I've grabbed these and am dropping them into the EON Archive folder I shared earlier (a subfolder titled 'Nihilist Contributions'). You can safely make that folder you created private / delete it now if you want.<br /> <br /> Quick reminder on getting things to me: Visit G+ and ping me a link to a shared folder (DropBox, GDrive, whatever) in a direct post - doesn't have to be a post in the community just add me to a circle then plus me in a post with the link. I'll do the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 03-12-2015, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T08:17:30-07:00","id":438425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=438379#post438379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks Nihilist. I've grabbed these and am dropping them into the EON Archive folder I shared earlier (a subfolder titled 'Nihilist Contributions'). You can safely make that folder you created private / delete it now if you want.<br /> <br /> Quick reminder on getting things to me: Visit G+ and ping me a link to a shared folder (DropBox, GDrive, whatever) in a direct post - doesn't have to be a post in the community just add me to a circle then plus me in a post with the link. I'll do the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>-fist pump-<br /> Great, it's unerring how much that was bothering me.<br /> -blush-<br /> <br /> I hope people find it useful or entertaining.<br /> Some explanations:<br /> - Qin bodyguards have too many lines - great look, but difficult to figure out.<br /> - The characters presented were run in a silver-age time-travelling story my brother ran out of a modified Aberrant setting - i've tried to keep them as compatible as possible, but a lot of my own (dirty) head-canon about the post Adventure! era has made its way into them for the 1950s character. I rather liked the Graceful Crane, would love to hear feedback there.<br /> - Chromatics are very earthlike in their skeletal and muscular anatomy, similar evolutionary solutions indeed.<br /> - Frantically French and Hidden Between Asteroids are 2120 adventures, i wrote neither of them.<br /> - I have no idea where the J. Snead Qin post came from, maybe i copied it off EON, but the original post? No idea. I'm simply glad i didn't lose it after all.<br /> - oh, god. The merits flaws and expanded backgrounds document is the very definition of poorly conceived, house-rule nonsense. The Merits and Flaws are collected from the books i had access to and have a handful of home-brewed additions also - but the rest was really just a thought experiment and never polluted the games i ran. I really only included it because it has a fair bit of (meaningless) content and food for thought.<br /> - Aww, my first handout for Trinity. I was still a teen when i pulled that out, kind of surprising how well it holds up after all the new information since. -nostalgia- I was already building to Tsuit Han getting free and the chase leading into a confrontation with Huang-Marr Biorgs at Boltzmann.<br /> - That's my avatar! Thief!<br /> - The developers chat is probably archived away somewhere, but i would have to look to be sure and i think i've proven i was far too lazy for that.<br /> - My rantings on Trinity era technology and commerce is something that i still find myself toying with every few years, if i ever have anything more to add i'll make sure the additions make their way to those archives. I would love for this document to be savagely critiqued, because my reason for writing it was getting a better sense of the mixed up technology flow in the three settings. Another thought experiment with little or no editing and far from complete.<br /> <br /> Love to hear what anyone thinks of the documents i had control over.<br /> CHILLs take on how much of the technology/commerce material he could use in the pure 2120 setting would be informative in particular, because much of it ties into the aberrant era sequentially - but i took great care to write it from a 2120 perspective.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the sweet hosting and posting, CHILL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Excuses and blame added. 03-12-2015, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:13:56-07:00","id":438698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=438425#post438425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CHILLs take on how much of the technology/commerce material he could use in the pure 2120 setting would be informative in particular</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, it really wouldn't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There's far more insightful folks than me out there, far....FAR more. My utterly useless feedback on pretty much everything unofficial is going to be of the 'huh' or 'cool' or 'yeah not my thing' variety - and that's probably about it, if I get time to look through it. Its not a lack of interest, just a time-constraint issue. Any other takers on the technology and commerce stuff?<br /> <br /> Admission time - I very rarely actually read anything we produced / stored on EON in any real depth - and if it was longer than 2 pages I just quickly skimmed it, posted it and moved on. I just made sure others could get the stuff and discuss it when I eventually relented and setup a chat then a forum, and that no rules / copyrights were being broken in fan publications etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=438425#post438425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for all the sweet hosting and posting, CHILL.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem - hope people find it all useful. Plenty more space where that came from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T19:28:40-07:00","id":439239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=438425#post438425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- My rantings on Trinity era technology and commerce is something that i still find myself toying with every few years, if i ever have anything more to add i'll make sure the additions make their way to those archives. I would love for this document to be savagely critiqued, because my reason for writing it was getting a better sense of the mixed up technology flow in the three settings. Another thought experiment with little or no editing and far from complete.</div> </div> </div> </div>While perusing the documents, the <i>Technology &amp; Commerce</i> one intrigued me the most. It's a long one and I just skimmed some of it. What I did read I liked. I thought it had some updated and insightful commentary on the subject that the original Trinity missed out on simply because of when it was written and released. I would definitely use some of your writing as a primer for new players to the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T20:42:14-07:00","id":439312,"title":"","content":"RE: Memory Lane<br /> <br /> This takes me back! I am glad that there are still people making use of some of this material ( I wrote the Nova Tech book and contributed to Forceful Personalities and The New Flesh..probably some other stuff have forgotten about).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T21:09:06-07:00","id":439346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=438698#post438698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh, it really wouldn't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There's far more insightful folks than me out there, far....FAR more. My utterly useless feedback on pretty much everything unofficial is going to be of the 'huh' or 'cool' or 'yeah not my thing' variety - and that's probably about it, if I get time to look through it. Its not a lack of interest, just a time-constraint issue. Any other takers on the technology and commerce stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Insight comes in different forms. You've run years long campaigns in the setting by your own admission, i can't help but try and tease some of that experience out.<br /> -shrug-<br /> No worries. The pure original Aeon setting is something i hold in esteem and you're kind of the only representative of it that i've personally encountered who wasn't corrupted by the need to make it fit in with anything else. I may end up calling you to account on some of it one day, because i am sincerely curious how some elements of the story (quantakinesis, order purges, Doyen, Nippon, the Chromatic 'deceivers', Coalition Furies, etc...) figure into the setting as you see it. You've mentioned not accepting official sources too (eden &amp; maybe process 418 as printed), so knowing where you drew the line might make things a bit clearer.<br /> -points and nods forebodingly at CHILL-<br /> <br /> So how did you 'CHILL-rate' it? [ ] huh [ ] cool [ ] yeah not my thing<br /> -tease-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=438698#post438698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admission time - I very rarely actually read anything we produced / stored on EON in any real depth - and if it was longer than 2 pages I just quickly skimmed it, posted it and moved on. I just made sure others could get the stuff and discuss it when I eventually relented and setup a chat then a forum, and that no rules / copyrights were being broken in fan publications etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>-chuckles-<br /> I suppose that precludes finding your credits on anything after the A-Z Player's Guide... Wait, you're credited in India Underground as having contributed writing as well as a number of other services... Surely you must've read anything crediting you on so many fronts! Don't take it the wrong way, but i am going to laugh <i>so</i> hard if you didn't. -anticipation-<br /> I couldn't even fit a<i> character </i>onto less than two pages, i produce <i>handouts</i> longer than that, some of my <i>posts</i> here are longer than that.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingOfDreams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439239#post439239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While perusing the documents, the <i>Technology &amp; Commerce</i> one intrigued me the most. It's a long one and I just skimmed some of it. What I did read I liked. I thought it had some updated and insightful commentary on the subject that the original Trinity missed out on simply because of when it was written and released. I would definitely use some of your writing as a primer for new players to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>[ ] huh [x] cool [ ] yeah not my thing<br /> -smile-<br /> Well, if you would use it then i suppose i'm on the right track. Any critique would be welcome from a fellow writer - you have my contact details if you ever have any. I'm assuming you're talking about the computer stuff, because that's the first bit that isn't just empty headings. I'm glad it wasn't too raw to make some sense out of, some of that stuff was added recently and i haven't had enough time away to come back and edit it yet.<br /> Thanks for commenting, KingOfDreams.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439312#post439312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: Memory Lane<br /> <br /> This takes me back! I am glad that there are still people making use of some of this material ( I wrote the Nova Tech book and contributed to Forceful Personalities and The New Flesh..probably some other stuff have forgotten about).</div> </div> </div> </div>Another fan author?<br /> -Rubs hands together in glee-<br /> <br /> [ ] huh [x] cool [ ] yeah not my thing<br /> <br /> Check back tomorrow, i'll refresh my memory of NovaTech and have some comments/questions then if you can spare the time. As i've said to the other contributors, sincere thanks for adding to my collection and keeping this fantasic setting alive over the years. Any clarifications on what you did on FP and TNF would allow me to make comment there too.<br /> Respect.<br /> P.S. Did you know CHILL never read more than two pages of it while he was doing the layouts and graphics?<br /> -smile-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  [x] huh [ ] cool [ ] yeah not my thing 03-13-2015, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:09:46-07:00","id":439925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439346#post439346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may end up calling you to account on some of it one day, because i am sincerely curious how some elements of the story (quantakinesis, order purges, Doyen, Nippon, the Chromatic 'deceivers', Coalition Furies, etc...) figure into the setting as you see it. You've mentioned not accepting official sources too (eden &amp; maybe process 418 as printed), so knowing where you drew the line might make things a bit clearer.<br /> -points and nods forebodingly at CHILL-</div> </div> </div> </div>I laugh at your foreboding nod, pfah!<br /> <br /> Ahem.<ul><li>QuantaK. Relegated to history. All chibs dead or otherwise out of play. Gone. Boom. Stabby-stabby &amp; turned into sticky-paste. Not a PC option</li> <li>Order purges. There was really only 1 purge, see above - although the Docs were coming close and I had plans to split that order up following the DR series. Never actually got around to it though</li> <li>Doyen. Yep, used them as per the DR series of books. Made no real modifications to them and didn't use them again outside running those scenarios</li> <li>Nippon. Never used it. *shrug*. Didn't come up in game either. Skim-read the fluff once, but never had to come back to it.</li> <li>Chromatics. See Doyen answer above</li> <li>Coalition. As per the Alien: Deception book, not used them since then</li> <li>418. Didn't advance the timeline to it. If I had needed to, I'd have to come up with something else. Not sure what that would be, but it absolutely would not be introducing non-prometheus chamber psions / powers</li> <li>Eden. Blew up. All dead. Especially that annoying Nova that vanished the Chromatics at Karoo. Put the vanishing Chromatics down to some space-mad Abbie whose reasons remain a mystery *spooky music*</li> <li>While I'm at it - Teleporters. They did return, but I had them do so in minimal numbers and as NPC's, none of which I used in games outside of the DR series. Am apprehensive about the Porter's being returned and ready to play in the TC reboot. Prefer these to be back-story and not playable</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439346#post439346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how did you 'CHILL-rate' it? [ ] huh [ ] cool [ ] yeah not my thing<br /> -tease-</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the one with many pages yeah? Um. Not sure. Didn't actually get a chance to skim through it yet. Is on my list though. Can we add a: 'Plan to read [ ]' on this CHILL-scale thingy? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439346#post439346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-chuckles-<br /> I suppose that precludes finding your credits on anything after the A-Z Player's Guide... Wait, you're credited in India Underground as having contributed writing as well as a number of other services... Surely you must've read anything crediting you on so many fronts! Don't take it the wrong way, but i am going to laugh <i>so</i> hard if you didn't. -anticipation-<br /> I couldn't even fit a<i> character </i>onto less than two pages, i produce <i>handouts</i> longer than that, some of my <i>posts</i> here are longer than that.<br /> -smile-</div> </div> </div> </div>Err.... um......well. <br /> <br /> *sigh*<br /> <br /> Yeah I got nothing. Laugh away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For InUn I think I did some minimal pickup writing - really minimal, hence the writing credit. Mainly though I co-ordinated folks (which was a massive job, granted) and did layout, then others picked it up, polished it etc. I've never actually sat down and read it completely. I really should do that.<br /> <br /> -Plan to read [x]-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439346#post439346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S. Did you know CHILL never read more than two pages of it while he was doing the layouts and graphics?<br /> -smile-</div> </div> </div> </div>CHILL can't event remember doing the layout for it. At all. That's the file I mentioned earlier that I found in my archives and sat there for a good few minutes pulling a Gandalf (&quot;I have no memory of this......&quot;). Looks great thought huh?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T23:35:24-07:00","id":440974,"title":"","content":"[!--- NOVA-TECH ---!]<br /> Well, the layouts are great. -smile- Love to know how you did that title, CHILL. If you can remember that much...<br /> <br /> This document is mostly rules, so i'm probably going to miss something on my first run at it. It's been a number of years since i used these rules myself and i'm not really fresh on Adventure super science either. -blush-<br /> So first up, Reighnhell, how did <i>you</i> use these rules? You specify the intent is for Mecha-style results, which i think has a place in the setting (all three eras) - but the player i had who used these rules created a WH40k 'killa-can' kind of armor that was still mostly small enough to move around indoors (although there was some laser cutting involved at times). So, was i misusing your concept? No big deal, just wondering. How much modification (in your mind) would these rules require for an 'Iron Man' suit as you stipulate?<br /> Could you expand a bit on your thinking with Quantum Batteries, the differences between them and actual Dixon Batteries and the specifics of recharging? I ran these rules in a 2120 tainted-nova campaign and there just wasn't enough justifiable Taint/Quantum energy available for environmental charging outside of Tainted areas, does this sound right in your view?<br /> Were you at all looking at 2120 VARGs when you did this, if so, how did that influence you? After being innovated by the inventing Nova, were these creations fully pilotable by base-lines?<br /> The power armor advancements for flight &amp; energy weapon recharge are missing their R&amp;D times, care to issue some 'official' errata? Why no cost or R&amp;D for the weapons listed? Are the advancement options for each size of design arbitrary or did you test to arrive at them. if so can you expand on how you tested?<br /> On page eight, you have a heading for Adding Nova Innovations. You write;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;If the suit it is being built into has Atomic Power, then the Innovation automatically receives Quantum 1, Quantum pool 10. Every 2 dots of Quantum uses 1 option (rounded up).Every 20 points of Quantum pool uses 1 option. The points provided by Atomic power are not counted for the previous figures.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Can you please add some detail to this? We need the Atomic Power option, but then we can add more Quantum and Quantum pool with spare options on the armour or on the seperate innovation? And these additional points don't stack with the Atomic Power advancement? What about the Q-Pool stacking with the Battery? I may be a little dumb, but i'm just not getting it here.<br /> I liked the construction flaws, selecting them is a bit wierd, but the mechanic is good.<br /> Thanks again for the contribution, armor-wearing super-heroes is an element of the genre that the Aberrant game never really embraced, but i always felt there was room.<br /> P.S. If you are interested, the player character that used these rules in my game was a fellow who fully called himself 'The president of the suit club' and was an entertaining hot-mess of a tainted mega-intelligent on Mars, where i had an enclave of tainted-novas. The name came from his suit not being entirely unique amongst them (since environment suits are so ubiquitous on Mars) and his need to stand out and feel important. He was an ambitious Thug at times, but was very protective of his little enclave.<br /> <br /> <br /> I moved some of the response to CHILL into a new thread, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/441130-pure-2120-trinity-the-chill-way\">Pure 2120 Trinity: the CHILL way</a>, i don't want his perspective lost in the purpose of this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439925#post439925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the one with many pages yeah? Um. Not sure. Didn't actually get a chance to skim through it yet. Is on my list though. Can we add a: 'Plan to read [ ]' on this CHILL-scale thingy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your scale, which i found amusing enough to repeat three times.<br /> -shakes head-<br /> I have a wierd sense of humor...<br /> I'm not forcing you, i'll live without your feedback - but like i said, your perspective is kind of unique to me.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439925#post439925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err.... um......well.<br /> <br /> *sigh*<br /> <br /> Yeah I got nothing. Laugh away<br /> <br /> For InUn I think I did some minimal pickup writing - really minimal, hence the writing credit. Mainly though I co-ordinated folks (which was a massive job, granted) and did layout, then others picked it up, polished it etc. I've never actually sat down and read it completely. I really should do that.<br /> <br /> -Plan to read [x]-</div> </div> </div> </div>-deep belly laughter-<br /> This is so awesome, i am going to get days (at least) of internal amusement out of this.<br /> It clearly wasn't apathy, the layouts would have been a massive job, so you cared. Just not enough to pay any attention to the material!<br /> In the intervening years you never even decided to check it out belatedly!<br /> -wipes laughter tears from eyes-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=439925#post439925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CHILL can't event remember doing the layout for it. At all. That's the file I mentioned earlier that I found in my archives and sat there for a good few minutes pulling a Gandalf (&quot;I have no memory of this......&quot;). Looks great thought huh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, now to be entirely clear, you did a fantastic job on the layouts - all respect due, which just makes it even funnier. I'm hoping that i'm laughing with you here CHILL, because i appreciate the hell out of what you've done over the years. I've just added the bonus detail of finding any credits to you on these books (except AZPG) a joke that will keep on giving. Thank you for your efforts and the wonderful punchline.<br /> -laughs all the way out of the thread-<br /> Spectacular!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  I wonder how many of my posts i haven't edited later. -muses- 03-14-2015, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T07:54:41-07:00","id":441301,"title":"","content":"I think I can explain CHILL's memory gaps concerning InUn and layouts. <br /> <br /> He had originally planned to do the full layouts, but the team kind of dissolved on the home stretch. He had already produced all of the base page frames that were used in the book. I had done some writing and my room mate at the time was the artist on the book. Between the two of us we had copies of about all the files that were supposed to be in the book (though now that I think about it I can't remember why). Anyway, at this point CHILL had handed the reins of EON over to someone else and it appeared the book was dead. So I got a program and spent 24 hours putting all the pieces together. I'd always intended to go back and fix it (removing the duplicated text, fixing the font problems etc.) But at this point I don't think I still have all the constituent files (most, but not all).<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's my big contribution to the history of Trinity.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T11:08:15-07:00","id":441628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=441301#post441301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I can explain CHILL's memory gaps concerning InUn and layouts.<br /> <br /> He had originally planned to do the full layouts, but the team kind of dissolved on the home stretch. He had already produced all of the base page frames that were used in the book. I had done some writing and my room mate at the time was the artist on the book. Between the two of us we had copies of about all the files that were supposed to be in the book (though now that I think about it I can't remember why). Anyway, at this point CHILL had handed the reins of EON over to someone else and it appeared the book was dead. So I got a program and spent 24 hours putting all the pieces together. I'd always intended to go back and fix it (removing the duplicated text, fixing the font problems etc.) But at this point I don't think I still have all the constituent files (most, but not all).<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's my big contribution to the history of Trinity.<br /> <br /> -Slag</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, another fan-author. Any chance of getting you to check back in a day or two to sate an end users curiousity?<br /> India Underground was a pretty interesting bit of lore and an impressive contribution to the history of Trinity that i've made some use of through the years - but i like to refresh before i leap in and make a fool of myself. I'd ask CHILL, but...<br /> -uncontrolled fit of laughter-<br /> <br /> -regains composure-<br /> If you can let me know what you worked on, i can make my questions topical, should you have the time. But in either case, thanks truly for the work you put into this and for not &quot;being the ass that deleted the entire book&quot;. -smile-<br /> Out of interest, you don't happen to still have the page borders do you?<br /> So, thanks for posting and getting the thing out there for us, Slagheap. Your efforts are well appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T15:52:06-07:00","id":441903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=441301#post441301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I can explain CHILL's memory gaps concerning InUn and layouts.<br /> He had originally planned to do the full layouts, but the team kind of dissolved on the home stretch. He had already produced all of the base page frames that were used in the book. I had done some writing and my room mate at the time was the artist on the book. Between the two of us we had copies of about all the files that were supposed to be in the book (though now that I think about it I can't remember why). Anyway, at this point CHILL had handed the reins of EON over to someone else and it appeared the book was dead. So I got a program and spent 24 hours putting all the pieces together. I'd always intended to go back and fix it (removing the duplicated text, fixing the font problems etc.) But at this point I don't think I still have all the constituent files (most, but not all).<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's my big contribution to the history of Trinity.<br /> <br /> -Slag</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep - that sounds right - there you go folks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:08:58-07:00","id":441918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=440974#post440974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[!--- NOVA-TECH ---!]<br /> <br /> -deep belly laughter-<br /> This is so awesome, i am going to get days (at least) of internal amusement out of this.<br /> It clearly wasn't apathy, the layouts would have been a massive job, so you cared. Just not enough to pay any attention to the material!<br /> In the intervening years you never even decided to check it out belatedly!<br /> -wipes laughter tears from eyes-</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=440974#post440974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[!--- NOVA-TECH ---!]<br /> Alright, now to be entirely clear, you did a fantastic job on the layouts - all respect due, which just makes it even funnier. I'm hoping that i'm laughing with you here CHILL, because i appreciate the hell out of what you've done over the years. I've just added the bonus detail of finding any credits to you on these books (except AZPG) a joke that will keep on giving. Thank you for your efforts and the wonderful punchline.<br /> -laughs all the way out of the thread-<br /> Spectacular!</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that is hilarious now I think about it. I'm not sure why I've never seen it from that perspective before. hah! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You're right, it absolutely wasn't an issue with not caring - heck no. Definitely the files took forever to put together for things like InUn (not to mention trying to get the material collated and so on from fans all doing this when they could). The key motivator for me with EON which had been running for 6 years before I called it quits, was to facilitate a resource fans could enjoy. <br /> <br /> That meant my time spent evolved to running a basic archive, to chat service, a forum, to a larger archive of material, even a publication or two, or just dumping some of my own notes online. We had a lot of stuff on EON at one point, and it took a good hour or two a day, every day, just to keep things ticking over. Think about things like server problems, forum moderation, site file management and all that comes with it - never mind actually trying to spend time reading everything. The community (which really sprung up around the forum) functioned really well - with some nudging from the small handful of mods here and there, and periodically from me. The EON community were a great bunch really, very rarely did we have (at least to my memory) any real issues like you get in some other places. Says a lot about the fan base, and explains why all the fan supplements started to appear.<br /> <br /> Now, to add to your giggles - can you imagine me getting tons of Aberrant RPG material from very enthusiastic folks to post on the site, with me not actually reading it (not my kinda game and had little time). Always asked 'so whatcha think?'. I must have dodged that question a hundred times. But still, I made darned sure it all got posted and promoted as much as I could. Happened every day. I was a facilitator, basically. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:25:51-07:00","id":441947,"title":"","content":"RE: Nova Tech<br /> <br /> Been absolutely forever since I took a pass at those rules. I will go over it and see if I can conjure some revisions and clarifications.<br /> <br /> RE:Other Work<br /> <br /> I had a few enhancements in Forceful Personalities<br /> The majority of my contributions are in &quot;The New Flesh&quot; - Mostly in Drugs, and the &quot; Blood and Thunder&quot; Section.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T01:27:15-07:00","id":442326,"title":"","content":"A fourth page on my first thread:<br /> [ ] huh [ ] cool [ ] yeah not my thing [x] plan to read<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=441918#post441918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that is hilarious now I think about it. I'm not sure why I've never seen it from that perspective before. hah! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You're right, it absolutely wasn't an issue with not caring - heck no. Definitely the files took forever to put together for things like InUn (not to mention trying to get the material collated and so on from fans all doing this when they could). The key motivator for me with EON which had been running for 6 years before I called it quits, was to facilitate a resource fans could enjoy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right?<br /> I'm kind of ashamed i never spent any real time on EurOpNet before the forum had been up for a a while, even then i spent years lurking before contributing myself. It certainly makes me read the EON html you shared with a newfound sense of respect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=441918#post441918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That meant my time spent evolved to running a basic archive, to chat service, a forum, to a larger archive of material, even a publication or two, or just dumping some of my own notes online. We had a lot of stuff on EON at one point, and it took a good hour or two a day, every day, just to keep things ticking over. Think about things like server problems, forum moderation, site file management and all that comes with it - never mind actually trying to spend time reading everything. The community (which really sprung up around the forum) functioned really well - with some nudging from the small handful of mods here and there, and periodically from me. The EON community were a great bunch really, very rarely did we have (at least to my memory) any real issues like you get in some other places. Says a lot about the fan base, and explains why all the fan supplements started to appear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my brother has been an unpaid webmaster for a number of years out of sheer passion for the subject matter too, so i can kind of understand the level of effort you put in there. Regardless of how much of it you read, EON grew into possibly the best resource for Trinity for a while - even surpassing the White-Wolf site at the end there. So your work formed a really solid base for the community long after official support seemed to evaporate.<br /> All this makes me even more interested in how you might react to some of the ideas i put into that Tech document - the Opnet history crap in particular. But again, there's no pressure or expectations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=441918#post441918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, to add to your giggles - can you imagine me getting tons of Aberrant RPG material from very enthusiastic folks to post on the site, with me not actually reading it (not my kinda game and had little time). Always asked 'so whatcha think?'. I must have dodged that question a hundred times. But still, I made darned sure it all got posted and promoted as much as I could. Happened every day. I was a facilitator, basically. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This occured to me, but for you to verify that suspicion is very rich indeed, creators run on feedback - this is the gift that keeps giving. You must be one slippery customer to get serious feedback out of, <i>especially</i> for aberrant/adventure material. Just thinking about it has stapled a grin on my face.<br /> In riposte, i refer you to the first two paragraphs of your 'Words from the Producer' on p11 of InUn, when you finally get around to reading it.<br /> -supressed laughter finally escapes-<br /> You're...<br /> <br /> [ ] huh [x] cool [ ] yeah not my thing [ ] plan to read<br /> <br /> ...in my book, CHILL. When i went looking for missing resources, i never expected to find such a wonderful, 'TL-DR' meme behind them. Bravo, sir!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=441947#post441947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: Nova Tech<br /> <br /> Been absolutely forever since I took a pass at those rules. I will go over it and see if I can conjure some revisions and clarifications.<br /> <br /> RE:Other Work<br /> <br /> I had a few enhancements in Forceful Personalities<br /> The majority of my contributions are in &quot;The New Flesh&quot; - Mostly in Drugs, and the &quot; Blood and Thunder&quot; Section.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you, it's been a while, thanks for your time in any case Reighnhell.<br /> I will definitely have questions about TNFs Drugs section, as a primarily 2120 setting ST i was a bit personally affronted by such a detailed list of hi-tech performance drugs in a supplement from the aberrant/nova era. Some of TNF is entirely new to me, so i'll have to pull a leaf from CHILL's book and... [x] plan to read.<br /> Looking forward to your insights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Don't you dare auto-emoticon me, forum! 03-15-2015, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T07:30:03-07:00","id":442492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=442326#post442326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> i refer you to the first two paragraphs of your 'Words from the Producer' on p11 of InUn, when you finally get around to reading it.<br /> -supressed laughter finally escapes-</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah. Yeah - I meant every word of it though. I think a great job was done on that book. There was a ton of back and forth work behind the scenes on InUn, file crashes, delays, a handful of personality clashes to manage and everything that comes from producing fan-supplements with a dozen or so people involved, not to mention yours truly bowing out of EON and others taking the reins. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I still need to get around to actually ready every bit of it. Its on the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T10:27:23-07:00","id":449453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=442492#post442492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah. Yeah - I meant every word of it though. I think a great job was done on that book. There was a ton of back and forth work behind the scenes on InUn, file crashes, delays, a handful of personality clashes to manage and everything that comes from producing fan-supplements with a dozen or so people involved, not to mention yours truly bowing out of EON and others taking the reins.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I still need to get around to actually ready every bit of it. Its on the list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't doubt for a second that you were proud of the book and the work done on it, the backstory of production itself seems like it could've filled another dozen pages or so. I sense no actual arrogance on your part and your honest support and efforts decrease the inherent humor by exactly 0%.<br /> -smile-<br /> Like i've said, i enjoyed it and i've used it. You were one of those who made it possible, do not mistake my laughter as any form of derision towards you. In some ways i hope you never actually read it, just for the potential epitaph/obituary:<br /> &quot;Here lies CHILL, he truly did plan to read.&quot;<br /> -tease-<br /> Rather, take my playful teasing as a heightened enjoyment of the product, that i consider to be worthy of the setting i hold in such high regard. Hopefully once Reighnhell responds below, i can get a interview with Slagheap over his contributions on the project.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=441947#post441947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: Nova Tech<br /> <br /> Been absolutely forever since I took a pass at those rules. I will go over it and see if I can conjure some revisions and clarifications.<br /> <br /> RE:Other Work<br /> <br /> I had a few enhancements in Forceful Personalities<br /> The majority of my contributions are in &quot;The New Flesh&quot; - Mostly in Drugs, and the &quot; Blood and Thunder&quot; Section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so without knowing your specific enhancements on Forceful Personalities, i'm going to have to leave that be or make comment on every enhancement that book has to offer.<br /> <br /> <u>The New Flesh Drugs</u><br /> First off, i'm sorry i remarked upon these being presented for Aberrant instead of Trinity, they actually fit the era they are meant to be in just fine. I think my issues arose from other biotech detailed in that chapter. I've written this as if you designed all of these drugs, feel free to comment on those you didn't, but also let me know either way.<br /> Endless Bountiful Harvest is a lovely dark touch, do you have any idea on what might have ultimately happened to this poor nova in your own head-canon?<br /> Also, i'd like to hear your solution for the drug cocktail i proposed in the 'Character - Lloyd Spite c2004' document in CHILL's archive, posted in the 'Nihilist Contributions' folder, just because you've had to put some thought into this stuff. At your leisure, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Amor</b>: Nice one, all the earmarks of a drug that would see use despite the ethical and moral problems. I see this as being able to be used in the 2120s also, perhaps with less addictive qualities due to the Sudamerican pharmaceutical industry of that era. I can use this, so i like it.<br /> <br /> <b>Anti-Aging Cocktail</b>: While this seems pretty intuitive as a product to be desired, the side effect of sociopathy and OD result of brain failure are not as intuitive. Is this result a simulation of neural pathways being reset, leaving the brain un-imprinted on fellow humans? Would this begin with other personality changes before the full sociopathy emerged, do you suppose? Definitely a Drug i would expect to show up during the era, nice to see it here.<br /> <br /> <b>Baraka</b>: Intuitive, horrifying and nicely ruled to boot. How do you see the practitioners of this morbidity hiding themselves? Baselines don't have much recourse to avoid the pursuit of righteously indignant novas. But otherwise i like that this was added, even just for the morose story-telling potential (the hints of the effects being mostly psychosomatic are quite delectable).<br /> <br /> <b>Crimson</b>: An interesting twist on Red-7, i'm assuming it's a later development along the same line of Red-7. What was the thinking behind no OD effects here? What do you imagine would happen on 3-10 doses more than recommended? Stacking would make it overpowered, obviously, but surely something occurs beyond the first dose, right? I like the progression from Red-7, this works i think.<br /> <br /> <b>1st Gen Anti-Taint</b>: Does the user actually gain a point of Mega-Intelligence through this drug's usage or just the Taint Resistance enhancement? Gaining the mega-attribute seems a little extreme, care to comment? Why no taint-resistance for those with higher that one Mega Intelligence? Otherwise i love the development process described and it's an interesting idea - how many generations of these drugs do you suppose might have emerged before the era came to an end? Why weren't they more influential in preventing what became the Aberrant War and leading to the Chinese Ultimatuum of 2061? Very interesting proposition.<br /> <br /> <b>Green Honey</b>: I don't like introducing rule-enforced rape into a RPG, in a way this is much worse that the infamous first contact with the Coalition in Aeon/Trinity - because while the Breeders are definitely drawing from tentacle-rape tropes, their motivations are alien and possibly more easily correlated to a kind of genetic hunger. Novas at least have their three free points of resistance to fall back on, but failing that Willpower at +3 difficulty is a steep incline to surmount just to avoid being taken down a path that many players could find unacceptable. Starting PCs in both Aberrant and Adventure! start with three willpower, making resisting this drug next to impossible without committing freebie/bonus points at creation. How would you justify this?<br /> Anyone who hasn't erupted is very likely to see their characters raped after simply coming into contact with the user's bodily fluids (as little as momentary flesh to flesh contact or simple proximity as forensic science shows). This is fine as a dark-side plot device taking place 'off screen', but why have it be so difficult to avoid when the consequences could leave participating players feeling violated?<br /> <br /> <b>Hyperzine X</b>: Mite for the brain - intuitive enough. I might have leaned towards Schizotypal behaviour rather than Bi-Polar, what was the reasoning here? Otherwise this is a natural fit.<br /> <br /> <b>Joy Buzz</b>: Sounds like a highly addictive MDMA, while i understand this is a tie in to the rise of the Nova underworld, i have a hard time seeing Utopia being so bull-headed when research indicates a small number of people are going to go looking for this kind of outlet despite all and any educational and legal barriers. The sub-effect of it sometimes working on low-constitution Novas seems like the only really new thing here. What am i missing?<br /> <br /> <b>Longpig</b>: -chuckle-Ok, here you have Kuru and Kreutzfield-Jakob Syndrome alongside OK Maerth's psuedo-scientific aphrodesiac effect - which honestly might fit in a tongue-in-cheek Adventure! story, but i have no idea why it appears in a fictionally modern scientific 'drug' section. Now, i might have gone out of my way to slip 'Longpig' in there just for a giggle myself, but how does this really belong in this list? What does this add to the setting?<br /> <br /> <b>Mnemosyne</b>: This fills an ecological niche opened by Lethe, it's good material and i would definitely use it. But the scientific aspect is kind of glossed over in the drive to fill the hole, i'm guessing because you were building intrigue over the creator, but some indicator of <i>how </i>this works is its only downfall. Otherwise, it's a good one.<br /> <br /> <b>Nemukame</b>: This is a good idea, but total immunity is a bit strong in my opinion, why so extreme on this and Green Honey above? I like it and would see it as something i'd like to use, but i'd like to hear why it was so strong too. Why wasn't permanency at least threatened in the OD and effect entries?<br /> <br /> <b>Noctisol-3</b>: As someone who has stayed awake for close to 120 hours before and commonly stays awake for 60+, this drug personally seems a bit underpowered and easily simulated with actual current drugs. Admittedly, present drugs aren't a guaranteed three days, but can be ramped up to that level - i seem to remember stories of combat vets going those lengths without chemical assistance also. The coma OD seems a little counter-intuitive also, where does that come from. the idea that the user has already been awake for three days prior to the second dose?<br /> <br /> <b>Suisho</b>: Fair enough, i can see a demand for that. But why no hard rules for the intended use? The only rules presented are for trying to provide therapy for those who were forced to take the drug prior to being psychologically (and perhaps otherwise) tortured? I can't see how those rules would come up as often, since the drug isn't directly made by crime syndicates, although admittedly Kuro-Tek is into some shady shit. Good idea, but the execution left something to desire in the form of hard and fast rules for its primary usage.<br /> <br /> <b>Super-Mite</b>: Like Crimson, this seems a logical extension of Mite. I can see how to use it and i like the short-cut logic to avoid simply raising the mega-strength cap. Intuitive and sequential stuff, i like it.<br /> <br /> <b>Tainted Soma</b>: Good concept, nice and intuitive. But baselines surviving on a botch and dying on a failure seems counter intuitive, why do it this way when most PCs playing Aberrant are likely going to be novas? Plus, wouldn't the brain pour out through the nose?<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> The Blood and Thunder section goes from page 81 to page 155, which is a bit much for me to cast as wide a net over - did you write all of this or just parts? Because i'm going to need a while to comment of seventy pages of mostly combat rules...<br /> -raises eyebrows-<br /> <br /> Thanks again, all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Endless Bountiful Post editing 03-19-2015, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T08:04:02-07:00","id":450438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=449453#post449453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do not mistake my laughter as any form of derision towards you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh heck no, I never would. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T07:04:05-07:00","id":451487,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: The New Flesh Drugs</b><br /> <br /> The New Flesh was a fan project that had many hands on it. The base mechanics for Drugs was something I developed mainly to make the drug rules cross-compatible between settings.<br /> <br /> I will focus on the Drugs that I had put together<br /> <br /> <b>Baraka</b><br /> Baraka was originally a plot idea I never got to use. The Baraka cult was actually going to be led by a mega-charismatic nova who felt that communion with the flesh and blood of Nova's could elevate all of humanity. The cult focused their predation on Nova's with fewer abilities to protect themselves from harm. I imagine the Teragen would have something to say about this.<br /> <br /> <b>Crimson</b><br /> Mechanically speaking, the drawbacks of Crimson were already pretty steep. Multiple doses at once would just increase the cumulative sudden death risk ( if I had to do over again, I would clarify that the death risk cumulative over a lifetime - if a user was at 15% and took a dose 2 years later, the risk would go to 18% as if they had never stopped)<br /> <br /> <b>Hyperzine X</b><br /> Looking back, I would agree with you.I went with Polar Disorder because it seemed like losing your advanced intelligence would cause a deep depression, but I can see more Schizophrenic behavior would be just as likely.<br /> <br /> <b>Noctisol-3</b><br /> Three days seemed like a good rule of thumb for wakefulness with relatively minor side effects from a single dose of the drug. If I were to re-do the rules, I would give a solid 5 or 7 days per dose.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Other Work</b><br /> <br /> Here are the things I worked on in TNF by section<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 1</b> - Drugs, Novel Sapients and Artificial Novas (Spark Soldiers, Spark Juice)<br /> <b>Chapter 2 -</b> New Maneuvers, Combat Styles, Combat Merits &amp; Flaws, Expanded Weapons Listings, Nova Techniques, and various abilities in Combat Enhancements and Combat Body Modifications<br /> <b>Chapter 3</b> - Sources of Injury<br /> <b>Chapter 4 - </b>Mega-Physicals and Other Mega- Attributes (various enhancements), Adaptive Variations (various modifications, powers and addenda)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T09:14:28-07:00","id":451601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: The New Flesh Drugs</b><br /> The New Flesh was a fan project that had many hands on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's a little less focused that the previous mega-attribute books, i suppose a lot of folks wanted to have their ideas heard. Was it an interesting development process, could you give us some background if you have any?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The base mechanics for Drugs was something I developed mainly to make the drug rules cross-compatible between settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i sort of had to eat my words when i realized how compatible most of it was... Nice to see the Trinity details for drugs from TerraVerde compliemented and expanded to fit bits from Aberrant, the only thing missing is an entry for Adventure! style super-science options. -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Baraka</b><br /> Baraka was originally a plot idea I never got to use. The Baraka cult was actually going to be led by a mega-charismatic nova who felt that communion with the flesh and blood of Nova's could elevate all of humanity. The cult focused their predation on Nova's with fewer abilities to protect themselves from harm. I imagine the Teragen would have something to say about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is 'plot hook' written all over that object, sometimes that's what tech really is in RPGs. Where does the name come from? For some reason i can see the church of Michael eventually devolving to this with 'communiom wafers'. I imagine the Teragen would say very little, while independants and righteous pundits alike would rage against it like cannibalism, then when the public spotlight had diminished the Teragen would wordlessly delever a verdict and punishment to those resposible. Possibly with spectacular consequences. But Geryon would sure as hell be pissed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Crimson</b><br /> Mechanically speaking, the drawbacks of Crimson were already pretty steep. Multiple doses at once would just increase the cumulative sudden death risk ( if I had to do over again, I would clarify that the death risk cumulative over a lifetime - if a user was at 15% and took a dose 2 years later, the risk would go to 18% as if they had never stopped)</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, valid point. When that clarification is applied, OD becomes more or less irrelevant. I was just hoping for some kind of horrific aberrant transformation or something, i guess. -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hyperzine X</b><br /> Looking back, I would agree with you.I went with Polar Disorder because it seemed like losing your advanced intelligence would cause a deep depression, but I can see more Schizophrenic behavior would be just as likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bipolar also works - fits of activity with crashes as you realize your work has lost a certain edge, i guess a few different psychological responses could occur. Alzheimers might be an example of extreme mental degeneration also, but there are a lot more out there too. In any case, it fills the space opened up for Physical by Mite with a Mental variation - nice. One could see a 'crimson' level variant developing in time...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Noctisol-3</b><br /> Three days seemed like a good rule of thumb for wakefulness with relatively minor side effects from a single dose of the drug. If I were to re-do the rules, I would give a solid 5 or 7 days per dose.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly a high value research target for military agencies, so it has a good niche to fill. I might have done it a little differently, but the idea is similar (i would have lead into psychosis rather than coma). Cool for the setting, could see it being used to show how desperate a pursuer is getting. Or send a number of other signals, when properly placed in game.<br /> <br /> Three of those drugs fill intuitive niches in the drug lanscape past 2008, which is useful setting upgrade stuff, letting the PCs know that time is more than just an arbitrary raising of their age. The other is essentially a plot device on a serving cart, with a couple of fun rules attached. So i approve of the contributions here, good stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Other Work</b><br /> <br /> Here are the things I worked on in TNF by section<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 1</b> - Drugs, Novel Sapients and Artificial Novas (Spark Soldiers, Spark Juice)<br /> <b>Chapter 2 -</b> New Maneuvers, Combat Styles, Combat Merits &amp; Flaws, Expanded Weapons Listings, Nova Techniques, and various abilities in Combat Enhancements and Combat Body Modifications<br /> <b>Chapter 3</b> - Sources of Injury<br /> <b>Chapter 4 - </b>Mega-Physicals and Other Mega- Attributes (various enhancements), Adaptive Variations (various modifications, powers and addenda)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still going to need time to see what i really need to comment on here, i'll let you know when i have more through PM. Plus Slagheap has gotten back to me too, so i have his material from InUn to catch up on too. Please excuse me while i take them up for a good read.<br /> Thanks heaps for answering so far, Reighnhell - hope i'm not wasting too much of your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  What is this, the spanish inquisition? 03-21-2015, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T15:01:31-07:00","id":452038,"title":"","content":"Anyone have a custom ST screen for Aberrant? I bought the one off of DriveThru but its a bad scan. Pieces cut out where the panels folded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5371-sahugani","name":"Sahugani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T23:53:41-07:00","id":452327,"title":"","content":"Sounds like an issue for DriveThruRPG, maybe send them a request for assistance on the matter, they get back pretty quick for most problems.<br /> -shrug-<br /> Sorry you didn't get what you were after, Sahugani. Of course, .pdf screens aren't really what they are meant to be on principle either. Let us know if you get any joy from DriveThru on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T01:47:37-07:00","id":462027,"title":"","content":"I've always been fond of <b>1,001 Aberrant Nights</b> (<a href=\"http://www.dark-kingdom.org/Aberrant/abtoc.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.dark-kingdom.org/Aberrant/abtoc.html</a>) by Kimberly Giannola. Originally conceived as a collection of thirty six in-character essays, roughly half of the fourteen (published) entries are written as articles for a(n in-game) news website by the nova Sherazahde, an independent nova with some friends in the Teragen. The others are written from other character perspectives, dealing with issues from relations between the XWF and the Teragen, to what its like to erupt with an incredibly potent (and dangerous) power<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><i>Taken from <b>eXistenZialist</b>, Volume I Issue I.</i></u> I hadn\u2019t thought about <b><i>Ashnod</i></b> until I saw the XWF Broadcast. I\u2019m certain my jaw was open during the whole speech. I mean, I\u2019d seen tapes of her before, OpNet videos of her many speeches and appearances. But they were viewed in the knowledge that this was in the past. It\u2019s different, a lot different, to watch events as they are occurring live.<br /> <br /> Live life as a Nova, she told me all those weeks before. Discover what it means to be part of the One Race. Was I doing that? I did not know then and I am not certain I know now, either. I watched the XWF Pay-Per-View because I thought it would educational. A little bit of culture, maybe. It was, after all, the highest-grossing sports industry in history. I don\u2019t know what I expected. Something like professional wrestling, I guess. Something more orchestrated. Fake, even.<br /> <br /> Gods, it was barbaric. Brutal and disgusting. There wasn\u2019t anything fake about it. These people were honestly trying to wound each other. I remember flinching several times throughout it, wincing as one combatant was injured or another knocked unconscious. Strange, to think that I, with all the violence I have seen and all the fights I have been in, would be squeamish at such a display. Nonetheless, I was revolted and appalled at it. These were my people, right? This is what we were doing for money?<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t believe anyone would do this. Since my eruption, I\u2019ve had to pay for very little. I go to get ice cream, and a simple smile gets me it free. I don\u2019t even try to do this, I just smile as I\u2019m getting it, and the clerk tells me there\u2019s no charge. I mean, expensive stuff, my house, the furniture, I still have to pay for all that. But not as much as most people. Or the salary they offered me. Oh my word, I almost fell out of my seat. That much money to be a part time columnist? Several times what I would have expected or even asked for.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, but they wanted to know my \u201cNova\u201d name. After all, it would be a Nova column, written by a recent eruptee, they wanted a public image their readers would instantly recognize. I\u2019ve tried to avoid using a Nova name after the way Ashnod told me it would be some kind of liberation, or baptism, for me to do so. I mean honestly\u2026Ashnod\u2026Narcosis\u2026Splash\u2026Lotus Infinite\u2026these are hardly names that grown women use. I told them I\u2019d get back to them.<br /> <br /> Travel expenses. Paid trips to Ibiza to get into the Amp Room and give the skinny on that. Get interviewed by Project Utopia as an applicant and tell what I could of that experience. Everything. Amazing how you can convince others to pay you for things you wanted to do already. And with so little effort! If I could do this, why were all these others sacrificing their bodies to the XWF like that? I wonder just how much they were getting paid to do it. It had to be a literal fortune.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019m trying to say is this: even though I\u2019m not getting paid anywhere near what those Novas employed by DeVries, Utopia, or the XWF get paid, my financial well-being is certainly better than the average baseline. Enough to live comfortably and not have to worry about late bills or emergencies in the future. And if I can manage that for my writing alone, you have to ask if it is worth it to put your life on the line in the \u201csquared circle\u201d for the chance to be decadently wealthy. I suppose the legions of loyal marks are part of it. Merchandising too; I can\u2019t imagine what it is like to have several action figures modeled after you. I\u2019d imagine it gets addictive after a while, and you become as dependant upon the attention your are getting as your fans are upon getting to observe your every move.<br /> <br /> I watch the early matches. The ones with the new names trying to establish themselves. If anything, they are even more brutal than the well-known faces, having to prove themselves. They do all the truly dangerous moves, the deadlier maneuvers, trying to become recognized and beloved by the fans. Then comes the main event, this \u201cLast Nova Standing Battle Royale.\u201d They are all there: Crater, the Shadow Serpent, the Untouchable, Mutilator, and several others who I can tell by the crowd reaction are big names though I\u2019ve never heard of them.<br /> <br /> Then they vanish, and a few minutes later, Ashnod is on the screen addressing the crowd. The media is calling that speech <i>Ashnod\u2019s Declaration</i> now. Not quite the <i>Null Manifesto</i>, but still memorable enough to those that follow the growing transhumanist movement.<br /> <br /> I remember experiencing that, not just viewing it. Experiencing it. The butterflies gathering in my stomach, the constant shifting of my posture and position as the cameras zoomed in and out on this woman I considered a friend. And for the first time, the conversation we had months before made sense to me. <i>Ashnod</i> made sense to me. Clarity had been bestowed, and while I still don\u2019t agree with everything Ashnod has said, I suddenly glimpsed the ever-widening gulf between what it means to be a Nova and what it was to be a baseline. And it was far vaster than I ever let myself believe until then.<br /> <br /> I was baptized.<br /> <br /> Now I needed a name to signify this.<br /> <br /> Regardless of what you might believe, coming up with a name is not something a Nova takes lightly. Or at least, not something this Nova did. How exactly does one come up with a simple one or two word label that will stick with you from that point on?<br /> <br /> You can go the route of many Novas, and use a name that describes your powers in some fashion or other. Splash, Skew, Fire Fox, and Firefly are all examples of this. But I did not want to use that methodology. My abilities are subtle enough that I wished to keep them as unknown as possible, and I did not want my name giving hints to any potential threats. You have got others whose names mean absolutely nothing except in some personal sense. Geryon, Totentanz, the Ragnarockette\u2026you get the idea. Or the Novas who simply use their known names: Sophia Rousseau, Raoul Orzaiz, Ana Gracia Texeira. Then you have the fanboys (and fangirls) whose names might have well been taken from the world of comic books. But I didn\u2019t care for that at all.<br /> <br /> So the second option seemed best, something personal that didn\u2019t really apply to my powers, but might apply to my outlook or my behavior. Or it might not. That is the beauty of such a name.<br /> <br /> Of course, then comes the rather difficult task of choosing one if you don\u2019t have one in mind.<br /> <br /> Finally, after dwelling on it for some time, it finally arrived. Of course, it waited until I had stopped concerning myself with it, and merely came to me upon a whisper or a memory. Which was, of course, as it should.<br /> <br /> Sherazahde. A teller of tales.<br /> <br /> I know I\u2019m supposed to register this name so that no one can claim right to it, but screw that. This isn\u2019t a copyright, and I\u2019m not a piece of merchandise. It\u2019s who I am now and anyone wants to dispute me for it, you are more than welcome to.<br /> <br /> Just don\u2019t expect to see me in any gaudy costume anytime soon. </div> </div> </div>She's also got a couple of unpublished articles in the series that just never got posted. If you get in touch with her, and ask nicely, she might sent them to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T02:48:40-07:00","id":462043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=462027#post462027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always been fond of <b>1,001 Aberrant Nights</b> (<a href=\"http://www.dark-kingdom.org/Aberrant/abtoc.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.dark-kingdom.org/Aberrant/abtoc.html</a>) by Kimberly Giannola. Originally conceived as a collection of thirty six in-character essays, roughly half of the fourteen (published) entries are written as articles for a(n in-game) news website by the nova Sherazahde, an independent nova with some friends in the Teragen. The others are written from other character perspectives, dealing with issues from relations between the XWF and the Teragen, to what its like to erupt with an incredibly potent (and dangerous) power<br /> <br /> She's also got a couple of unpublished articles in the series that just never got posted. If you get in touch with her, and ask nicely, she might sent them to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> Also something i've never seen before. I'll add it to the OP and have a look in - but i'm still trying to get time to read InUn again and go through The New Flesh more critically. So you may have to forgive my not having anything to say about this discovery, yet.<br /> Thanks for bringing it to my attention One Vorlon, I'll see if i can get in touch for the unpublished stuff too. Since the new edition may be ambiguously coming soon, i think all this stuff should be given a little attention - the fans have dedicated some valuable thought to the setting over the years.<br /> Looking forward to scrolling through it - and i'm still coming back with more for Reighnhell and Slagheap, if anyone is wondering if i've fallen off the face of the earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T00:30:08-07:00","id":464388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=462027#post462027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always been fond of <b>1,001 Aberrant Nights</b> (<a href=\"http://www.dark-kingdom.org/Aberrant/abtoc.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.dark-kingdom.org/Aberrant/abtoc.html</a>) by Kimberly Giannola. Originally conceived as a collection of thirty six in-character essays, roughly half of the fourteen (published) entries are written as articles for a(n in-game) news website by the nova Sherazahde, an independent nova with some friends in the Teragen. The others are written from other character perspectives, dealing with issues from relations between the XWF and the Teragen, to what its like to erupt with an incredibly potent (and dangerous) power<br /> <br /> She's also got a couple of unpublished articles in the series that just never got posted. If you get in touch with her, and ask nicely, she might sent them to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, I'm actually really touched that someone liked my little contribution to the Aberrant universe. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Note to self: I should really re-format the 1,001 Aberrant Nights site. It's appallingly bad to look at. I'm impressed that anyone managed to persevere through the terrible backgrounds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","name":"Ashnod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T03:37:18-07:00","id":464493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=464388#post464388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, I'm actually really touched that someone liked my little contribution to the Aberrant universe. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Note to self: I should really re-format the 1,001 Aberrant Nights site. It's appallingly bad to look at. I'm impressed that anyone managed to persevere through the terrible backgrounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great to have you with us Ashnod, One Vorlon delivered your works to me at least, so i'll second that thanks.<br /> <br /> Glad to hear you see the format needs some adjustment<br /> -tease-<br /> when did you first post that site out of curiousity? Just for a sense of the history behind your writing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T09:10:26-07:00","id":464734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=464493#post464493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when did you first post that site out of curiousity? Just for a sense of the history behind your writing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sheeshz...around 2002, I think? At least the initial entries.<br /> <br /> Many of these characters are either of my own creation: <i>Sherazahde, Ashnod, Salamander, Fracture, Machina;</i> analogues of the characters of other players in tabletop games I participated in:<i> Lucious Clay, Malu Hekili, Aurifex, Apep; </i>or analogues of characters that I interacted with at the old N!Prime site: <i>Prodigy, Wizard, Troll.</i><br /> <br /> It started largely as way for me to pen out some of the thoughts I had on the setting as described in the core books or to provide alternative takes on some of the ideas. As both a player and a storyteller, Aberrant is interesting to me not as a game about superpowered people, but as a means of telling stories about what having that manner of power does to both the mind of an individual and the behavior of society at large.<br /> <br /> For example, the story of Malu Hekili suddenly finding herself with a cult she neither asked for nor wanted, but at the same time, felt compelled to honor their affection in some way was me wanting to tell a variation of an India Syndrome story in a first world nation. I wanted to remove the stigma that this was something that happened only in isolated parts of the world. At the same time, it also gave me the opportunity to talk about how novas were not unlike the pantheons of bygone civilizations, and that those stories may have actually been based upon something tangible.<br /> <br /> Sherazahde's and Fracture's eruption stories were told together in an attempt to show the confusion and uncertainty that might arise in the initial moments between being normal and having destructive potential. In Sherazahde's case, the circumstances became largely comical in hindsight although they were not at the time. In Fracture's case, there is nothing comical about it; it was an event that ended up defining the young woman who endured it as well as the three Utopian novas asked to intervene in it. Most of the in-setting writing regarding eruption is told from the point of view of the aftermath but not in the moment, and I wanted to portray something more intimate.<br /> <br /> I know I originally said I was planning on thirty six or so essays, but a few things happened that waylaid my plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","name":"Ashnod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T06:45:57-07:00","id":466017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=464734#post464734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sheeshz...around 2002, I think? At least the initial entries.<br /> <br /> Many of these characters are either of my own creation: <i>Sherazahde, Ashnod, Salamander, Fracture, Machina;</i> analogues of the characters of other players in tabletop games I participated in:<i> Lucious Clay, Malu Hekili, Aurifex, Apep; </i>or analogues of characters that I interacted with at the old N!Prime site: <i>Prodigy, Wizard, Troll.</i><br /> <br /> It started largely as way for me to pen out some of the thoughts I had on the setting as described in the core books or to provide alternative takes on some of the ideas. As both a player and a storyteller, Aberrant is interesting to me not as a game about superpowered people, but as a means of telling stories about what having that manner of power does to both the mind of an individual and the behavior of society at large.<br /> <br /> For example, the story of Malu Hekili suddenly finding herself with a cult she neither asked for nor wanted, but at the same time, felt compelled to honor their affection in some way was me wanting to tell a variation of an India Syndrome story in a first world nation. I wanted to remove the stigma that this was something that happened only in isolated parts of the world. At the same time, it also gave me the opportunity to talk about how novas were not unlike the pantheons of bygone civilizations, and that those stories may have actually been based upon something tangible.<br /> <br /> Sherazahde's and Fracture's eruption stories were told together in an attempt to show the confusion and uncertainty that might arise in the initial moments between being normal and having destructive potential. In Sherazahde's case, the circumstances became largely comical in hindsight although they were not at the time. In Fracture's case, there is nothing comical about it; it was an event that ended up defining the young woman who endured it as well as the three Utopian novas asked to intervene in it. Most of the in-setting writing regarding eruption is told from the point of view of the aftermath but not in the moment, and I wanted to portray something more intimate.<br /> <br /> I know I originally said I was planning on thirty six or so essays, but a few things happened that waylaid my plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is solid introduction, i'm more excited to get to your writing now, Ashnod. It helps that you have a charming, reductionist approach to the camper elements of the setting (capes, spandex and cults of personality), lending an air of deconstruction to the result. At least in the sample submitted by One Vorlon above from Sherazahde's perspective. Thanks for posting this introductory teaser to properly hook me - i kind of need two different heads for reading setting material (or non-fiction) and fiction, these details helped to fire up my fiction-head. Good stuff.<br /> ...<br /> Apologies to all for my brief hiatus, by early next week i should be free to properly respond to Reignhell, Slagheap and Ashnod in the manner i would like. Thanks for your patience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T01:09:47-07:00","id":467116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=466017#post466017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is solid introduction, i'm more excited to get to your writing now, Ashnod. It helps that you have a charming, reductionist approach to the camper elements of the setting (capes, spandex and cults of personality), lending an air of deconstruction to the result. At least in the sample submitted by One Vorlon above from Sherazahde's perspective. Thanks for posting this introductory teaser to properly hook me - i kind of need two different heads for reading setting material (or non-fiction) and fiction, these details helped to fire up my fiction-head. Good stuff.<br /> ...<br /> Apologies to all for my brief hiatus, by early next week i should be free to properly respond to Reignhell, Slagheap and Ashnod in the manner i would like. Thanks for your patience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a problem. It's going to take me a few days to do anything with the material for you, though. I have a deadline at work coming up very soon, plus having a week of business travel coming up right after. Now that I know there is still interest in, I'll find motivation, but real life unfortunately has a bit of creep right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","name":"Ashnod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:17:32-07:00","id":472789,"title":"","content":"All apologies for my absence. Thanks for your patience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Other Work</b><br /> <br /> Here are the things I worked on in TNF by section<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 1</b> - Drugs, Novel Sapients and Artificial Novas (Spark Soldiers, Spark Juice)</div> </div> </div> </div>Spark Soldiers/Juice is excellent work. As soon as i started reading i thought; of course. It's intuitive, emotive, eminently plot-worthy and well ruled as far as i can tell with a brief lookup. The flavour text deploys sensible and official sounding jargon and it all fits on just more than two pages. You and anyone else who worked on it deserve to be congratulated, adds depth to the 2008 setting with a few subtle rule adjustments, easily reduced to a paragraph sized summary for quick reference.<br /> I'd love to hear how it was playtested/balanced, if you can remember.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Chapter 2 -</b> New Maneuvers, Combat Styles, Combat Merits &amp; Flaws, Expanded Weapons Listings, Nova Techniques, and various abilities in Combat Enhancements and Combat Body Modifications</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks like there is no way for me to divide your work from the rest of this chapter, so i'm just going to have to take it on headlong and generalize a whole lot.<br /> Nova combat can be a fun prospect, even unadorned, so a decent release of combat rules was lacking for the setting. It may be a little low-brow, but who cares if you're having fun with it. My only objection is that more options just makes for more time consumed per combat turn which in my experience; can already be a long process.<br /> Combat Styles would have been a hit with some of my group i think, they already seized upon the Trinity PG martial arts styles and it could have been a pleasant break from seeing all XP going directly to powers, mega attributes and enhancements for the combat specialized. The mechanics are creative and lend themselves to being used in any of three settings, so that is promising. Hopefully, when i play with the appropriate players again, i'll be able to make some use of these rules. Any suggestion of how you created the styles could be helpful as guidelines. How these were play-tested would also be very interesting with an anecdote or two.<br /> You guys really approached this from every angle you could think of, i approve highly. More merits and flaws are always welcome in my view. Whoever came up with the 'World Warrior' merit name needs to take a bow before my insistent applause. -smile-<br /> Are you privy to why the Max Str limits weren't worked around in the weapons section? It seems that masterwork weapons provide the means, but i'm not finding the mechanism there. Maybe there is something in the tech section concerning material science...<br /> Nova techniques are very interesting, designing them to work for other inspired is good etiquette and makes them available to a wider selection of PCs across the settings. How the combat techniques balance out across the settings is something i'd be interested in hearing your commentary on. Along with any play-testing details/anecdotes (again), if you can be bothered.<br /> I'm still overwhelmed by all of these powers and enhancements - i tend to see character generation for Aberrant as a kind of shopping spree - unless i have the need to really look and have an idea of what i'm looking for then they all blend together in a colourful but nonsensical display of plenty. So, i'll just leave that uncommented upon here, apologies.<br /> All in all, the Blood and Thunder chapter is as rich a source of combat rules as is available in any of the other setting books from any era. It contains mostly rules that are entirely compatible with all three settings with fun mechanics to distract combat-oriented play from the inevitable arms-war of higher Quantum levels. It's imaginative, well realized (at least the parts i read in depth) and makes me want to run a Nova combat encounter again.<br /> I would have concerns with balance if the play-testing wasn't done, perhaps you could allay those with any details of the balancing process adhered to. You have mentioned many hands working on it, i doubt they all took the same approach, but perhaps by explaining your own and describing any group guidelines - my apprehension will be negated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Chapter 3</b> - Sources of Injury</div> </div> </div> </div>This section is comprehensive and pretty well balanced, i have had to make game calls where guidelines like this would have been enormously helpful. Although much of it will be used rarely, the resource is invaluable and i can't think of a better collection - the only things missing are the rules covered in the core-book combat sections.<br /> Good stuff, i appreciate the work you put in here - some good mechanics too from what i'm seeing, although i won't be going point for point. I'd be interested in your Orbital fall mechanic being expanded to use on other planetary objects (for different atmospheric densities and gravity mainly), as the only orbital falls i ever ran were on Luna &amp; Mars in the 2120s...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=451487#post451487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Chapter 4 - </b>Mega-Physicals and Other Mega- Attributes (various enhancements), Adaptive Variations (various modifications, powers and addenda)</div> </div> </div> </div>Refer to my reasons above for why i'm not going through the enhancements and powers, drowning in sparkly options here. -smile-<br /> <br /> I didn't get a good first impression of The New Flesh in its complete form, but it's grown on me from unexpected directions. The more time i spend picking through it, the more cool stuff i find therein - had a release of this calibre been for the 2120s it would quickly find itself amongst my favourite fan-books and definitely brings the creativity of 'Brainwaves' to bear on the mega-physical dynamic.<br /> But it may take me years to entirely know the powers and enhancements contained in here, which is a pity, because some of the parts i've properly read have had some excellent systems, clever ideas and great reference materials. It's definitely one of the most comprehensive fan-books for the TU, if not the most. It isn't as focussed as the two prior mega-books, but it's also close to five times the size of <i>Brainwaves</i> and double that of <i>Forceful Personalities</i>. The only negative to this fan-book is if you are looking mostly for setting information, it's still in there - don't mistake me, only as prelude to usable rules in almost all cases.<br /> Thank you for your efforts in the production of this book Reighnhell, the sheer scope of which is still too great for me to fully grasp weeks after first viewing its contents.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Now, to Slagheap in regards to India Underground.<br /> What I'm quoting here is from Slagheap on my 'Message Center' page, apologies to Slagheap if greater privacy was intended:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Geoff &quot;Breearg&quot; Bain wrote most of the book, in fact the book was his idea. At some point toward the end he just disappeared, and I'm not sure where he got off to.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's mysterious.<br /> The development of this book sounds like a kind of accidental success, maybe you and CHILL could put all these developmental anecdotes into order and give us an idea of the whole process. When was the final .pdf first uploaded, can you place it into context with what other fan-projects had already been released? How long did it take to all come together? What was the reception for the creation like at the time of its release? What do you think might have happened to Mr. Bain? If we can't have him speak for himself, what kind of approach did he take to the setting and meta plot in general?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Most of my contributions are in the front of the book. I wrote all of chapter one except the order organization (and I named Project Harmony).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Did someone else come up with the concept of Project Harmony and not give the idea a name, Mr. Bain perhaps? I couldn't say the first Chapter is bad, but it doesn't make much sense without the details presented in Chapter four and elsewhere, which might contribute to the length of time i've taken to comment on your input. Of course, i personally have no idea of how to create the atmousphere i find lacking - maybe more scary emails, some history of the Order and its 'first' family or greater academic details on the early development of Noetic science. I understand this was done under time and motivational constraints and yet it outlines the Order well enough that i've used it specifically as preparatory material for one PC who lived through the events and had worked with Chibs.<br /> I'm not sure if this is the equivalent of the full-colour setting information sections of the original books - but i tried to read it as such. My favourite part has to be the scant operational details on the purge itself (p19) - it makes me hungry for more. I was sad to see the reference in the ST section (chapter four) didn't make it in - can you give me some idea of what that missing reference might have discussed? Earlier in the chapter you call it &quot;one of the largest massacres of the 22nd century&quot;, but lacking that missing reference i personally dismissed this as Doyen propaganda to elicit fear of surviving QKs - assuming the eventual ambush to have been quite surgical and deliberate in New Delhi. Care to affirm or set me straight?<br /> I'm not sure where else to put this; but in the Jnyadeep section, the 'rehabilitated' aberrants from the core book's entry on the Chitra Bhanu (core book, p63) get mentioned briefly. This was one of the things i seized on for a tainted 2120 aberrant campaign, so i'd love to hear you comment on the idea of 'rehabilitated' war-era aberrants coming and going from the Bombay clinic.<br /> If/When you are fishing about your head for me, see if you can conjure up a depiction of these aberrant capture operations for me - as it came up recently in a thread about quantum power suppression by order Psions. You may not have wrote about it directly yourself in the bits you've pointed out, but you may be my best bet for more detail there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>In chapter 2 I wrote the &quot;flavor&quot; text for all the standard modes, and I also designed the standard Enhancement mode.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Lazy bloody co-writers. -smile-<br /> While this is mostly reiteration, your style of writing works well for the flavour text. You place the mode power in context and add a subtle air of shared experience somehow, without dragging on. Nice work there.<br /> Enhancement has a good feel to it, i believe something in CHILL's 'What we know' document mentions the OPP team bringing a similar kind of capability to the Aesculapians. Did you also do the alternate modes for Enhancement starting on p27? I assume you weren't trying to compensate for the power levels seen in the Aberrant setting, or if you were you were being very light handed and/or subtle about it. Can you comment on how you designed Enhancement in particular, how you balanced the rules, whether you made concessions to the other game lines and if you have made any house-rule adjustments in the interim for fine tuning?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i> I also helped Jake write the dysfuction section.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Quantakinetic Dysfunction: Even the concept must have given many Doyen whatever Doyen have instead of nightmares. The unexpected result of QK, noetically abused by their three-dimensional recipients - that research into 'curing' taint must have been promising indeed for the Doyen to have taken the risk.<br /> Apart from pointing out the obvious there, i have little more to add. The Dysfunction section is useful and even more discouraging than some of the core dysfunctions - which can fail to ward off mode extremism as much as intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I also handled all the sidebars (I think there might be two in chapters 1 and 2).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So, all of the sidebars in the book or just those in the first two chapters?<br /> First two are plot hooks, nice, i only wish there was more like them to spin into an expanded player's section.<br /> The third is a few retrospective opinions on the Purge, care to comment on how you assigned these opinions to their respective sources?<br /> Next sidebar on p22 is the obligatory 'taint is not quantum' disclaimer found in a few books and even more fan-made materials (i still have an old handout outlining this noetic principle lying around).<br /> Very next page has sidebar number five on the similarities between the 'Bestowed Enhancement' and 'Catabolysis' powers - i guess the Doyen chamber division of aptitudes could have been mentioned here - but it wouldn't have added much.<br /> Sidebar six on page 27 feeds into my need for Aeon/Trinity to be a <b>Sci</b>-Fi setting, none of my players who know more about science than i qualify as abusive - a couple of minutes with a reference is generally all it takes to settle it properly when problems arise. Science is mostly pretty good like that.<br /> Sidebar seven on p33 gives some ball-breaking variants on dysfunction rules that would have appealed to me when i had two legionnaires happily maintaining different dysfunctions for munchkin-ward purposes. -sigh-<br /> The sidebars dispersed throughout chapter three are good setting pieces and make chapter one seem somewhat naked in comparison. Even chapter four could have used more of these - if this was your doing, what was your design behind this bottleneck?<br /> The last two are details on individuals including rules to repurpose one as a daredevil/paramorph post Venezuela event.<br /> Your style works well in these, like the mode power descriptions, i would be tempted to think your greatest weakness as an author is in word count.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i> Geoff wrote all of chapters 3 and 4 himself (I may have tweaked a couple of sections, but those were almost entirely him).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to take away from your own contributions here, but he did a great job. I can't actually see myself accepting it all at face value, maybe changing a few dates and adding some more ambiguity in places. The Doyen section in particular seems like it could have been turned into something more with the details given, yet the threshold is ultimately never crossed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i> Jake wrote chapter 5.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>A pity that the 'Diablo's Asteroid' gear didn't make it in - that would have been fun super-science for the 2120s. This is something i'll have to consider expanding myself one day, the notion of a Rogue Chib/Aberrant scientific alliance is well tailored to the post Venezuela Effect setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i> Geoff wrote almost all of chapter 6 except most of the Character templates which Jake wrote with some input from me (Xavier was a character I actually played in a couple of games).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean about Geoff, he put a lot of the core information together in terms of importance and sheer imagination.<br /> I'd be interested to hear a summary of your experience gaming as Xavier Sloane, if you have the time and inclination. Consider it an expanded character background, if that helps.<br /> Perhaps i'm just forgetting where, but i can't remember ever seeing the 'thought discipline' ability before, where did this come from? Seems almost a little too handy...<br /> <br /> Thanks again for the reply Slagheap, all apologies for my lateness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=467116#post467116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a problem. It's going to take me a few days to do anything with the material for you, though. I have a deadline at work coming up very soon, plus having a week of business travel coming up right after. Now that I know there is still interest in, I'll find motivation, but real life unfortunately has a bit of creep right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Real life has this boorish habit of taking priority over the terribly important business of fandom. -smile-<br /> I'll let you know when i have more for you if you'd like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  There had to be something... -facepalm- 04-08-2015, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T16:56:53-07:00","id":473515,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Spark Soldiers</b><br /> <br /> Both Spark Soldiers and Spark Juice come from my actual games. For few years, Aberrant was the only rpg I was running (and I was doing twice weekly sessions at that). So alot of my personal game notes and home brew ideas ended up being submitted to various fan projects. The Spark Soldiers were a way to introduce super-powered cannon fodder into the game world while staying within the thematic boundaries of how rare and unique each nova truly was. I provided mechanics and general ideas and let the project wordsmiths polish the concepts. Overall some of my better work.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Combat</b><br /> <br /> With my Combat contributions, I went for something that could be used across all the game lines, but felt true to the real world sources. Basing it off of skills specialties was something I felt that with allow the system to be plugged into an existing game with little trouble.<br /> If I had to do over, I would make the combat styles Merit based (similar to NWOD) and I would have tried to streamline things to keep combat moving quickly.<br /> <br /> I am very sensitive to game balance, but I ran into the hazards of creating way more content than a dedicated team of players could working through in a year. Ultimately I went my instincts. Having played for years with players who seemed to go out of their way to break systems into a million pieces, I developed a good sense of where the system held up, where it bent,and where it broke andlet that be my guiding star. Some of my concepts could stand to be refined, but hopefully not too many, and not too much.<br /> <br /> Looking over the rules, leaving out things like the strength limits feels like an oversight, and would be corrected if I had to do it again.<br /> <br /> As common for the fan projects, there are more ideas in play than what any of us could have rigorously play tested. Most of the time my players were still finding out cool tricks from the published sources, while I had devoured the published sources and was filling in the spaces the canon material didn't cover.If you ever decide to crack open the Trinity books and play with any of those ideas, i would love to know what works and what doesn't.<br /> <br /> At least for my part, it felt to me that the three settings could have benefited from more mechanical cohesion, as I say them and different pieces of a muchlarger story, and playing one part as if theothers didn't exist always felt weird. As such I always used all three settings as a reference point and in points of conflict, I went with what I felt was the strongest example (usually Adventure or Trinity - as much as I love Aberrant, i could almost hear the system groaning under the strain of supporting such a high-power genre).<br /> When i get my hands on Sardonix I am probably going to see if I can update and convert some of the ideas in my old files.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Sources of Injury</b><br /> <br /> This material was almost copy/pasted word for word from my notes. I have enjoyed enjoyed running games where the primary antagonist is nature and the environment. And I had immense fun putting Nova characters into environments that would be fatal to baselines. This involved a good of amout of real world research but I think it translated into alot of cool elements to spice up a session.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Chapter 4</b><br /> <br /> Another place where the many of the powers and enhancements I contributed were clipped right from my notes. This was very much a &quot;drink from the hose&quot; chapter. I think we went into this went so much enthusiasm because at least for those of us working on things, Aberrant had so much depth to the setting that was begging to be explored, trying to answer the fundamental position of the setting - <i>what would you do with the power of a god</i>. Over all, most the material is good, some of it is bad,and much of it is just weird (you can decide what is what as you read the material).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 04-08-2015, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:12:21-07:00","id":473569,"title":"","content":"Let's see if I can respond to your comments coherently. A lot of this stuff is a fairly fuzzy memory.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 1 and 2 Generally</b><br /> I just named Project Harmony. Geoff had already written about it, but he hadn't given it a name. I thought naming it made it easier to talk about.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure only wrote the side bars in chapters 1 and 2.<br /> <br /> While I was (and to a degree still am) fairly pleased with the modes I wrote, the general setting stuff I wrote is a mess. It's pretty much an uncontrolled dumpster fire. The modes though I think still hold up pretty well. Design wise, we were writing these after Terra Verde was published. So, we sort of used that as a guide and tried to present something that hinted at the kinds of powers you might see in Aberrant without just making mode dots = specific aberrant powers.<br /> <br /> <b>The Other Chapters Generally</b><br /> I can't speak much to the rest. For the most part I tried to leave everything Geoff wrote as he wrote it. It was never the plan that I would be the one with final edit on the book, so I didn't want to disrupt the work that was already done. I think the only thing I changed was the part about the Chib that gets tainted (don't really remember where it was in the book or the name of the character). Geoff had originally written it so that the guy actually became a tainted psion that turned into something like an aberrant character with lots of aberrations. He then had the guy charge off into the sunset like a big monstrous plot hook. I changed it because, as it was originally written, it directly contradicted prior statements in earlier official books about how psi and taint would interact. I don't think I still have the original version anywhere. In hind sight that might not have been too cool of me. But, I really didn't like the original version.<br /> <br /> I don't know what came of Geoff. I think he was from New Zealand. Last I heard he was in college somewhere, but that was a decade ago at least.<br /> <br /> <b>Xavier</b><br /> I don't really have any stories to share about him, other than to explain his original creation. He was a character I switched to in the middle of a game while my main character was written out of the story for a bit. Xavier was intended to be totally reasonable at all times. My GM at the time (Jake, the artist), used him as a plot device to convince some of the other players that the Big Bad in our story (a Rogue Chib) was actually a bad guy. He was supposed to die making that point (and at the time did).<br /> But I enjoyed him so much (and the other players liked him too), so we retconned in a last minute medical rescue for him and brought him back for another story some years later.<br /> <br /> Thought Discipline is a special ability that Directive agents could get in Aberrant. The rules are from the Directive Source book. The story was that he had rediscovered the techniques for Though Discipline and written his Doctoral Dissertation on it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T21:24:06-07:00","id":473832,"title":"","content":"This is a slight tangent, but as I found it in the EON Archive, it's pertinent to this thread. Mind you, I'm about to go on a rant about one particular fan product I found in the Archive, namely Space Tactics a.k.a. &quot;Tactics and Strategy in Three Dimensions: How to Wage Combat in Space.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know this is a fan product so it's quality is not going to be up to the standards of an officially published book, but I swear, this thing reads like it was written by someone who learned English as a second language. One of the headings is titled &quot;Aloneness&quot; which isn't even a word (&quot;Solitude&quot; or &quot;Self-sufficiency&quot; would have been mildly better choices given the subject of not being able to depend on anyone but yourself). And near the beginning of the essay, beam weapons are mentioned as being advantageous as they do not need ammunition (because they're energy weapons, natch); literally two sentences later, the author says &quot;remember that a number of weapons become beam weapons; with no gravity, mortars and artillery shells have no arcs.&quot; So what this author is essentially saying is that beam/energy weapons don't require ammunition but ammunition fired in space becomes a beam/energy weapon simply because there's no gravity to give the ammunition a downward arc.<br /> <br /> WTF?<br /> <br /> The best/worst part was when I read that (and this is what convinced me the author needed to have his ass removed with a spoon) radar is essentially useless in space (and I shit you not that the author wrote this) because apparently <i>radio waves can't travel through a vacuum</i>.<br /> <br /> Double WTF??<br /> <br /> If anyone here doubts whether radio waves can travel through a vacuum, I refer you to Project Diana, conducted in 1946, where the US Army bounced radio waves off the surface of the Moon. Now, I'm no astronomer, but I'm willing to wager that there's quite a bit of vacuum between Earth's atmosphere and the Moon. And that's not even mentioning all the radio and television waves radiating out from Earth into space for the last 70+ years. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So once I finished reading that paragraph, I thought that the author simply confused radar and sonar. But then a couple paragraphs later, under the heading &quot;Vacuum,&quot; he writes &quot;Something that you have this much of needs to be noted. Radar and sonar do not work in a vacuum (lidar systems work fine, however).&quot; As for that first sentence, doesn't that read like it was written by someone who learned English as a second language? It took me a minute to realize that the &quot;something&quot; he's referring to is vacuum and I only realized that because &quot;Vacuum&quot; was the heading of the paragraph, rather than actually mentioning the word &quot;vacuum&quot; in the sentence itself. And as for the second sentence, the author merely compounds his previous error by restating that radar doesn't work in vacuum (false) and then mentions sonar not working in vacuum either (which is true but is so obvious it's like saying water is wet). And by mentioning radar and sonar in the same sentence, the author seems to realize that they're two different things (even though he seemed to conflate the two just a couple of paragraphs ago) but doesn't realize that they work <i>very </i>differently in vacuum.<br /> <br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my rant's finished. If you're in the mood to facepalm at something, by all means, read Space Tactics. But if you're looking for something useful for space combat rules for Trinity, look elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T10:43:14-07:00","id":474482,"title":"","content":"-settles in-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473515#post473515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Spark Soldiers</b><br /> <br /> Both Spark Soldiers and Spark Juice come from my actual games. For few years, Aberrant was the only rpg I was running (and I was doing twice weekly sessions at that). So alot of my personal game notes and home brew ideas ended up being submitted to various fan projects. The Spark Soldiers were a way to introduce super-powered cannon fodder into the game world while staying within the thematic boundaries of how rare and unique each nova truly was. I provided mechanics and general ideas and let the project wordsmiths polish the concepts. Overall some of my better work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a fun ride for a while there, i had a similar run from the end of the 1990s to the early 2000s, so i can respect that self-hamster-wheel method of play-testing. My brother ran the game out of its native setting and would almost definitely have used this (i think, because he liked his cannon fodder), i myself could see Spark Soldiers still being made in post-apocalyptic middle-eastern labs headed up by either pre-Venezuela event remnants or even being deregulated by the Trinity to protect against 2122+ inspired.<br /> The matter-of-fact point about Spark Soldiers being a pure innovation (as opposed to an advancement, from Adventure's super science chapter) unable to be recreated by the non-inspired is a very clever touch (as is the taint/age limit). Using core rules from one of the main books to limit the technology to time-periods of greater threats prevailing, turning the creators into Gauntlet-like spawners for game-play purposes and restricting their use in periods where they could be abused.<br /> You say you let the project writers fill in the setting material, but i'd love to hear (due to my own interests) how this technology might have developed toward the end of the era. Specifically whether some extension to lifespan might have seen some Spark Soldiers still lurking about in the 2060s and early 70s; a period which i've spent a lot of time thinking about. No pressure, but since you are the original author and i'm interested, it seems a waste to not ask.<br /> Thanks for sharing these rules and discussing them, they look like fun on paper. Just to finish up, do you want to take a crack at describing what type of arrangements of these things you would personally use against a team of PC novas? Numbers, powers, gear, that kind of thing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473515#post473515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Combat</b><br /> <br /> With my Combat contributions, I went for something that could be used across all the game lines, but felt true to the real world sources. Basing it off of skills specialties was something I felt that with allow the system to be plugged into an existing game with little trouble.<br /> If I had to do over, I would make the combat styles Merit based (similar to NWOD) and I would have tried to streamline things to keep combat moving quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I spent some time wondering about the fundamental relations between specialities, backgrounds/adversarial-backgrounds and merits/flaws myself, but i never got to see some of the interesting things nWOD did with the ideas (strictly oWOD here).<br /> Honestly, some of the Baroqueness of your combat style rules are what draws me in - as long as it stays on the character creation/advancement side of the ST screen; i've found burying players in complex options that can be reduced to easily understood and recorded in-game effects makes for happy players. But, i would be remiss to not agree that in-game combat encounters need to flow at decent to rapid rates. In that respect, i'm yet to read anything in the combat section that slows down turn-by-turn play like multiple purchases of Quickness straight from the core-book anyway.<br /> My balance snark has much tastier morsels to growl at then the well-intentioned, optional, expanded combat rules you've presented. -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473515#post473515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very sensitive to game balance, but I ran into the hazards of creating way more content than a dedicated team of players could working through in a year. Ultimately I went my instincts. Having played for years with players who seemed to go out of their way to break systems into a million pieces, I developed a good sense of where the system held up, where it bent,and where it broke andlet that be my guiding star. Some of my concepts could stand to be refined, but hopefully not too many, and not too much.<br /> <br /> Looking over the rules, leaving out things like the strength limits feels like an oversight, and would be corrected if I had to do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your experience shows, after a while veteran STs like yourself can generally see balance in the numbers and have learned to improvise adjustments on the fly. But you can't really teach that and younger STs will sometimes need the support granted by well-treaded/tested rulings. The New Flesh as a whole is a grab bag of toys, but not all are created equal - so far your contributions have been well-received on my end, so i trust your instinct enough to want to try some of them at least.<br /> I still don't know how Totentanz always appears with two full spears then... Probably all promotional shots. -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473515#post473515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As common for the fan projects, there are more ideas in play than what any of us could have rigorously play tested. Most of the time my players were still finding out cool tricks from the published sources, while I had devoured the published sources and was filling in the spaces the canon material didn't cover.If you ever decide to crack open the Trinity books and play with any of those ideas, i would love to know what works and what doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The New Flesh credits page was suspiciously void of any play-tester credits, but i didn't want to assume. I understand how that comes about, it just strikes me as strange to have so many contributors, yet so little quality assurance in comparison. Like a cart without a horse.<br /> I feel kind of guilty, knowing that i'm banking on fan-authors being starved of feedback to draw them out. Yet, a project like the New Flesh with all its promise and content never got the benefit of in-house critique in the form of quality assurance or play-testing. Surely opinions would have dripped from every surface? What am i missing? Was the whole thing done in a locked forum with no public access or something of that ilk?<br /> I visited EON when The New Flesh was being put together there - whoever was webmaster at the time had no issue granting me access on request and i copied everything i could get my hands on (mostly stuff from the appendix, if i remember correctly). But there wasn't much there to comment on at the time and i wasn't certain how welcome i would be posting in a locked forum.<br /> -shrug-<br /> Because i write my own house-rules and have just now shared some online, i can sympathize with your interest in feedback. I'll try to promise i'll let you know with a PM here on Onyx Path if/when i do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473515#post473515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least for my part, it felt to me that the three settings could have benefited from more mechanical cohesion, as I say them and different pieces of a muchlarger story, and playing one part as if theothers didn't exist always felt weird. As such I always used all three settings as a reference point and in points of conflict, I went with what I felt was the strongest example (usually Adventure or Trinity - as much as I love Aberrant, i could almost hear the system groaning under the strain of supporting such a high-power genre).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well put, if you just ignore the typos.<br /> -tease-<br /> I agree with this sentiment and generally take a similar approach, while the PCs may be having a ball, the ST is privy to just how badly Quantum powers are breaking the universe. All the PCs have to worry about by contrast is Taint and i personally heard that groaning as weeping. -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473515#post473515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When i get my hands on Sardonix I am probably going to see if I can update and convert some of the ideas in my old files.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let us know when you do, i'll certainly be interested. Include rules for orbital re-entry on different planets too, please. -smile-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473515#post473515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Sources of Injury</b><br /> <br /> This material was almost copy/pasted word for word from my notes. I have enjoyed enjoyed running games where the primary antagonist is nature and the environment. And I had immense fun putting Nova characters into environments that would be fatal to baselines. This involved a good of amout of real world research but I think it translated into alot of cool elements to spice up a session.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had heaps of occasion to use such a reference during my own games, instead i ended up fudging everything. With so much of my Aberrant games taking place in hostile off-world environments, i can sympathize with nature as antagonist in a way. I took heaps of liberties dropping the tainted nova PCs into normally fatal situations and making them think fast to survive too. Perhaps this is why i see your work here as such a valuable contribution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473515#post473515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Chapter 4</b><br /> <br /> Another place where the many of the powers and enhancements I contributed were clipped right from my notes. This was very much a &quot;drink from the hose&quot; chapter. I think we went into this went so much enthusiasm because at least for those of us working on things, Aberrant had so much depth to the setting that was begging to be explored, trying to answer the fundamental position of the setting - <i>what would you do with the power of a god</i>. Over all, most the material is good, some of it is bad,and much of it is just weird (you can decide what is what as you read the material).</div> </div> </div> </div>If i make it back here for some reason i'll be sure to post comments. &quot;Drink from the Hose&quot; sounds right, i think i used &quot;drowning&quot; to describe the depth and number of powers and enhancements found there. If there are any you contributed that you would recommend on the level of your Spark Soldier tier work, please point them out. Browsing them all one-by-one is a little numbing.<br /> Thanks again, Reighnhell. Not only do i appreciate your feedback, i actually agree with most of it too.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473569#post473569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's see if I can respond to your comments coherently. A lot of this stuff is a fairly fuzzy memory.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 1 and 2 Generally</b><br /> I just named Project Harmony. Geoff had already written about it, but he hadn't given it a name. I thought naming it made it easier to talk about.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure only wrote the side bars in chapters 1 and 2.<br /> <br /> While I was (and to a degree still am) fairly pleased with the modes I wrote, the general setting stuff I wrote is a mess. It's pretty much an uncontrolled dumpster fire. The modes though I think still hold up pretty well. Design wise, we were writing these after Terra Verde was published. So, we sort of used that as a guide and tried to present something that hinted at the kinds of powers you might see in Aberrant without just making mode dots = specific aberrant powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely useful to be able to identify the cause of the purge under a single heading, good organizational etiquette. The 'uncontrolled dumpster fire' is a fun visual, i would instead suggest your style doesn't lend itself to such a spectacle, even in failure. Don't take this as an insult, just critical analysis, the setting information you wrote was less revealing than the ST section and still concise enough that i used it to introduce a player to the order - so in that regards it wasn't useless/failed in my experience.<br /> Your modes are good. I think they fit better than some of the official Teleportation modes, so whatever schema you were using seems to have worked out. You clearly weren't trying to balance out the differences between the Aberrant and Trinity systems too heavily, why the decision to mimic the appearance/capabilities of Aberrant powers? Just bringing the 'quantum glove' of QK to bear in the systems?<br /> Because i hounded Reighnhell so hard about it; did you do any play testing of these rules? How were they balanced?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473569#post473569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Other Chapters Generally</b><br /> I can't speak much to the rest. For the most part I tried to leave everything Geoff wrote as he wrote it. It was never the plan that I would be the one with final edit on the book, so I didn't want to disrupt the work that was already done. I think the only thing I changed was the part about the Chib that gets tainted (don't really remember where it was in the book or the name of the character). Geoff had originally written it so that the guy actually became a tainted psion that turned into something like an aberrant character with lots of aberrations. He then had the guy charge off into the sunset like a big monstrous plot hook. I changed it because, as it was originally written, it directly contradicted prior statements in earlier official books about how psi and taint would interact. I don't think I still have the original version anywhere. In hind sight that might not have been too cool of me. But, I really didn't like the original version.<br /> <br /> I don't know what came of Geoff. I think he was from New Zealand. Last I heard he was in college somewhere, but that was a decade ago at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are talking about Sajeesh Pilarkat (p65), in my copy i have that story pretty much as you describe it.<br /> - Early QK loses control of powers, taint-field instability given as reason.<br /> - Loss of control leads to instant mutational tainting of said QK, Order puts subject into confinement alongside aberrants.<br /> - Tainted QK is both described as both being irradiated with and being diseased by enough Taint to kill a human.<br /> - Tainted QK escapes to the Himalayas in the chaos of 2109 QK purge, seeking a cure for his condition.<br /> <br /> If this is the changed version, what exactly did you change? As far as i can tell it's the same in the version CHILL has posted in his EON archive, so either your memory is playing tricks on you or there is another version circulating.<br /> I guess the idea of Taint affecting a Psion in the same manner as it does Aberrants isn't really clear cut - i'd like to hear your expanded thoughts here since you clearly spent time considering it at some point.<br /> <br /> To play devil's advocate; i thought that Taint disease could affect Psions just maybe more rarely than the un-dunked - with some exceptions for Bio- and Vita-kinetics. Taint Virus/Bacteria once mutated and physical is no longer subject to sub-quantum nullification alone, it needs chemical and biological treatment alongside the noetics.<br /> If infested with enough tainted matter, a Psion could feasibly become a source of further Taint propagation. Taint tends to mutate the noetic template of a subject/victim leading to physical mutation in earth-based life forms. If Pilarkat's 'quantum glove' slipped when he was psionicly manipulating a dangerous amount of taint, it seems reasonable that a high enough dosage could see him seriously affected. Given he was a talented QK he might be able to survive the exposure due to a reflexive defence against the Taint better than most other sufferers.<br /> Care to take a crack, if i'm understanding it right?<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473569#post473569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Xavier</b><br /> I don't really have any stories to share about him, other than to explain his original creation. He was a character I switched to in the middle of a game while my main character was written out of the story for a bit. Xavier was intended to be totally reasonable at all times. My GM at the time (Jake, the artist), used him as a plot device to convince some of the other players that the Big Bad in our story (a Rogue Chib) was actually a bad guy. He was supposed to die making that point (and at the time did).<br /> But I enjoyed him so much (and the other players liked him too), so we retconned in a last minute medical rescue for him and brought him back for another story some years later.<br /> <br /> Thought Discipline is a special ability that Directive agents could get in Aberrant. The rules are from the Directive Source book. The story was that he had rediscovered the techniques for Though Discipline and written his Doctoral Dissertation on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the original creation counts as a story - any time a NPC makes a positive personal impact on a group it's worthy of memory. It's one of those things that tabletop RPGs do; but doesn't really happen in any other form of entertainment.<br /> I haven't spent much time with the Directive source - not my setting. Occasionally my brother mentions things out of it and i feel just as naked. Probably something i should add to my list...<br /> Thanks for the reply, Slagheap. I know a lot of this is fuzzy for you so i appreciate the effort, if it's of any consolation the torrent of questions i would have for Geoff Bain would have been much worse. -smile-<br /> I don't remember all that well, but i have the distinct impression that India Underground was one of the first fan-produced materials i discovered and i needed to read much of it back through because of how long has passed in between. Some of it has become indivisible from canon in my games - including Dhiren aberrant capture, Project Harmony, rogue Chibs and concealed Psion-made Taint reduction processes. It's been a very handy and durable (despite being bound together with simple binding clips) addition to my collection over the years - for that i thank you for the time you put into it, no matter any flaws.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=473832#post473832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a slight tangent, but as I found it in the EON Archive, it's pertinent to this thread. Mind you, I'm about to go on a rant about one particular fan product I found in the Archive, namely Space Tactics a.k.a. &quot;Tactics and Strategy in Three Dimensions: How to Wage Combat in Space.&quot;<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> WTF?<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Double WTF??<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my rant's finished. If you're in the mood to facepalm at something, by all means, read Space Tactics. But if you're looking for something useful for space combat rules for Trinity, look elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Savage words. I suspect much context is missing from this document as it stands, more than just physical laws are bent in its text. But i defend its right to interpretation, maybe the author had a vision for a radar-less vacuum and preferred that to what hard-science offered. I've heard it said that Aeon/Trinity 'isn't about the tech, it's about the psions', and while i'd personally go without psions before going without tech in my sci-fi - it's none-the-less how many approach the setting.<br /> But, your opinion is as valid on the subject as anyone else. Feel free to tear apart one of my (mostly unfinished) docs in the 'Nihilist Contributions' folder, i'm certain i'll prove a more satisfying target.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> Thanks for the quick replies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T15:32:47-07:00","id":474977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=474482#post474482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Savage words. I suspect much context is missing from this document as it stands, more than just physical laws are bent in its text. But i defend its right to interpretation, maybe the author had a vision for a radar-less vacuum and preferred that to what hard-science offered. I've heard it said that Aeon/Trinity 'isn't about the tech, it's about the psions', and while i'd personally go without psions before going without tech in my sci-fi - it's none-the-less how many approach the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. While I must honestly call myself a bigger fan of &quot;soft sci-fi&quot; like Star Wars and Star Trek than I am of Aeon/Trinity, I do find the hard sci-fi aspects of Trinity a very refreshing change of pace. Granted, the psions themselves are soft but much of the tech is hard, and seeing both in the same place makes for very useful tools for a Storyteller. But the whole thing about radar not working in vacuum goes beyond &quot;hard vs. soft&quot; sci-fi and jumps feet-first into Flat Earth nonsense. It's one thing to have stuff like warp speed tech that can &quot;bend&quot; the rules of relativity. It's damn well another to say that radio waves can't travel in a vacuum when we've known <i>since the last century</i> that they do. My problem isn't soft sci-fi <i>per se</i>, it's sloppy research. Either that or it's a case of They Just Didn't Care.<br /> <br /> In any case, anything that makes reasonably seasoned sci-fi fans like us who actually have a smattering of understanding of scientific laws (or just folks who just watched the new <i>Cosmos </i>with Neil deGrasse Tyson last year) put their faces in their palms should be excluded from a Trinity book, fanmade or (especially!) official.<br /> <br /> (SHAMELESS PLUG TIME: If you haven't see the new Cosmos, I <i>very </i>heartily recommend it. Not only do the special effects make it visually entertaining, but Dr. Tyson uses language that's very easy for the viewer to understand. Buying the whole series on DVD or BluRay is well worth the price. And who knows, there might be useful tidbits that would be useful for a hard Sci-fi Trinity campaign. The new rendition of Carl Sagan's <i>Pale Blue Dot</i> speech alone can give you a sense of scale of how vast, compared to Earth, the solar system really is. Not to mention some beautiful shots of the Mars surface as well as other exotic locations in the solar system that are shown elsewhere in the episodes.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=474482#post474482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, your opinion is as valid on the subject as anyone else. Feel free to tear apart one of my (mostly unfinished) docs in the 'Nihilist Contributions' folder, I'm certain I'll prove a more satisfying target.<br /> -smile-</div> </div> </div> </div>Be careful what you wish for, my friend....<br /> <br /> *grins wickedly*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 04-09-2015, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T00:44:19-07:00","id":482092,"title":"","content":"From another thread, in regards to <i>A Breed Apart</i>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/423285-building-a-trinity-era-nova-sane-ones-please?p=481932#post481932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It lost me a few pages in. Fan supplements tend to do that to me, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, to each their own. Any particular reason why? Although i don't get much use out of it myself, i tend to agree with Su-tehp that it's an easy read at least. I would have done much of it differently, but the writing isn't as hard to decipher as others, as far as i remember.<br /> Could be interesting to hear another writer's opinion is all.<br /> Yes, i'm still getting to commenting on your fiction (in the coming weekend, i hope), apologies for this delay - i'm fighting off a flu and i lack the brain.<br /> -sniffle-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/423285-building-a-trinity-era-nova-sane-ones-please?p=482048#post482048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Breed Apart has to be the single best fanbook I've ever encountered for the Aeonverse. It just looks and feels like an official book even though I know it's not. Also, the idea of the conflict between the motherhunters and the delivery boys is one I find intriguing. Not to mention it has alot of <i>really </i>unfortunate implications for the Trinity era if a Storyteller were to use Hatcher Aberrants in his Trinity campaign. Just consider if just even one hatcher Aberrant survived the Exile and managed to have 60 years worth of offspring...</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally found A Breed Apart a little contradictory from a strictly 2120s perspective, the second and third generations of Nova offspring seem perfectly capable of changing the endgame in 2061 and don't entirely comply to what we see in the Aeon/Trinity era. I did like the hatchers, but it was a concept i'd already played with in my own curiously Aberrant-centric view of the 2120s, but eventually rejected due to my understanding of the low statistical occurrence of Aberrants in that era. Maybe somewhere off-world, but nowhere local. While it was an easy read and i do feel most makes sense, i simply didn't have much room for it - it's one of the few fan-supplements that stay on the shelf in my own games (in 2120, where i have hard-wired my own version of 2nd &amp; 3rd generation Novas into the setting).<br /> I really enjoyed the Noetics Field Report (for the Sci-Fi aspect), Asia Ascendant and Brainwaves - with special mention to the incomplete Storytellers Guide. I know two were technically official, but they were bold and consistent and changed the way i saw some aspect of the game.<br /> -shrug-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Too many uses of a particular word. 04-16-2015, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T16:47:37-07:00","id":482933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=482092#post482092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From another thread, in regards to <i>A Breed Apart</i>:<br /> <br /> Fair enough, to each their own. Any particular reason why? Although i don't get much use out of it myself, i tend to agree with Su-tehp that it's an easy read at least. I would have done much of it differently, but the writing isn't as hard to decipher as others, as far as i remember.<br /> Could be interesting to hear another writer's opinion is all.<br /> Yes, i'm still getting to commenting on your fiction (in the coming weekend, i hope), apologies for this delay - i'm fighting off a flu and i lack the brain.<br /> -sniffle-</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it reads and feels like a fan supplement to me. Some of the characterizations seem off, and even forced, particularly what Justin Laragione was saying in the earliest section. Even when he disagreed with AEON or Thetis, I could still get some sense of the character and where his loyalties and conflicts rested. His words in that section read like the storyteller saying &quot;this is story that is being told, and just go with it with a minimal amount of questions, please.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's my opinion, obviously, and I know it's probably not one that others agree with.<br /> <br /> I also almost never enjoy anything fan-created that introduce new systems or materials into the setting. I found the detail on what happens to female novas during pregnancy unnecessary and even a bit...awkward. I can't recall reading rules for pregnancy in any previous game and certainly not anything produced under the White Wolf banner.<br /> <br /> New Flesh, for example, read mostly to me like a power-gamer's playground instead of adding anything meaningful into the setting about what it would mean to have Mega-Physicals.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","name":"Ashnod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T02:51:52-07:00","id":483376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=482933#post482933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it reads and feels like a fan supplement to me. Some of the characterizations seem off, and even forced, particularly what Justin Laragione was saying in the earliest section. Even when he disagreed with AEON or Thetis, I could still get some sense of the character and where his loyalties and conflicts rested. His words in that section read like the storyteller saying &quot;this is story that is being told, and just go with it with a minimal amount of questions, please.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I think i agree, some of the language in that Laragione directive (p4) doesn't feel right. It's something i've been guilty of myself at times - putting words into an established character's mouth without taking the time to tailor it to their style of saying it. I think it comes from too much gaming writing and not enough fiction writing - because once those points need explaining in-game i tend to go all in on the character's personal spin - but that isn't reflected in the writing.<br /> All it takes is to use an unimportant name and most of the issue goes away, but i wouldn't claim to have the character insight you are capable of. I'd love to hear the guidelines you might adhere to for writing Laragione, just from memory.<br /> But this is what's expected from fan supplements, which rarely have editors, play-testers or other QA folks. The work is done as a labour of love and may never be looked at again after it's submitted - going straight into circulation. Entirely free fan-books are a different beast entirely from a published book and dismissing them all due to their origin is generalizing, not that they get all that much better, but they aren't promising the same yield as legitimate published books might either.<br /> I can get harsher on these creations, but unless that critique can go towards an improved product, i feel like it's a waste of time. Instead, i'm just glad to get a chance to interact with some of the contributors that have variably entertained, frustrated and completely lost me over the years. No need to scare them away with scathing critique, i figure. Maybe i could start another thread for <i>that</i> purpose.<br /> -smile-<br /> But don't take this the wrong way, i'd love for you to take a run at some of these books to counter-weight my own forgiving style of commentary - after all, no writer really wants to be soft-balled by critics when they could be learning from mistakes and improving. Do they?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=482933#post482933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also almost never enjoy anything fan-created that introduce new systems or materials into the setting. I found the detail on what happens to female novas during pregnancy unnecessary and even a bit...awkward. I can't recall reading rules for pregnancy in any previous game and certainly not anything produced under the White Wolf banner.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Almost? So there is something fan-created that you have enjoyed previously?<br /> Yeah, i wasn't a big fan of the concepts A Breed Apart introduced. Rules for any aspect of sex have little use in my games and i don't know if i'd want them in there. I mean, there is the genetic aspect and romantic aspect which are both indivisible from a dramatic standpoint - but neither need dedicated gaming systems, in this gamers opinion. Too much micro-management leaves little room for improvisation. The 10 to 1 ratio of male to female writers probably didn't help much either.<br /> Since you have a 2nd Generation Nova in your fiction (Apep), perhaps you could share your vision of Nova pregnancy and children?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=482933#post482933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Flesh, for example, read mostly to me like a power-gamer's playground instead of adding anything meaningful into the setting about what it would mean to have Mega-Physicals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, i commented on how little setting information the New Flesh actually contained, it works as a grab bag of combat rules but has little else to offer the setting as a single work. With all due respect to Reighnhell, the New Flesh lacked a sense of direction and vision and over-compensated with pure rules.<br /> Reighnhell also worked on A Breed Apart, so maybe he would like to reply to this...<br /> -shrug-<br /> Okay, onto the 1001 Aberrant Nights.<br /> ...<br /> <br /> <u>Ashnod's Declaration</u><br /> XWF, eh? Ok, you set the scene well in a brief camera pan and then launch straight into the commentary team - setting up the Catalysts (loaded name, took me a second pass to read it as a group name), their loose relation to the Teragen (at least in XWF eyes) and pushing the brutality of the arena. I had completely forgotten there were casual nova fatalities, i'd assumed most fatalities were from the mitoids trying to keep up - which wouldn't work here.<br /> While the premise is great, i feel Ashnod's actual declaration runs a little long and may be a little florid for the minds who consume the XWF. Lucky there is some social power-set at play, although i would have preferred you to describe <i>Awe Inspiring</i> rather than simply call it out anime style, because a live crowd might have ignored the material and instead entertained itself with anti-terat chants (or similar) - which might have decreased the impact somewhat.<br /> Otherwise, this is a good hook and i'm interested to see where you go from here. Any particular reason why the XWF drew you in? Seems out of beat a little with the rest of the articles, but not really in a bad way.<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume I Issue I</u><br /> This is a really solid piece of character establishment, i get a sense for Sherazahde and even more i like her. She shows humility, humour and compassion without subtracting from any other elements of the setting. Your use of the setting is nice as well, subtle enough to keep things framed without getting in too deep on anything (except maybe the Nova rights issues).<br /> Great, i hope there is more like this.<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume I Issue II</u><br /> Wow, you really have a way with this character. The media savvy way you present the 'zine politics and the pleasant words with which Sherazahde protests the invasion of her personal identity by the editors all conjure the allusion of a person (nova) with opinions and background all her own, unrelated to the few details she drops in the previous article.<br /> The way you have the article still be the meat, but bleed through the character is rather well done. I don't know where the over-plot is going here, but the work here doesn't derail that despite how fabulous Sherazahde is (at least not yet).<br /> Are you playing with sexism on the 'innocent enough' lines? It seems Sherazahde isn't really the precious type - is this clash a product of the magazine content or just meant to be representative of standard concerns for publishers of the time?<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume I Issue III</u><br /> Well, damn. This is just getting better. You just conjured more setting material for mega physical than 'The New Flesh' does in 200+ pages. It's creepy and provocative, grounded only by the half-drunken commentary. While the perfectionist in me suggests that it lacks something to put it over the edge into true brilliance, i would none-the-less recommend this as excellent setting material for the Amp Room. Better introduction than what we get in the first entry (Ashnod's Declaration) for Machina. So this one deserves praise.<br /> If anything, i would prefer to see a little characterization of Count Orzaiz, just because everyone else seems to get some and your style seems like you could affect a decent Orzaiz. Similarly, i have littleclue who Sin-Eater is after this, but i get the impression this might be intentional. The public fellatio is a bit much, but this is the Amp Room and a bit much <i>is</i> called for, i just might have preferred more suggestion than declaration (did Sherazahde verify for herself that there was mouth to penis contact amidst the mess those two end up in?).<br /> It's kind of strange to see you write in the intended accent - should i assume this is an idiosyncracy of Sherazahde? Or yours? Getting a bit meta, i know...<br /> <br /> <u>Unaired interview with Dr. Nathaniel Prescott</u><br /> You wrote; 'End Day', i presume you meant N-Day? Just a detail.<br /> My goodness, Ashnod. I was expecting much less than you're delivering here, mysterious secret origin stuff with great characterization of <i>Machina</i> and a spectacular baseline perspective on her eruption. I really like the human duplicity in being mesmerized and frightened (over-awed?)by their employers transformation, the sense they are struggling with their own perceptions - regardless of what their head is telling them.<br /> The year of this event seems curiously missing, as it reads as retrospective. The image of Dr. Ramsey prior to eruption is mostly seen from the eyes of others and leaves some further characterization to be desired on the personal front - although her interview questions address this, she remains too distant to get a feel for.<br /> Because i am a sucker for anything resembling Sci-Fi, the lab setting of this article contributes to it being my favourite so far - only slightly edging out the charming Sherazahde.<br /> <br /> <u>Unaired lecture/presentation by Alexi Boreanz</u><br /> This one counted a seventeen pages in my Copy/Paste document - so i'm glad you got me hooked in the earlier articles.<br /> There is, therefore, much to be commented upon here. The narrative is US-centric, but with fair reason to be, given the location and speaker. Clever work conflating the Teragen with youth disillusionment, i've always felt the possibility of the Teragen undergoing some kind of 'heel/face turn' as Utopia gains notoriety was inevitable by the end of the war, you feed into that a bit here.<br /> Slightly Jarring to hear Ashnod go from Anthropology to Sixth Sense and back again without providing support like she has with her other arguments. Since everything else in this article has been academic in presentation. That derailed my reading a bit, because 'psychic' can be a loaded term in the greater setting, relating to Psionics and other noetic/telleric weirdness - which is mostly avoided by Aberrant. I'm not sure if i should be thinking about those sources in relation to this, because i don't know how much of it you are using here.<br /> Your descriptions of eruptions really are special, a lovely intersection of the human and post-human, i'd love to see more in that vein. Nice twist at the end, again there is just a little something missing from really putting it over the edge, but an excellent bit of writing.<br /> Purely for the sake of concision, i'd want Ashnod to cut down on the loquaciousness - the narrative gets bogged down by the (intriguing none-the-less) philosophy. But, after her declaration in part one, i'm going to take it as a character trait. Certainly the proper deployment of social powers can easily buy up the attention of an audience for the time she uses - but her powers don't quite reach the reader.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume II Issue XI</u><br /> Wow.<br /> I said i wanted more eruption material and here it is. I have to ask whether this was much work or whether the idea came and the writing afterwards was comparatively easy.<br /> Sherazahde is charming and colourful as usual, Fracture is (as advertised) harrowing. At this point i'm actually not really reading for critical analysis - just enjoying the writing, but i notice that the thread of nova rights isn't really explored here for the first time since the opening article. Maybe i'm reaching for an over-arching link between them all, but fiction does tend to do that.<br /> Because you make these personal eruption experiences so juicy, i have to suspect you enjoy doing them. Any advice for others on eruptions? It feels like you could have some useful insights on the event for the rest of us.<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from the private journal of Malu Hekili</u><br /> This is getting harder to read critically, i'm just enjoying the Fracture stuff too much. This is great storytelling, showing no malice on the end of the T2M members, even a level of care that feels suitable for the Novas that willingly enter that service.<br /> Your knowledge of the setting really helps to keep my disbelief suspended, although i'd be misleading you to say i'd be a good judge of that. My preference tends to run to the 2120 Aeon/Trinity stuff, so some of the names you mention may not be ringing the right bells on my end. But the use of deconstruction, characters and setting are all way above average for a fan author and make me wonder how long you have been writing for - or whether you use language in your work.<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume III Issue I</u><br /> The way you approach the science through Sherazahde bears elements of her character, nice. Was it intentional that while Ashnod tends to lecture, i could read Sherazahde all day and never feel talked down to? Subtle work there, if so.<br /> Just a note on words, as an Australian myself, i hear the word 'Aboriginal' used above 'Aborigine' in most written contexts these days - often with 'Australian' prefixed for clarity. If you are interested in the usage of the word from its relevant country. Can you tell it's getting harder for me to find faults in the writing?<br /> Ooh, Sherazahde is talking about pre N-Day eruptions in relation to Dogma. We seem to be seeing her attitude drift Terat-ward in this article, but is she actually convinced that there were rare eruptions prior to the Quantum explosion of 1998 onward? Is this a belief you share as the author, or just further characterization?<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from Time magazine &quot;India comes to America&quot;</u><br /> I have no immediate criticism of this piece, which is an unusual state for me. I suppose i could take issue with the article being a bit on the casual side for Time, but the details are all solid. I hope you take it as a compliment that i actually looked up some of the terms and language you used to fill in some details (i know little about Hawaii), same as i would for a real news article - so despite the casual sound, i still read it the way you intended.<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume III Issue IX</u><br /> What is going on with Sherazahde? The way you write her up from the mundane to the super-human and back is not only lovely, but also a bit more sophisticated than some of your other writing. Is there more of you getting into this character? If not, why do you think she comes across as so relatable? How do you write that on purpose?<br /> I mentioned a couple of these articles were just shy of brilliance, well i believe this one has the right touch to earn that title. There is humour, catastrophe, danger, hope and insight present, all it lacks is a romantic interest and who really cares about <i>that</i> shit?<br /> -smile-<br /> If you want i can look a bit closer for flaws, but i think you kind of knocked it out of the park here. Good work.<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from online article &quot;Is there a method to their madness?&quot;</u><br /> Nice fluff piece for Apep. Apep picture books, as a concept seem to neatly encapsulate the vacant commercialism of the era, at least in symbolism. While this article isn't on the same level as some of the other spectacles you've done, it clearly illustrates a complex young nova both liberated and confined by her own power. In truth, it makes for a great online article - <i>because</i> of the shortfall in comparison to Sherazahde. It's less ambitious and feels somewhat more 'human' for that - with no disrespect intended toward Sherazahde's 'humanity'.<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist Vol III Issue X</u><br /> After the initial splash of fabulous Sherazahde, this was reading like a informercial for the Nova gallery/cafe NewGround, but as you got into the art-philosophy i calmed down and ended up liking the article despite that early misjudgement. Just a touch of force-feeding going on here, but you end up in a good place so i can understand the path you took.<br /> Some of the 'art' you describe is intriguing and i wish i was aware of all the Novas you ascribe them to, since you tend to take a personal approach to the characters you portray, for the most part.<br /> <br /> <u>Excerpt from Psychology Today article</u><br /> Good thinking, good writing and right for the stated source (Psychology Today), but slightly heavy with Meehan's story. He's an interesting character, but it just seems odd that he would receive so much attention in the article, even if it's only an excerpt. Had the article been framed around his particular experience it would have made more contextual sense to focus on Meehan, but this is a minor quibble at best.<br /> I suppose at this point, i'm a bit overwhelmed. Impressed as hell, but steadily becoming useless for critical evaluation. If there is anything you would like more feedback on, point it out and i'll get into the details - but at this point i would need the prompting to continue. Because i enjoyed way too much of these stories to think in terms of critique.<br /> -blush-<br /> ...<br /> So just a few details...<br /> What year is this occuring in? You mention 'decade(s)' of XWF, but it hadn't been running that long in 2008, right? The XWF .pdf i have dates the founding of the promotion to 2004.<br /> How do you read the Null Manifesto? The university lecture and other sources condemn the material, yet the imminently sympathetic Sherazahde seems much less judgemental. I'd like to hear your own point of view.<br /> Did many/any of these characters see play? Do these 1001 Aberrant Nights stories tie in at all to those tabletop stories that aren't preserved as well?<br /> How does your view of these events fit in with the greater three piece setting? Any notion of these characters fates by 2120? Where do you get the notion of pre-N-Day novas from and do they at all figure into the 1920 Adventure! approach?<br /> Was there a unifying over-plot going on here? I got a sense that we might be building toward something related to Nova Rights, then the eruption stories blew me away and i started reading them episodically. Lots of loose threads wagging in the winds, would your future articles have addressed this or continued to leave them loose in true Trinity Universe tradition.<br /> <br /> As a final word, i was really impressed with these short stories, more than i expected to be. You seem to have an admirable talent with words and an entertaining style, Ashnod. I'll definitely chase up the unpublished stuff when you have time, i like what i've seen so far. I haven't read all that much Aberrant fan-fiction, but yours has certainly taken a pole position amongst them - good stuff.<br /> P.S. please forgive any grammatical or spelling errors, if i'm unclear please ask, i will be happy to clarify. But i've already spent too much of the evening getting this far and so this is how it's getting posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T06:37:08-07:00","id":483484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=483376#post483376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u>Ashnod's Declaration</u><br /> XWF, eh? Ok, you set the scene well in a brief camera pan and then launch straight into the commentary team - setting up the Catalysts (loaded name, took me a second pass to read it as a group name), their loose relation to the Teragen (at least in XWF eyes) and pushing the brutality of the arena. I had completely forgotten there were casual nova fatalities, i'd assumed most fatalities were from the mitoids trying to keep up - which wouldn't work here.<br /> While the premise is great, i feel Ashnod's actual declaration runs a little long and may be a little florid for the minds who consume the XWF. Lucky there is some social power-set at play, although i would have preferred you to describe <i>Awe Inspiring</i> rather than simply call it out anime style, because a live crowd might have ignored the material and instead entertained itself with anti-terat chants (or similar) - which might have decreased the impact somewhat.<br /> Otherwise, this is a good hook and i'm interested to see where you go from here. Any particular reason why the XWF drew you in? Seems out of beat a little with the rest of the articles, but not really in a bad way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the one piece I want to revise more than any other. I'm frankly embarrassed by it.<br /> <br /> At its core, it is a basically a retelling of something that happened in a table-top game, but the larger issue is that Ashnod is a much different character than how she is portrayed here. Accurately portraying Ashnod requires me as the author slipping into a very particular mindset, and the brutal truth for me as a writer is that I missed it badly here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume I Issue II</u><br /> Wow, you really have a way with this character. The media savvy way you present the 'zine politics and the pleasant words with which Sherazahde protests the invasion of her personal identity by the editors all conjure the allusion of a person (nova) with opinions and background all her own, unrelated to the few details she drops in the previous article.<br /> The way you have the article still be the meat, but bleed through the character is rather well done. I don't know where the over-plot is going here, but the work here doesn't derail that despite how fabulous Sherazahde is (at least not yet).<br /> Are you playing with sexism on the 'innocent enough' lines? It seems Sherazahde isn't really the precious type - is this clash a product of the magazine content or just meant to be representative of standard concerns for publishers of the time? </div> </div> </div>I'd almost forgotten about this one.<br /> <br /> The <i>innocent enough</i> remark was basically the editor's fear that he (she says they mostly to smokesceen the fact that the boss is pretty much one man) had hired someone who could write, but wasn't involved enough in the nova world to get him the stories he was hoping <i>eXistenZialist</i> could publish. It was of great concern that to his perception his writer may not have had any decent nova networking or nova connections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume I Issue III</u><br /> Well, damn. This is just getting better. You just conjured more setting material for mega physical than 'The New Flesh' does in 200+ pages. It's creepy and provocative, grounded only by the half-drunken commentary. While the perfectionist in me suggests that it lacks something to put it over the edge into true brilliance, i would none-the-less recommend this as excellent setting material for the Amp Room. Better introduction than what we get in the first entry (Ashnod's Declaration) for Machina. So this one deserves praise.<br /> If anything, i would prefer to see a little characterization of Count Orzaiz, just because everyone else seems to get some and your style seems like you could affect a decent Orzaiz. Similarly, i have littleclue who Sin-Eater is after this, but i get the impression this might be intentional. The public fellatio is a bit much, but this is the Amp Room and a bit much <i>is</i> called for, i just might have preferred more suggestion than declaration (did Sherazahde verify for herself that there was mouth to penis contact amidst the mess those two end up in?).<br /> It's kind of strange to see you write in the intended accent - should i assume this is an idiosyncracy of Sherazahde? Or yours? Getting a bit meta, i know... </div> </div> </div>I didn't want to focus on Orzaiz on this one. He was a mechanism to get Machina out of her little seclusion and into the Amp Room. There's obviously a story there, but that's not the story of what Sherazahde saw in the Amp Room that night.<br /> <br /> To the other point about the public sex - she didn't have to verify it. The two novas in question wanted everyone to know that was what they were doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Unaired interview with Dr. Nathaniel Prescott</u><br /> You wrote; 'End Day', i presume you meant N-Day? Just a detail.<br /> My goodness, Ashnod. I was expecting much less than you're delivering here, mysterious secret origin stuff with great characterization of <i>Machina</i> and a spectacular baseline perspective on her eruption. I really like the human duplicity in being mesmerized and frightened (over-awed?)by their employers transformation, the sense they are struggling with their own perceptions - regardless of what their head is telling them.<br /> The year of this event seems curiously missing, as it reads as retrospective. The image of Dr. Ramsey prior to eruption is mostly seen from the eyes of others and leaves some further characterization to be desired on the personal front - although her interview questions address this, she remains too distant to get a feel for.<br /> Because i am a sucker for anything resembling Sci-Fi, the lab setting of this article contributes to it being my favourite so far - only slightly edging out the charming Sherazahde. </div> </div> </div>It's been a while since I wrote it, but I <i>think</i> End Day was a deliberate choice on the part of the narrator. The day that everything normal ended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Unaired lecture/presentation by Alexi Boreanz</u><br /> This one counted a seventeen pages in my Copy/Paste document - so i'm glad you got me hooked in the earlier articles.<br /> There is, therefore, much to be commented upon here. The narrative is US-centric, but with fair reason to be, given the location and speaker. Clever work conflating the Teragen with youth disillusionment, i've always felt the possibility of the Teragen undergoing some kind of 'heel/face turn' as Utopia gains notoriety was inevitable by the end of the war, you feed into that a bit here.<br /> Slightly Jarring to hear Ashnod go from Anthropology to Sixth Sense and back again without providing support like she has with her other arguments. Since everything else in this article has been academic in presentation. That derailed my reading a bit, because 'psychic' can be a loaded term in the greater setting, relating to Psionics and other noetic/telleric weirdness - which is mostly avoided by Aberrant. I'm not sure if i should be thinking about those sources in relation to this, because i don't know how much of it you are using here.<br /> Your descriptions of eruptions really are special, a lovely intersection of the human and post-human, i'd love to see more in that vein. Nice twist at the end, again there is just a little something missing from really putting it over the edge, but an excellent bit of writing.<br /> Purely for the sake of concision, i'd want Ashnod to cut down on the loquaciousness - the narrative gets bogged down by the (intriguing none-the-less) philosophy. But, after her declaration in part one, i'm going to take it as a character trait. Certainly the proper deployment of social powers can easily buy up the attention of an audience for the time she uses - but her powers don't quite reach the reader.<br /> -smile- </div> </div> </div>Again - this is me failing Ashnod's character. Not happy with this piece. It is going to be difficult for me to re-write it, because not only will I have slip back into Ashnod's head, I'm going to have to slip back into her head at this point in her life. When last I was in there, she'd moved beyond this particular phase of just showing up unannounced and doing this kind of thing.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, I'll probably excise it entirely from <i>1,001 Aberrant Nights</i> rather than re-write it. It doesn't fit thematically with what I was intending to do with it. Ashnod needs to be represented in the <i>Aberrant Nights</i> narrative, both because of her connection to Sherazahde and her importance to the changing nature of the setting, but the two pieces that she has featured in were unfortunately written during moments when I, as the author, neither did her the proper justice nor gave greater consideration to how those pieces fit.<br /> <br /> Ashnod deserves better than how she is represented in these stories.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume II Issue XI</u><br /> Wow.<br /> I said i wanted more eruption material and here it is. I have to ask whether this was much work or whether the idea came and the writing afterwards was comparatively easy.<br /> Sherazahde is charming and colourful as usual, Fracture is (as advertised) harrowing. At this point i'm actually not really reading for critical analysis - just enjoying the writing, but i notice that the thread of nova rights isn't really explored here for the first time since the opening article. Maybe i'm reaching for an over-arching link between them all, but fiction does tend to do that.<br /> Because you make these personal eruption experiences so juicy, i have to suspect you enjoy doing them. Any advice for others on eruptions? It feels like you could have some useful insights on the event for the rest of us. </div> </div> </div>In all honesty, I don't really recall Sherazahde speaking too much about nova rights, either thematically or directly. I'll have to look back and verify that.<br /> <br /> As for eruptions: wait until you get to Salamander's eruption. She is a character you haven't met yet except for a cursory mention.<br /> <br /> As for advice: That's difficult, partially because I have a very particular view of them and that view doesn't translate well to everyone else's setting. Eruption, I think, would be a terrifying thing at least initially. It was certainly terrifying for both Sherazahde and Fracture, but for entirely different reasons. A moment exists between the normal and the paranormal, where everything is as you believed it was, and then where everything is radically different in almost every appreciable way, even if it isn't appreciated at that moment. In Fracture's case, she erupted with her Immolate: Spatial Distortion ability (which did aggravated damage) on and disintegrating everything around her that she didn't innately attune to herself. I try to put myself into the head of someone experiencing that moment and wrestle with the thoughts I'd be having.<br /> <br /> Eruptions where the individual's life is in danger and the eruption is a reactionary measure to save someone's life tend to be the norm, both in most canon eruptions and from I understand in most table-top settings, but for some reason it always feels more like a moment of &quot;oh, suddenly I have powers now!&quot; as opposed to the confusion and distress one might otherwise feel. Yes, you suddenly developed density control and you phase through the wall and your car as your car smashed into that wall. But do you know how to control your density abilities? Do you think you are a ghost? Dead, and viewing the scene of the carnage? Do you panic if you cannot immediately become corporeal again, because you don't know how yet?<br /> <br /> Many things to keep in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Excerpt from the private journal of Malu Hekili</u><br /> This is getting harder to read critically, i'm just enjoying the Fracture stuff too much. This is great storytelling, showing no malice on the end of the T2M members, even a level of care that feels suitable for the Novas that willingly enter that service.<br /> Your knowledge of the setting really helps to keep my disbelief suspended, although i'd be misleading you to say i'd be a good judge of that. My preference tends to run to the 2120 Aeon/Trinity stuff, so some of the names you mention may not be ringing the right bells on my end. But the use of deconstruction, characters and setting are all way above average for a fan author and make me wonder how long you have been writing for - or whether you use language in your work. </div> </div> </div>Although the writing on this is entirely mine, I can't lay claim to Malu. She's a character my friend Kelly played in the same game as Fracture (my character) did. I really wish I felt I had more license to play around with Malu and write more of her story because I found what she did with Malu was often surprising. Malu was fundamentally a good person, and this put her at odds with a great many people in the setting. But even a fundamentally good person had their limits, and near the end of the story Malu and Fracture were part of, Malu was willing to stare down Pax, a literal hurricane ready to wreck havoc and destroy the island around them, should he not back down.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume III Issue I </div> </div> </div></u><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way you approach the science through Sherazahde bears elements of her character, nice. Was it intentional that while Ashnod tends to lecture, i could read Sherazahde all day and never feel talked down to? Subtle work there, if so.<br /> Just a note on words, as an Australian myself, i hear the word 'Aboriginal' used above 'Aborigine' in most written contexts these days - often with 'Australian' prefixed for clarity. If you are interested in the usage of the word from its relevant country. Can you tell it's getting harder for me to find faults in the writing?<br /> Ooh, Sherazahde is talking about pre N-Day eruptions in relation to Dogma. We seem to be seeing her attitude drift Terat-ward in this article, but is she actually convinced that there were rare eruptions prior to the Quantum explosion of 1998 onward? Is this a belief you share as the author, or just further characterization? </div> </div> </div>Yeah....pre-N-Day novas. I'll talk to that more in a bit, but, for the sake of full disclosure.<br /> <br /> When this was written, Sherazahde has inside knowledge. She knows at least one of them. She isn't talking to that point, mind you, but it does color her opinions of the material she is writing about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Excerpt from Time magazine &quot;India comes to America&quot;</u><br /> I have no immediate criticism of this piece, which is an unusual state for me. I suppose i could take issue with the article being a bit on the casual side for Time, but the details are all solid. I hope you take it as a compliment that i actually looked up some of the terms and language you used to fill in some details (i know little about Hawaii), same as i would for a real news article - so despite the casual sound, i still read it the way you intended. </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not sure I did Hawaii justice here, but I'm glad it came off as intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist, Volume III Issue IX</u><br /> What is going on with Sherazahde? The way you write her up from the mundane to the super-human and back is not only lovely, but also a bit more sophisticated than some of your other writing. Is there more of you getting into this character? If not, why do you think she comes across as so relatable? How do you write that on purpose?<br /> I mentioned a couple of these articles were just shy of brilliance, well i believe this one has the right touch to earn that title. There is humour, catastrophe, danger, hope and insight present, all it lacks is a romantic interest and who really cares about <i>that</i> shit?<br /> -smile-<br /> If you want i can look a bit closer for flaws, but i think you kind of knocked it out of the park here. Good work. </div> </div> </div>Sherazhade comes across as relatable because she's not above being self-deprecating. She finds it embarrassing to admit to her audience that she was shopping in a large box store, of all places, but she's going to be honest about that fact for the purpose of the story rather than make her nova life seem more glamorous. She over-exaggerated her level of combat prowess in the early columns largely to satisfy the demands of her editor to bring more readers in, but has no trouble fessing up to the fact that it was a fabrication and doesn't mind sharing the embarrassing details. She's not perfect - she got bored and gave up on Hap Ki Do because she was young at the time. She endured some bullying in school, but that story doesn't end with her getting sweet revenge. She had an awkward adolescence, but became an articulate and well-traveled adult.<br /> <br /> There's a lot in there that many readers can relate to.<br /> <br /> You may or may not be surprised that <i>none of that</i> was a conscious decision on my part as her author. My characters are not constructs. Once I have the basic idea of who they are, I just let them take control. Most of the stuff I wrote about Sherazahde I did not know when I first started writing her.<br /> <br /> The two pieces with Ashnod are moments where I tried to force the issue, and they didn't work out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Excerpt from online article &quot;Is there a method to their madness?&quot;</u><br /> Nice fluff piece for Apep. Apep picture books, as a concept seem to neatly encapsulate the vacant commercialism of the era, at least in symbolism. While this article isn't on the same level as some of the other spectacles you've done, it clearly illustrates a complex young nova both liberated and confined by her own power. In truth, it makes for a great online article - <i>because</i> of the shortfall in comparison to Sherazahde. It's less ambitious and feels somewhat more 'human' for that - with no disrespect intended toward Sherazahde's 'humanity'. </div> </div> </div>The whole &quot;novakillers&quot; idea was meant to tackle the disturbing popularity of people like Totentanz and how novas like he, and Apep for that matter, are glamorized. Yeah, it's not a piece written by a serious journalist or researcher. But it's more than just that. The whole trope of the <i>spiritual assassin</i> is something that I have trouble with, and I wanted to deal with the truth that while Apep had a high body count she's obviously not killing other novas for the sake of doing so. The writer in this piece is trying to acknowledge that with what little knowledge of her is actually available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Excerpt from eXistenZialist Vol III Issue X</u><br /> After the initial splash of fabulous Sherazahde, this was reading like a informercial for the Nova gallery/cafe NewGround, but as you got into the art-philosophy i calmed down and ended up liking the article despite that early misjudgement. Just a touch of force-feeding going on here, but you end up in a good place so i can understand the path you took.<br /> Some of the 'art' you describe is intriguing and i wish i was aware of all the Novas you ascribe them to, since you tend to take a personal approach to the characters you portray, for the most part. </div> </div> </div>That's part of her job. <i>eXistenZialist</i> sent her to NewGround to write about it. And the truth of the matter is once she got there, it's basically this exotic nova museum crafted by a mega-intelligent nova. She didn't really know <i>what</i> to write about - museums are about as interesting as a library from a basic description sense. It isn't the Amp Room. But then as she started looking at all the artwork, the whole idea that Meehan was protecting humanity from them struck her. Whether or not that is true is a question for Meehan himself, but she left there with that impression.<br /> <br /> The piece was written by her with that in mind. Okay, I'm here, this is what I'm seeing, tons of artwork, yeah, we get it, wait...oh...OH...OH, I get it....<br /> <br /> It's not something that immediately springs to mind as one walks in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Excerpt from Psychology Today article</u><br /> Good thinking, good writing and right for the stated source (Psychology Today), but slightly heavy with Meehan's story. He's an interesting character, but it just seems odd that he would receive so much attention in the article, even if it's only an excerpt. Had the article been framed around his particular experience it would have made more contextual sense to focus on Meehan, but this is a minor quibble at best.<br /> I suppose at this point, i'm a bit overwhelmed. Impressed as hell, but steadily becoming useless for critical evaluation. If there is anything you would like more feedback on, point it out and i'll get into the details - but at this point i would need the prompting to continue. Because i enjoyed way too much of these stories to think in terms of critique.<br /> -blush- </div> </div> </div>Part of the whole theme of <i>Aberrant Nights</i> was supposed to be that the articles and interviews are supposed to embellish the <i>eXistenZialist</i> articles. In that sense, Meehan's story takes precedence because it is embellishing the NewGround column.<br /> <br /> It's also why the Ashnod piece at the university needs to go. It embellishes nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So just a few details...<br /> What year is this occuring in? </div> </div> </div>Left deliberately vague, unless specific dates are mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You mention 'decade(s)' of XWF, but it hadn't been running that long in 2008, right? The XWF .pdf i have dates the founding of the promotion to 2004. </div> </div> </div>Relic of the tabletop game that story is referencing, and would be changed in the revision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you read the Null Manifesto? The university lecture and other sources condemn the material, yet the imminently sympathetic Sherazahde seems much less judgemental. I'd like to hear your own point of view. </div> </div> </div>There's precious little we actually have on the Null Manifesto, just a few excerpts here and there. Can you be more specific in what you're looking for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did many/any of these characters see play? Do these 1001 Aberrant Nights stories tie in at all to those tabletop stories that aren't preserved as well? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does your view of these events fit in with the greater three piece setting? Any notion of these characters fates by 2120? Where do you get the notion of pre-N-Day novas from and do they at all figure into the 1920 Adventure! approach? </div> </div> </div>There are mentions of pre-N-Day novas in the various source material, so this wasn't something I felt I was forcing upon the setting. I also very much like the idea that certain aspects of our mythology, (Greek, etc,) may have actually been misrepresentations of pre-N-Day novas or stalwarts.<br /> <br /> These characters fates by 2120...yeah, but I'd like to hold off on that for the moment. I will say that I personally do not see these stories really fitting into the much of the Adventure! or Trinity settings. Sherazahde's work, and by extension of that all of the embellishing material, were meant to represent a moment in time between those two eras.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was there a unifying over-plot going on here? I got a sense that we might be building toward something related to Nova Rights, then the eruption stories blew me away and i started reading them episodically. Lots of loose threads wagging in the winds, would your future articles have addressed this or continued to leave them loose in true Trinity Universe tradition. </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I know my little writer's ego pictures Sherazahde's work being dug up or researched in the Trinity-era, something akin to Offred's accounting of what happened in the Republic of Gilead in <i>The Handmaid's Tail</i>. It's a record of what happened during the Aberrant years. Who some of the people were. What they could do. How they were changed and what it meant to be a nova, and not an <i>aberrant</i>.<br /> <br /> But again, that's my ego speaking, and not the truth. The truth is I honestly loved the setting, and I loved writing about different facets of what it mean to suddenly be a superhumanly powered person.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","user":"Ashnod","date":". 04-17-2015, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","name":"Ashnod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T09:54:24-07:00","id":484678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=483484#post483484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the one piece I want to revise more than any other. I'm frankly embarrassed by it.<br /> <br /> At its core, it is a basically a retelling of something that happened in a table-top game, but the larger issue is that Ashnod is a much different character than how she is portrayed here. Accurately portraying Ashnod requires me as the author slipping into a very particular mindset, and the brutal truth for me as a writer is that I missed it badly here.</div> </div> </div> </div>oo, sick burn.<br /> -smile-<br /> I can honestly see why, it's not a horrible piece, but it certainly doesn't do you justice, particularly not as an introduction. I would say, a passing mention of XWF does kind of belong in there with the pop-culture narrative, so don't strip the entire thing out like you plan to do with the university panel discussion scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd almost forgotten about this one.<br /> <br /> The <i>innocent enough</i> remark was basically the editor's fear that he (she says they mostly to smokesceen the fact that the boss is pretty much one man) had hired someone who could write, but wasn't involved enough in the nova world to get him the stories he was hoping <i>eXistenZialist</i> could publish. It was of great concern that to his perception his writer may not have had any decent nova networking or nova connections. </div> </div> </div>Okay, that makes sense. In some ways the shallow business and finance of Aberrant is more important to the setting than the allusions of comic-book power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't want to focus on Orzaiz on this one. He was a mechanism to get Machina out of her little seclusion and into the Amp Room. There's obviously a story there, but that's not the story of what Sherazahde saw in the Amp Room that night. </div> </div> </div>I understand it could have detracted from the focus of the scene, but with all the description of Machina - i felt Orzaiz could have used a spare adjective or adverb himself. He is the least defined of the characters you name in the scene - which means you've relied on the reader's knowledge of Aberrant to inform the imagination. Which is a little beneath your style, in my humble opinion - even the fire belching unknown nova has more characterization.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To the other point about the public sex - she didn't have to verify it. The two novas in question wanted everyone to know that was what they were doing. </div> </div> </div>-chuckle-<br /> That's the truth. Just my own opinion, i prefer uncertainty at times and with the mess of flesh you describe going on; i felt some ambiguity could have worked.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's been a while since I wrote it, but I <i>think</i> End Day was a deliberate choice on the part of the narrator. The day that everything normal ended. </div> </div> </div>Good point, i spotted another such word-substitution in another article and saw it as a personal flair. But i was still getting a feel for your style when i pulled that up - i was going to note any grammar and spelling too but knew immediately that would be too much for this format. Maybe the idea that it was coming from a scientist is what caught me up, it reads completely natural when Sherazahde does it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again - this is me failing Ashnod's character. Not happy with this piece. It is going to be difficult for me to re-write it, because not only will I have slip back into Ashnod's head, I'm going to have to slip back into her head at this point in her life. When last I was in there, she'd moved beyond this particular phase of just showing up unannounced and doing this kind of thing.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, I'll probably excise it entirely from <i>1,001 Aberrant Nights</i> rather than re-write it. It doesn't fit thematically with what I was intending to do with it. Ashnod needs to be represented in the <i>Aberrant Nights</i> narrative, both because of her connection to Sherazahde and her importance to the changing nature of the setting, but the two pieces that she has featured in were unfortunately written during moments when I, as the author, neither did her the proper justice nor gave greater consideration to how those pieces fit.<br /> <br /> Ashnod deserves better than how she is represented in these stories. </div> </div> </div>The longest piece of the series and you're thinking about scrapping it? I can see why, but it seems a pity to lose some of the philosophy there. Maybe try to condense the good bits and move them into Ashnod's Declaration?<br /> With your Avatar and Screen-name paying homage to this character, i feel ripped off that i didn't get to know her in these - i was getting the picture that she was some kind of monologuing villain however, and that didn't mesh with the rest of your genre-savvy work. Could you give us a brief outline of the character? Who is Ashnod if not the character i just read and the Author, who i am now writing to. This is getting meta again...<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In all honesty, I don't really recall Sherazahde speaking too much about nova rights, either thematically or directly. I'll have to look back and verify that. </div> </div> </div>You are correct, it isn't a focus specific to Sherazahde, more specific to you. A strength of yours is in the separation of Human and Nova, when it is alluded to in Sherazahde's articles that strength is evident and i misread it as a focus. But in the beginning i was also looking for an over-plot, which i gather you weren't really concerned with - i should have been reading them episodically (as opposed to serially).<br /> In a way all of your writing is 'thematically' about the differences and similarities between the species - hence my misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for eruptions: wait until you get to Salamander's eruption. She is a character you haven't met yet except for a cursory mention. </div> </div> </div>You tease, this isn't available to read!<br /> But i hope this means you'll give me a peek when you have the time. That would be something to look forward to.<br /> -rubs hands together-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for advice: That's difficult, partially because I have a very particular view of them and that view doesn't translate well to everyone else's setting. Eruption, I think, would be a terrifying thing at least initially. It was certainly terrifying for both Sherazahde and Fracture, but for entirely different reasons. A moment exists between the normal and the paranormal, where everything is as you believed it was, and then where everything is radically different in almost every appreciable way, even if it isn't appreciated at that moment. In Fracture's case, she erupted with her Immolate: Spatial Distortion ability (which did aggravated damage) on and disintegrating everything around her that she didn't innately attune to herself. I try to put myself into the head of someone experiencing that moment and wrestle with the thoughts I'd be having.<br /> <br /> Eruptions where the individual's life is in danger and the eruption is a reactionary measure to save someone's life tend to be the norm, both in most canon eruptions and from I understand in most table-top settings, but for some reason it always feels more like a moment of &quot;oh, suddenly I have powers now!&quot; as opposed to the confusion and distress one might otherwise feel. Yes, you suddenly developed density control and you phase through the wall and your car as your car smashed into that wall. But do you know how to control your density abilities? Do you think you are a ghost? Dead, and viewing the scene of the carnage? Do you panic if you cannot immediately become corporeal again, because you don't know how yet?<br /> <br /> Many things to keep in mind. </div> </div> </div>Bravo. You have a great feel for the cusp of transformation, thanks for the insights. I had a journalist nova of my own (found in the 'nihilist contributions' folder of CHILL's archive) erupt off of a particularly good batch of Acid and proceed to raid London (via mega-social) of its recreational drugs trying to feed a bottomless addiction - the idea of the eruption as epiphany, curse and never-ending curiosity is one i've used (with less applied examination) myself.<br /> I've used violent eruptions for NPCs, but whenever i play myself i prefer to avoid that for some reason - maybe because i can't personally relate to that kind of danger. So that just adds to my appreciation for your approach.<br /> The Eruption as a vibrantly personal and unique experience as you describe it, is something i take pretty seriously. Thanks again and i hope we get to see Salamander's eruption made publicly available at some point if you feel it's even stronger/scarier than Fracture's.<br /> -fingers crossed-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although the writing on this is entirely mine, I can't lay claim to Malu. She's a character my friend Kelly played in the same game as Fracture (my character) did. I really wish I felt I had more license to play around with Malu and write more of her story because I found what she did with Malu was often surprising. Malu was fundamentally a good person, and this put her at odds with a great many people in the setting. But even a fundamentally good person had their limits, and near the end of the story Malu and Fracture were part of, Malu was willing to stare down Pax, a literal hurricane ready to wreck havoc and destroy the island around them, should he not back down. </div> </div> </div>I had assumed a few of these names might have been controlled by other players, maybe an idea of the group and their characters could be useful to understand this. I feel the same when i write stuff for character's that were played, it seems so empty and wrong to feed them lines and actions when you know their soul is absent. Sometimes as a ST/GM/DM/whatever i'm prompted to make calls on where these characters are and what they are doing and it always makes me feel a bit dirty to make decisions for them.<br /> -shrug-<br /> It sounded Malu's story was tilting into aberrant war stuff - but i don't know how you would handle that stuff - because as you said; this is all only lightly connected to the future and past settings (Aeon/Trinity and Adventure! respectively). I also wish this had been included in the posted material more explicitly, because it's great drama and the actual depiction of these events remain nascent in what's available.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah....pre-N-Day novas. I'll talk to that more in a bit, but, for the sake of full disclosure.<br /> <br /> When this was written, Sherazahde has inside knowledge. She knows at least one of them. She isn't talking to that point, mind you, but it does color her opinions of the material she is writing about. </div> </div> </div>Which is why an outline of the actual table-top games could be handy for the overall story context - the missing over-plot i was sniffing for could likely be found there.<br /> I was still debating myself over whether the mechanism of inspiration was unique to the Aeon centuries (1922-2122+), i probably would have eventually leapfrogged it retroactively backwards in time, but i was hoping the PCs would be the agents of that change, not ST fiat.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm honestly not sure I did Hawaii justice here, but I'm glad it came off as intended. </div> </div> </div>In relation to Hawaii, you are the one-eyed leading the blind in this conversation. I had to wiki and source-check a few things you wrote just to be sure it was our Hawaii and not some fictional substitute.<br /> -blush-<br /> But i source-check every news article i read, so in that way it felt just right.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sherazhade comes across as relatable because she's not above being self-deprecating. She finds it embarrassing to admit to her audience that she was shopping in a large box store, of all places, but she's going to be honest about that fact for the purpose of the story rather than make her nova life seem more glamorous. She over-exaggerated her level of combat prowess in the early columns largely to satisfy the demands of her editor to bring more readers in, but has no trouble fessing up to the fact that it was a fabrication and doesn't mind sharing the embarrassing details. She's not perfect - she got bored and gave up on Hap Ki Do because she was young at the time. She endured some bullying in school, but that story doesn't end with her getting sweet revenge. She had an awkward adolescence, but became an articulate and well-traveled adult.<br /> <br /> There's a lot in there that many readers can relate to. </div> </div> </div>I suppose i didn't see that, despite her very specific character traits and opinions, Sherazahde is also an every-woman. I don't know her actual power-set, but not being able to measure up against combat specialized novas is nothing to be ashamed of - i've ran a fairly combat oriented nova campaign before and felt bad for the wonderful characters left out due to their alternate power-sets.<br /> I feel i could learn from the way you wrote the character - because i have a bad habit of writing from the top down instead of the ground up. Sherazahde is very grounded, which makes her an excellent vehicle for the base-line reader.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You may or may not be surprised that <i>none of that</i> was a conscious decision on my part as her author. My characters are not constructs. Once I have the basic idea of who they are, I just let them take control. Most of the stuff I wrote about Sherazahde I did not know when I first started writing her.<br /> <br /> The two pieces with Ashnod are moments where I tried to force the issue, and they didn't work out. </div> </div> </div>Actually, i partially relieved, had you done that on purpose you would be learned in writing skills i have no concept of how to even reach. I've been told i can hit this mark with played NPCs sometimes, but my writing pales in comparison to yours.<br /> -smile-<br /> Can you give us a better idea of how you forced the issue in Ashnod's scenes, i think it's clear now that you say it. But i'd like to know, for the record, what you were forcing towards in her appearances. Was she meant to be sympathetic, intellectual, zealous, superior or wordy? Because those are the adjectives i most easily summon in memory of her part.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole &quot;novakillers&quot; idea was meant to tackle the disturbing popularity of people like Totentanz and how novas like he, and Apep for that matter, are glamorized. Yeah, it's not a piece written by a serious journalist or researcher. But it's more than just that. The whole trope of the <i>spiritual assassin</i> is something that I have trouble with, and I wanted to deal with the truth that while Apep had a high body count she's obviously not killing other novas for the sake of doing so. The writer in this piece is trying to acknowledge that with what little knowledge of her is actually available. </div> </div> </div>The glorification of elites and warriors is definitely worrisome and entirely predictable to begin with, i imagined that by mid-century the opinion will have shifted drastically, but there would still be 'cults' of fans for the worst of the worst.<br /> By 'Spiritual Assassin' i presume you mean a kind of holy warrior, like the Hashashin or even honour-bound ninja or something similar? I think Apep is a wonderful character, but i would appreciate some details on how you were running the 2nd generation Nova. Was she a nova on birth or what? Was her mother even erupted when she had Apep? I did read that right didn't i, Ashnod is Apep's mother? Those two sure hit it lucky if Apep wasn't born into it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's part of her job. <i>eXistenZialist</i> sent her to NewGround to write about it. </div> </div> </div>heh. Okay, i lost sight of Sherazahde's articles being published in a culture (i assume) magazine - i suppose that just adds to the immersion then.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the truth of the matter is once she got there, it's basically this exotic nova museum crafted by a mega-intelligent nova. She didn't really know <i>what</i> to write about - museums are about as interesting as a library from a basic description sense. It isn't the Amp Room. But then as she started looking at all the artwork, the whole idea that Meehan was protecting humanity from them struck her. Whether or not that is true is a question for Meehan himself, but she left there with that impression.<br /> <br /> The piece was written by her with that in mind. Okay, I'm here, this is what I'm seeing, tons of artwork, yeah, we get it, wait...oh...OH...OH, I get it....<br /> <br /> It's not something that immediately springs to mind as one walks in. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, all that part i liked - good journalistic instinct there. Might have made for a frustrating read by the base-line readership, but i believe Sherazahde mentions that in either this article or the Amp-Room one.<br /> The concept of a nova protecting the communal human psyche from nova expression is delectable, something i've played with myself at times. In a way it might be a kind of 'Prime Directive' for responsible novas, treating the nova creativity the same as one might treat advanced technology - which in a memetic and cultural way; art is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Part of the whole theme of <i>Aberrant Nights</i> was supposed to be that the articles and interviews are supposed to embellish the <i>eXistenZialist</i> articles. In that sense, Meehan's story takes precedence because it is embellishing the NewGround column. </div> </div> </div>I appreciate this, i only thought it could have been more naturally situated in an article about Down Syndrome specifically, but i conceed i was scraping the bottom of the barrel for critique by then. You had left me rather speechless at the end there.<br /> -smile-<br /> Of course, 1,001 Aberrant Nights is a kind of companion to the game it sprang from as well - so i'd even advise working in some more elements of what was occurring in the games as another common link where possible. Episodic is fine, but elements of the articles imply serialization and then fail to deliver much in that vein. I understand this is probably also a symptom of being unfinished - but i thought i'd mention it.<br /> <br /> <br /> In relation to setting year:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Left deliberately vague, unless specific dates are mentioned.<br /> <br /> Relic of the tabletop game that story is referencing, and would be changed in the revision. </div> </div> </div>So, for a frame of reference what year was this occurring in when originally played, out of curiosity?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's precious little we actually have on the Null Manifesto, just a few excerpts here and there. Can you be more specific in what you're looking for? </div> </div> </div>Sure, i was wondering whether you saw the call for novas to discover their own society/culture/laws separate (or perhaps even above) from that of humanity as a worthy pursuit, or one which is an act of warmongering. I know it isn't that simple, but those are two extremes which seem to get rolled out by the usual suspects. Different characters you write seem to see it differently, but if i had to guess i would assume you fell on the 'worthy pursuit' end of the spectrum - i just didn't want to assume when i have your ear.<br /> It's not really all that important, just thought it could add some insight as to where you are writing from.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes. </div> </div> </div>Quoting that without context is a bit vapid of me, but if you could give us some details of that campaign, it might go toward tying the articles together stronger and adding some context and texture.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are mentions of pre-N-Day novas in the various source material, so this wasn't something I felt I was forcing upon the setting. I also very much like the idea that certain aspects of our mythology, (Greek, etc,) may have actually been misrepresentations of pre-N-Day novas or stalwarts. </div> </div> </div>I read the pre-N-Day novas as stalwarts of the earlier Hammersmith era (Adventure!), i never went in for the whole ancient nova temptation because i had the notion that the Hammersmith/N-Day/Venezuela effects were all self contained and didn't propogate so far through the dimension of time - but i had plans that could have gotten me to where you started.<br /> Still, the difference in head-canon makes little difference and the only mentions are cloaked in uncertainty and opinion which helpfully allows me to read it without questioning the base assumptions. If i'm reading it right, i think the OPP team are going for some 'ancient' setting material in this edition - so you may be validated yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These characters fates by 2120...yeah, but I'd like to hold off on that for the moment. I will say that I personally do not see these stories really fitting into the much of the Adventure! or Trinity settings. Sherazahde's work, and by extension of that all of the embellishing material, were meant to represent a moment in time between those two eras. </div> </div> </div>Glad to have cleared that up, allows me to focus on the writing and not get too hung up on setting material and meta-plot. So this is all at some unstated point between 2008 and 2120? It makes me wonder if you were still moving toward an Aberrant War in your vision, or whether the Aeoon society had any real presence there? Just because i'm a fan-boy for this stuff.<br /> -blush-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know. I know my little writer's ego pictures Sherazahde's work being dug up or researched in the Trinity-era, something akin to Offred's accounting of what happened in the Republic of Gilead in <i>The Handmaid's Tail</i>. It's a record of what happened during the Aberrant years. Who some of the people were. What they could do. How they were changed and what it meant to be a nova, and not an <i>aberrant</i>.<br /> <br /> But again, that's my ego speaking, and not the truth. The truth is I honestly loved the setting, and I loved writing about different facets of what it mean to suddenly be a superhumanly powered person.<br /> </div> </div> </div>That is interesting, i have played with using aberrant setting material in my 2120s games as recovered/restricted data from before the data crash and subsequent seizure of resources by Aeon. Mostly i used dramatic and impersonal pieces, but the effect of such media infecting the carefully pruned memetic zeitgeist of the future era could be much more critical. If you're interested, a war correspondence article in the style of Sherazahde could go a long way to reconciling your articles with the less relatable types i sometimes let free in the future. That human-like touch would go a long way when refuting the monstrous aspect of those novas.<br /> I would assume writing by a nova as charismatic as Sherazahde might have been amongst the records the trinity would order destroyed due to the chance of 'Almost Live' style quantum effects. But the way i played it, Aberrant sympathizers on Mars and in the Belt would have passed the data around like a virus in a controlled habitat (eww).<br /> Your love for the setting really comes through and if you still feel it, i would certainly like to read anything else you produced in these veins going forward. You have a noteworthy talent for it and i'd encourage you to feel proud of what you've done. Even if it's hard as a writer to look back on it, there is some good stuff in there and i feel like the time i spent on it wasn't wasted in the least.<br /> I would ask after your influences. I wonder if you have any particular super-power comics/stories that inform your take on the setting (i couldn't ignore the casual 'fastball special' reference)? I'd also like to know how familiar you are with the other two settings in the series, just out of curiousity and to inform any future reading of your work.<br /> <br /> If anyone more knowledgable than i in the Aberrant setting has anything to add, please feel free to jump in - i'm not so sure of myself when in comes to this era. <a href=\"http://www.dark-kingdom.org/Aberrant/abtoc.html\" target=\"_blank\">Here is the link again, just for convenience</a>.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the replies Ashnod, these were a great read and i hope to see your name pop up on the forums when you have opinions to share. You certainly seem to have a solid grasp of the mood and theme of the Aberrant era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Added link. 04-18-2015, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T14:05:52-07:00","id":484845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=484678#post484678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> oo, sick burn.<br /> -smile-<br /> I can honestly see why, it's not a horrible piece, but it certainly doesn't do you justice, particularly not as an introduction. I would say, a passing mention of XWF does kind of belong in there with the pop-culture narrative, so don't strip the entire thing out like you plan to do with the university panel discussion scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this piece can't be stripped out. <i>Ashnod's Declaration</i> was, pardon the in-game pun, a catalyzing event for Sherazahde. Until that time, she was content to live a fairly anonymous life without reaping any of the benefits of novahood. She felt no need to speak out or about the events that was happening.<br /> <br /> That story, however, is unlikely to be told within the context of <i>Aberrant Nights</i>, as it is more the personal story between Ashnod and Sherazahde themselves. I've written up some of that, but of it is still in my head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, that makes sense. In some ways the shallow business and finance of Aberrant is more important to the setting than the allusions of comic-book power. </div> </div> </div>And comic-book power is, in my opinion, the <i>least</i> interesting aspect of Aberrant. The psychological and sociological aspects are more important in almost every way. These are things that every now and then get the briefest of elaborations within X-Men, but then Marvel will pull a House of M and destroy everything they built up in an effort to satisfy the demands of their readership.<br /> <br /> The <i>What would you do with the power of god</i><i>?</i> question is interesting, but to me, <i>How would having the power of a god change you?</i> is more interesting one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand it could have detracted from the focus of the scene, but with all the description of Machina - i felt Orzaiz could have used a spare adjective or adverb himself. He is the least defined of the characters you name in the scene - which means you've relied on the reader's knowledge of Aberrant to inform the imagination. Which is a little beneath your style, in my humble opinion - even the fire belching unknown nova has more characterization. </div> </div> </div>And this is true, but in Sherazahde's opinion, <i>everyone </i>reading her columns knows who Orzaiz is as much as they know who Pax is. She didn't feel the need to speak about in a column that was largely about aberration, especially when by all visible accounts Orzaiz is not aberrated.<br /> <br /> But your point is good one. I shall consider if some embellishment is necessary in that section of the story. If nothing else, a contrast between the highly-inhuman Machina and the highly-human Orzaiz.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The longest piece of the series and you're thinking about scrapping it? I can see why, but it seems a pity to lose some of the philosophy there. Maybe try to condense the good bits and move them into Ashnod's Declaration? </div> </div> </div>The initial thought was this was meant to introduce the Fracture / Malu arc of the story.<br /> <br /> Boreanaz speaks about Fracture, that leads into Sherazahde's account of Fracture's eruption, that leads into Malu's journal related to her involvement with Fracture's time with Utopia, which leads into the Sherazahde column about divinity and the article about India Syndrome as they both relate to Malu, etc.<br /> <br /> I'll consider a revision instead of an outright scrap, if you feel there is something there worth salvaging. Reading it now, it feels like I'm a swimmer who got a decent launch off the block, slow start once in the water, sprinted well through the water for a little bit, then lost all energy and inertia and floundered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With your Avatar and Screen-name paying homage to this character, i feel ripped off that i didn't get to know her in these - i was getting the picture that she was some kind of monologuing villain however, and that didn't mesh with the rest of your genre-savvy work. Could you give us a brief outline of the character? Who is Ashnod if not the character i just read and the Author, who i am now writing to. This is getting meta again... </div> </div> </div>UGH. Monologuing villain? Terrible failure on my part, then.<br /> <br /> I'm probably too close to the character to speak to her objectively. The very real problem I'm going to have in addressing who Ashnod is as a person is that there is no &quot;one&quot; version of her that I can point to. She was originally a table-top character of mine that, after a very very long table-top life, eventually found her way into an online game. That presented a great many difficulties, as the specifics of that table-top game <i>did not translate well at all</i> into an online medium where the canon world had to be preserved as much as possible in order for all players to have a common reference.<br /> <br /> That necessitated me revising a great deal of Ashnod's history into a more canon-friendly version, but this was something I did over time instead of immediately upon entering the new medium. However, over time and given the freedom to develop her within a primarily-text based medium where I had almost complete control over her instead of relying on storyteller input and machination, she became something else again.<br /> <br /> By the time I had a firm grasp on who the character of Ashnod was in my mind, the two pieces she appears in within <i>Aberrant Nights</i> had already been made publicly available. <i>Ashnod's Declaration</i> was a relic of the table-top era, and the university speech was a relic of the mid-way era after she was introduced to the online game but before I had fully nailed down who she was outside of the influence of her original setting.<br /> <br /> So, to a sense, I was forcing the issue when writing her. In the first, I was writing to my storyteller's setting within the confines of what was allowed, and the second, without fully appreciating who she was supposed to be.<br /> <br /> The truth on the monologuing aspect though...that's unfortunately part of who she is as a <i>mega-intelligent</i> nova. She uses very long sentences, over-explains, and has no internal editor when it comes to speaking aloud. It's not supposed to be <i>monologuing</i> in a super-villain sense, and if she's coming off that way, I need to seriously reconsider what happens when I slip into her head and let her take control.<br /> <br /> To sum Ashnod as briefly as I can without side-tracking this more than I already have: she was at one point a fairly influential member of the Teragen who felt very strongly about that fact that novakind needed to separate itself from baseline humanity for the benefit of both species. She didn't think co-existence was going to be possible until both species came to fundamentally accept that they were very different, but that being different didn't automatically mean being opposed to each other. After both species were separated sufficiently, she felt reintegration and co-existence would be more feasible. Then she met Elizabeth (Wizard), and everything changed. She eventually started wondering why on earth she was caring so fiercely about novakind when novakind seemed determined to not to care about itself. This is somewhat of the position Mal found himself in; but unlike Mal and would eventually become the Night of Long Knives within the Teragen, Ashnod began to feel apathetic about the Teragen. Essentially, &quot;Why am I trying so hard to show them that they are butterflies, when it is becoming painfully obvious to me that they <i>know</i> they are butterflies but are choosing to live as caterpillars?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are correct, it isn't a focus specific to Sherazahde, more specific to you. A strength of yours is in the separation of Human and Nova, when it is alluded to in Sherazahde's articles that strength is evident and i misread it as a focus. But in the beginning i was also looking for an over-plot, which i gather you weren't really concerned with - i should have been reading them episodically (as opposed to serially).<br /> In a way all of your writing is 'thematically' about the differences and similarities between the species - hence my misunderstanding. </div> </div> </div>And part of the allusion, as you note, is Sherazahde's transition towards something more in line with Ashnod's way of thinking. One of the tragedies, so to speak, of the Aberrant War is that many novas were forced to align with factions they might otherwise have despised merely for survival. Sherazahde, for better or for worse, is a woman who eventually felt that siding with the Teragen or those of sympathetic bent to the Teragen was inevitable. Not because she had feelings of nova-superiority, but because she knew baseline humanity was going to force her to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Eruption as a vibrantly personal and unique experience as you describe it, is something i take pretty seriously. Thanks again and i hope we get to see Salamander's eruption made publicly available at some point if you feel it's even stronger/scarier than Fracture's.<br /> -fingers crossed- </div> </div> </div>I don't feel it's stronger or scarier than Fracture's (though you might disagree), I feel it's noteworthy. Salamander is a self-erupted nova - someone who deliberately put her life in danger in order to try and erupt and was willing to risk death in order to become a nova.<br /> <br /> That kind of determination, fortitude, and perhaps even insanity, is something I find striking. And being a very young nova, Salamander thinks that makes her superior to every nova out there who are, in her very loud opinion, nothing more than <i>quantum accidents</i>. And some truth exists to her line of thinking on this. Is someone who <i>expects </i>to erupt, has prepared for it, is ready for the transition from latent nova to active nova, inherently better prepared for life as a nova post-eruption?<br /> <br /> It's an intriguing question. Salamander certainly thinks this is the case, especially when she interacts with novas who whine about how much harder life is as an erupted being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It sounded Malu's story was tilting into aberrant war stuff - but i don't know how you would handle that stuff - because as you said; this is all only lightly connected to the future and past settings (Aeon/Trinity and Adventure! respectively). I also wish this had been included in the posted material more explicitly, because it's great drama and the actual depiction of these events remain nascent in what's available. </div> </div> </div>As far as the timeline stuff, the whole incident with Fracture's eruption happened, IIRC, while Jennifer &quot;Slider&quot; Landers was still alive. The Aberrant War was quite a ways off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is why an outline of the actual table-top games could be handy for the overall story context - the missing over-plot i was sniffing for could likely be found there.<br /> I was still debating myself over whether the mechanism of inspiration was unique to the Aeon centuries (1922-2122+), i probably would have eventually leapfrogged it retroactively backwards in time, but i was hoping the PCs would be the agents of that change, not ST fiat. </div> </div> </div>There isn't <i>one</i> table-top game.<br /> <br /> Ashnod, Apep, and Sherazahde are based upon table-top characters in one game.<br /> Fracture, Malu, Lucious Clay, and Savannah &quot;Aurifex&quot; O'Shea came from another.<br /> Salamander was entirely online creation.<br /> James Meehan was a creation of a friend, and I have no idea if he ever had a table-top version or if he was strictly online.<br /> Elizabeth was a creation of another friend, who had both a table-top version and an online version, but IIRC the player tried to keep these competing events coherent in a single character.<br /> <br /> The world of <i>Aberrant Nights</i> is a composite of many sources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you give us a better idea of how you forced the issue in Ashnod's scenes, i think it's clear now that you say it. But i'd like to know, for the record, what you were forcing towards in her appearances. Was she meant to be sympathetic, intellectual, zealous, superior or wordy? Because those are the adjectives i most easily summon in memory of her part. </div> </div> </div>I think I might have already covered this, but -<br /> <br /> Intellectual, superior, and wordy sound accurate. Sympathetic, maybe. Ashnod is someone that believed that novas, on the whole, were a superior animal to baselines. Let me allow her to speak for herself on this topic:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;If I may, teleporters do <i>not</i> cross borders. While it may seem like teleportation operates in a linear fashion, it does not. When you relocate, you are not traveling in a direct line between your destination and point of origin. This operates differently per the individual, from merging locations in an immeasurable span of time, to shifting your spatial perception along an axis in which you don't move at all but instead the world adjusts to your shift. To cross a border, one must physically move over it, whether on foot, vehicle, or flight. You can make a solid argument for certain transmitters; Novas such as V here for whom travel through electrical networks might qualify as crossing a border depending on their medium. But not for teleporters or for warpers. To put this into another light, if I were to move this entire room right now to Luna we would leave what is considered the <i>boundaries</i> of Earth and enter the <i>boundaries</i> of Luna, but we would not be crossing the vacuum of space to get there.<br /> <br /> &quot;However, the issue I believe Preston is addressing is entry into a country illegally. While most baseline law does not address the issue of teleportation as a means of illegal entry, these laws will nominally define an illegal alien as one who is in the country without first legally being admitted at a defined checkpoint. Most baseline law as it is written cannot hold a teleporter guilty of crossing a border even if the act is in some way similar, but it can hold them guilty of being in the country illegally. A subtle, yet significant, difference.<br /> <br /> &quot;I do not expect most of you to understand this. Some of you will. Manipulating the fabric of space, whether teleporting, or warping, or another of the abilities I have demonstrated, is not just something I can do. It is part of what I <i>am</i>. I am not weaving poetry when I say this, even if it sounds poetic. As those who speak with plants understand them innately, so too is my relationship with size and distance. Distance and surface and space call out to me, sing to me if I may be so bold. I am aware, always, of the space between locations, objects, the positioning of items in a rooms, even cities. When I visited Chicago and spent my one complete week dormed down, all of that disappeared and left me clumsy and blind. This was not a matter of simply being unable to do something. Part of me was effectively stripped away. Should I compare this to having the artistic part of Prodigy's mind shut down, or the linguistic side of Ms. McLachlan's?<br /> <br /> &quot;These so called borders mean <b><i>nothing</i></b> to me. Imaginary lines, and nothing more, drawn up to divide up this planet like property. I recognize, for the sake of convenience, that the 547,030 square kilometers around the 105 square kilometers of the city whose inhabits call Paris is in turn called France, which is in turn part of a 4.97 million square kilometer spatial area which is recognized by the the majority of the planet as Europe, which is again in turn part of a larger spatial area of 485.83 million square kilometers sometimes called Eurasia. Do the concepts of Paris, France, Europe, and Eurasia extend beyond the labels assigned them? Not to one such as I.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am a resident of this <b><i>planet</i></b>, for the present time, not of any one nation. You ask me acknowledge that these tiny governments, whom have the audacity to proclaim that they are my not only my peers but my superiors, can limit my movement? Can you understand the insult, and the humiliation such an act requires?<br /> <br /> &quot;However, if that is too abstract, let me return to the realm of philosophy once more. I could, if I chose, argue that I cannot be considered an illegal alien as I am not a baseline and these laws were not written with anything other than baselines in mind. That the Zurich Accord says otherwise is meaningless. That any hastily added revisions to these laws to include novas are inapplicable, the same as if they were written to include sentient extra-terrestrial life.<br /> <br /> &quot;But more importantly, as we have established, these laws are part of a social contract. When Preston says that &quot;being able to evade most forms of baseline law doesn't make you immune, you're still breaking the law,&quot; he is neglecting the point that a law exists for the people to whom the social contract applies. In the case of border law, to protect the citizens who have accepted the social contract. I have no social contract with a baseline government. I do not ask for the protection of their military or their law enforcement, and to be fair, I truly do not <i>need</i> it, either. These governments will find it exceedingly difficult to enforce any such law upon me, and recognizing that, do little to stop me.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am going to address the issue of where Novas such as I go if we refuse to live in baseline society in a moment, but for now...given that I hold no official citizenships, that I do not recognize any baseline governments as holding any authority over me by social contract or for philosophical reasons, that I consider myself more than capable of defending myself against any threat of the non-erupted type hence needing no baseline protection, that I hardly expect them to be able to deal with any erupted threat that concerns me and in fact if they attempted to deal with something capable of threatening me it would probably be a death sentence, and as the threat of retribution by baseline authority gives me no motivation whatsoever to sacrifice or even limit part of what I am for the silly little lines they have drawn upon the globe, please try and persuade me why I should consider obeying these laws? Not because it is illegal in their eyes to disobey, or because it is the simply the way of the world. Why should I consider obeying these border laws? How does it benefit me, and what incentive do I have to do so?<br /> <br /> &quot;Must I reduce this to saying I teleport myself onto the Andes mountains simply to enjoy the view, and then ask you all to tell me why this border violation should concern me? That the desire to see the mountains at sunset overcame me, and I chose to see them right then and there. Why should I stop at a checkpoint at the border to get a passport stamped, knowing full well I will be leaving in exactly twenty-seven minutes when the sun has set? And then must I return to that checkpoint again, simply to get the passport stamped that I have left? What can be accomplished in two exertions has been expanded to four, for nothing more than a twenty-seven minute view of the sun setting in the Andes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Must I <i>also</i> get a passport stamped in the nation I am leaving at the beginning of this jaunt? Now it becomes six exertions: one to my nation's checkpoint, the next to the destination's checkpoint, a third to the mountains, a fourth back to the destination checkpoint, a fifth back to my nation's checkpoint, and a sixth to wherever I go from there.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dr. Smith has pointed out one exceedingly obvious matter to everyone, that any nova with harmful intent will not bother teleporting to a checkpoint. Forcing me to obey these absurd restrictions will not lessen the amount of crime or acts-of-war that would occur as a result of teleporation. So, let us try discussing this one more time, without heaping on the fear of death and destruction to the example. Why should I, without harmful intent, care about a restriction that those with harmful intent will circumvent altogether? Why should I care about this border law? What incentive do I have to honor it?&quot; </i><br /> <br /> And, referencing her week dormed down:<br /> <br /> <i>So you got me to do it, Preston. I <i>dormed down</i> for you, for a <i>week</i>.<br /> <br /> As the active quantum slowed like molasses to my node, then freezing in place as sap spilling from a tree, it was done.<br /> <br /> And I was blind.<br /> <br /> My temporal and spatial senses vanished, leaving me staggeringly blind. Years of having intimate knowledge of the passing of fractions of microseconds, of having complete and immediate understanding of the forms and distances of my surroundings changed so thoroughly the way I perceived the world even in passing, that the loss of those senses could only be compared to losing one's eyesight on the spot. Of having the very orbs cut from your sockets at the optic nerve and then left to find your way in the world without them.<br /> <br /> Sitting down, I found it necessary to collect my bearings, to attempt regaining cohesion and clarity. I watched time pass on the clock of my OpNet terminal, feeling the absence of time washing over me, longing to have it caress me as I had become accustomed to, as those moronic white digital seconds turned to minutes and then to an hour.<br /> <br /> As though the angels themselves had sung to me for years and suddenly silenced themselves.<br /> <br /> For some time now my very body has lit up the room or area I occupied, but that Sunday night I found myself laying in darkness. Not that I required (or so I thought then) sleep, some things even dorming cannot take from you, but that night I desired it. Lusted for it. Perhaps sleep would ease the pain I felt from losing my quantum senses I haven't even described the totality of it, merely touching upon the temporal and mentioning the spatial. The others I possesses, the sum of their loss...I might as well have lost limbs to be so crippled.<br /> <br /> And I lay there thinking <b><i>This is what <u><b>they</b></u> equate themselves with. This base state with no possibility of touching the cosmic glory beyond it. This simple form limited by every law of science known. This CAGE.</i></b><br /> <br /> My own philosophy made real. My node screamed at me to awaken it, to open the dam of energy I had willed into place and reclaim that which I purposely subdued. But no, no, I wouldn't be defeated so easily.<br /> <br /> Surely, after a few days to acclimate myself to this condition, I would not consider it such a burden. This thought seemed to make sense at the time. But underneath that thought was the truth, the truth that after you are so <i>awake</i>, you cannot go back. You cannot touch the cosmic and suddenly believe that it would be good to live without it.<br /> <br /> Except in comic books written by baseline writers, whose moral seems to be that being human is all we should aspire to. That anything else is either blasphemy or destined to end in madness or death. That humanity is the divinest state one can hope to achieve while living. Stories that glorify the human condition written by people who've never experienced anything beyond it.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By 'Spiritual Assassin' i presume you mean a kind of holy warrior, like the Hashashin or even honour-bound ninja or something similar? </div> </div> </div>No, I mean someone more like Thane Krios from the <i>Mass Effect</i> franchise. Someone who kills people for a living, but oh look, he's so spiritual and philosophical about what he does, and he has a code of honor that governs him, etc...I dislike this trope immensely, and I view the novakillers thing as baseline audiences assigning traits to novas who don't deserve them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Apep is a wonderful character, but i would appreciate some details on how you were running the 2nd generation Nova. Was she a nova on birth or what? Was her mother even erupted when she had Apep? I did read that right didn't i, Ashnod is Apep's mother? Those two sure hit it lucky if Apep wasn't born into it. </div> </div> </div>Yeah...that's going to difficult to explain. Apep is Ashnod's daughter, yes. That story is something better taken offline, as it's going to make no appreciable amount of sense here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, for a frame of reference what year was this occurring in when originally played, out of curiosity? </div> </div> </div>As I said, there's no <i>one</i> setting. It's a composite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, i was wondering whether you saw the call for novas to discover their own society/culture/laws separate (or perhaps even above) from that of humanity as a worthy pursuit, or one which is an act of warmongering. I know it isn't that simple, but those are two extremes which seem to get rolled out by the usual suspects. Different characters you write seem to see it differently, but if i had to guess i would assume you fell on the 'worthy pursuit' end of the spectrum - i just didn't want to assume when i have your ear.<br /> It's not really all that important, just thought it could add some insight as to where you are writing from. </div> </div> </div>On the mostly worthy pursuit, yes. More to the point, I disagree with the Zurich Accord, and I'd disagree even more so were I erupted.<br /> <br /> Violette &quot;V&quot; D'Aronique, a Utopian nova mentioned briefly, has a speech she gave on this after being released from Project Utopia. That's one of the unreleased parts of <i>Aberrant Nights</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Glad to have cleared that up, allows me to focus on the writing and not get too hung up on setting material and meta-plot. So this is all at some unstated point between 2008 and 2120? It makes me wonder if you were still moving toward an Aberrant War in your vision, or whether the Aeoon society had any real presence there? Just because i'm a fan-boy for this stuff. </div> </div> </div>The AEON Society had a big presence yes, and leaning more on the Proteus/dark Mercer future version of it.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Aberrant War was looming in the future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks for the replies Ashnod, these were a great read and i hope to see your name pop up on the forums when you have opinions to share. You certainly seem to have a solid grasp of the mood and theme of the Aberrant era. </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Brain is mush now. Will tackle more later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","user":"Ashnod","date":". 04-18-2015, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","name":"Ashnod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T17:48:35-07:00","id":484950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=484845#post484845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, this piece can't be stripped out. <i>Ashnod's Declaration</i> was, pardon the in-game pun, a catalyzing event for Sherazahde. Until that time, she was content to live a fairly anonymous life without reaping any of the benefits of novahood. She felt no need to speak out or about the events that was happening.<br /> <br /> That story, however, is unlikely to be told within the context of <i>Aberrant Nights</i>, as it is more the personal story between Ashnod and Sherazahde themselves. I've written up some of that, but of it is still in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad for that, the strong start of the Declaration article carrying into the second article built a feeling of connectivity that the whole would be weaker without. I feel silly to have lead with the cultural reference when there's actually a plot point in there too.<br /> -facepalm-<br /> I'm kind of frustrated to hear you have other writing that is set out of reach of my grubby little fingers (still in your head, no less), i can't speak for everyone, but i'd love to get a look at some more of your work on the subject.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And comic-book power is, in my opinion, the <i>least</i> interesting aspect of Aberrant. The psychological and sociological aspects are more important in almost every way. These are things that every now and then get the briefest of elaborations within X-Men, but then Marvel will pull a House of M and destroy everything they built up in an effort to satisfy the demands of their readership.<br /> <br /> The <i>What would you do with the power of god</i><i>?</i> question is interesting, but to me, <i>How would having the power of a god change you?</i> is more interesting one. </div> </div> </div>I'd say comic book powers are the least interesting part of <i>comics</i>, unless some nice sci-fi is involved (personal preference only). Although those powers are an important element of Nova character creation and thus loom large in the player's mind. I kind of drew away from the mainstream comic companies in the early nineties, i only check in for major events now - hence why i know House of M - Civil War also had an interesting notion going in, but also reset to default afterwards.<br /> I suppose there are reasons they do that beyond the questionable judgements of editorial mandate. mythological pantheons like DC and, to a slightly lesser extent, Marvel - really require an endgame going in, a handover point where the earth is given back to humans (or at least whatever is left of it, if anything). Alan Moore came up with something for DC in that regard, the X-men have Days of Future Past, Norse myth has Ragnarok, Aberrant has the war and Chinese Ultimatuum, etc... These days i prefer the deconstructions and reconstructions, but i never quite got back to my pre-pubescent excitement for super-powered stories.<br /> Enough about comics from me, but I'd still be interested to hear your comic influences when your poor brain recovers.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And this is true, but in Sherazahde's opinion, <i>everyone </i>reading her columns knows who Orzaiz is as much as they know who Pax is. She didn't feel the need to speak about in a column that was largely about aberration, especially when by all visible accounts Orzaiz is not aberrated.<br /> <br /> But your point is good one. I shall consider if some embellishment is necessary in that section of the story. If nothing else, a contrast between the highly-inhuman Machina and the highly-human Orzaiz. </div> </div> </div>Even when i'm right, i'm wrong.<br /> -tease-<br /> If i offer <i>nothing</i> else in our discussion, i can point to this and claim i was helping.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The initial thought was this was meant to introduce the Fracture / Malu arc of the story.<br /> <br /> Boreanaz speaks about Fracture, that leads into Sherazahde's account of Fracture's eruption, that leads into Malu's journal related to her involvement with Fracture's time with Utopia, which leads into the Sherazahde column about divinity and the article about India Syndrome as they both relate to Malu, etc. </div> </div> </div>Excellent point, i'll have to re-read it to see the whole structure a bit clearer (i looked too hard for connecting plots and missed the connecting themes), but i generally need a while before my memory isn't forcing me to skip large chunks of a re-read. Your self-awareness is astounding, you must have put quite a bit of good thought into these, or a tiny amount of sheer brilliance (your pick).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll consider a revision instead of an outright scrap, if you feel there is something there worth salvaging. Reading it now, it feels like I'm a swimmer who got a decent launch off the block, slow start once in the water, sprinted well through the water for a little bit, then lost all energy and inertia and floundered. </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent metaphor, there is some strong stuff that just kind of peters out by the end. I will have to look over it to give specifics, but i think the only egregious fault is having Ashnod talk so long without examination - the questions section should make up the lion's share of the scene in my humble opinion. Ashnod can still say a whole heap in this setting, she is probably much smarter than the majority of the audience, but the academics asking questions should be trying to tear her down the whole way - with good points of their own, sometimes even on her side. Ashnod might be objectively better than humans, but give our species a worthy voice in this conversation too.<br /> I know this is a little low-brow, chopping up a whole point into more accessible topics, but i feel it could create a greater atmosphere of academic inquiry and controversy. I've seen speakers stand against a whole floor of academics before and hold their own, it wouldn't be too hard for Ashnod to do this - the biggest challenge to her would probably be boredom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> UGH. Monologuing villain? Terrible failure on my part, then. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps villain is a bit colourful, i don't like to think there are any 'monologuing villains' in the setting (although their top layer may seem guilty, looking at Divis Mal), perhaps 'idealist' is the better fit. But, i stand by 'monologuing'.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The truth on the monologuing aspect though...that's unfortunately part of who she is as a <i>mega-intelligent</i> nova. She uses very long sentences, over-explains, and has no internal editor when it comes to speaking aloud. It's not supposed to be <i>monologuing</i> in a super-villain sense, and if she's coming off that way, I need to seriously reconsider what happens when I slip into her head and let her take control. </div> </div> </div>Apologies, i tend to over-use the word villain, if it helps that's because i see villainy and heroism in all good characters - antagonist and protagonists are decided by the party/players and are functionally still the same characters from behind the screen (motivations, background and opinions need only be tweaked).<br /> Your examples above really address that misconception - i think it must have been an issue with the uncertain characterization as i couldn't always tell if she was on the level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To sum Ashnod as briefly as I can without side-tracking this more than I already have: she was at one point a fairly influential member of the Teragen who felt very strongly about that fact that novakind needed to separate itself from baseline humanity for the benefit of both species. She didn't think co-existence was going to be possible until both species came to fundamentally accept that they were very different, but that being different didn't automatically mean being opposed to each other. After both species were separated sufficiently, she felt reintegration and co-existence would be more feasible. Then she met Elizabeth (Wizard), and everything changed. She eventually started wondering why on earth she was caring so fiercely about novakind when novakind seemed determined to not to care about itself. This is somewhat of the position Mal found himself in; but unlike Mal and would eventually become the Night of Long Knives within the Teragen, Ashnod began to feel apathetic about the Teragen. Essentially, &quot;Why am I trying so hard to show them that they are butterflies, when it is becoming painfully obvious to me that they <i>know</i> they are butterflies but are choosing to live as caterpillars?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Damn, now i wish you had this Ashnod be more evident in the writing. Sherazahde is charming, but Ashnod sounds fascinating (in a morbid sense). The combination of the two would have made for a load of fun, pity you never got around to finishing that part. I'd love to hear your take on the Divis Mal character (preferably in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/103062-divis-mal-what-s-his-deal\">Divis Mal thread</a>), since it seems Ashnod takes up that spiritual mantle left behind by pre-night-of-knives Mal. A role that absolutely calls for filling, and so far i'm impressed with Ashnod's fit.<br /> Why did everything change when she met Wizard? Is there some old forum where parts of this are preserved, so i can look it up myself rather than bother you with the details? Ian Watson, lead developer, has posted links to outside forums previously - so it isn't against the rules as far as i know.<br /> Would you say Ashnod is loosely a Jim-Crow-like separatist when it comes to inter-species relations? I imagine she would give me an earful for relating her to humans, but apart from the prospect of re-integration, i'm (maybe ignorantly) not sure how it differs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And part of the allusion, as you note, is Sherazahde's transition towards something more in line with Ashnod's way of thinking. One of the tragedies, so to speak, of the Aberrant War is that many novas were forced to align with factions they might otherwise have despised merely for survival. Sherazahde, for better or for worse, is a woman who eventually felt that siding with the Teragen or those of sympathetic bent to the Teragen was inevitable. Not because she had feelings of nova-superiority, but because she knew baseline humanity was going to force her to. </div> </div> </div>Glad i wasn't imagining it. One of the tragedies? I'd say the whole war is a tapestry of tragedies, it's one of the ways i disagree with the Aberrant setting, that put both Proteus and eventually Divis Mal out of range for any sympathy. -shrug-<br /> I'm glad to hear someone else thinks this way. I've always been of the firm belief that increasingly decent and reasonable novas will swell the ranks of the Teragen (or a like-minded group, under an evolved philosophy similar to Ashnods) by the war years, even if still vilified by the other major factions for their own reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't feel it's stronger or scarier than Fracture's (though you might disagree), I feel it's noteworthy. Salamander is a self-erupted nova - someone who deliberately put her life in danger in order to try and erupt and was willing to risk death in order to become a nova.<br /> <br /> That kind of determination, fortitude, and perhaps even insanity, is something I find striking. And being a very young nova, Salamander thinks that makes her superior to every nova out there who are, in her very loud opinion, nothing more than <i>quantum accidents</i>. And some truth exists to her line of thinking on this. Is someone who <i>expects </i>to erupt, has prepared for it, is ready for the transition from latent nova to active nova, inherently better prepared for life as a nova post-eruption?<br /> <br /> It's an intriguing question. Salamander certainly thinks this is the case, especially when she interacts with novas who whine about how much harder life is as an erupted being. </div> </div> </div><br /> Reading some of your replies, i believe i've identified another of your writing talents! Self promotion.<br /> -tease-<br /> The introductions you give for the things you've wrote have all made me want to read what you were talking about - with no other frame of reference for this character (except the knowledge that your character writing is strong), i now want to read about her. I think i could learn a lot by watching how you do this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as the timeline stuff, the whole incident with Fracture's eruption happened, IIRC, while Jennifer &quot;Slider&quot; Landers was still alive. The Aberrant War was quite a ways off. </div> </div> </div>Okay, that helps inform me of the atmosphere surrounding Utopia/Proteus at the time - smart people were definitely picking the thread up by then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There isn't <i>one</i> table-top game.<br /> <br /> Ashnod, Apep, and Sherazahde are based upon table-top characters in one game.<br /> Fracture, Malu, Lucious Clay, and Savannah &quot;Aurifex&quot; O'Shea came from another.<br /> Salamander was entirely online creation.<br /> James Meehan was a creation of a friend, and I have no idea if he ever had a table-top version or if he was strictly online.<br /> Elizabeth was a creation of another friend, who had both a table-top version and an online version, but IIRC the player tried to keep these competing events coherent in a single character.<br /> <br /> The world of <i>Aberrant Nights</i> is a composite of many sources. </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess i should have considered this, but hindsight is 20/20. Multiple games and formats - how very modern of you. It's only a matter of time for me at this stage...<br /> Thanks for the cheat-sheet. So you played Fracture, but who did you play first time, Ashnod? Meaning Sherazahde is someone else's character? You write the hell out of Sherazahde, what's the difference between her and Malu, that you write one but prefer not to write the other?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I might have already covered this, but -<br /> <br /> Intellectual, superior, and wordy sound accurate. Sympathetic, maybe. Ashnod is someone that believed that novas, on the whole, were a superior animal to baselines. </div> </div> </div>Sympathetic was really a cop-out way of saying 'factually correct', or perhaps 'frustratingly logical' - both of which i find (weirdly) sympathetic. I am philosophically entrenched in the idea that novas must be allowed to develop on their own, on their own terms - which may also have contributed.<br /> From a human perspective she is a scary individual - mostly because of her ideas and the fear of where they would leave humanity. But who cares about <i>that</i> shit? I found Mal sympathetic in the same way, but that character burns up in a bizarre twist to the meta-plot of the series. Again, i'd like to see where you fall on the Lustral-Star interpretation in the Divis Mal thread (post #5, first page), but no rush there, just curious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let me allow her to speak for herself on this topic:<br /> [...] </div> </div> </div>Sheeeit, Ashnod (referencing both character and poster)! Where was that voice in 1,001 Aberrant Nights? I can see why you think those pieces were failures, this Ashnod is much more concise and visceral. &quot;...This CAGE.&quot; is a terrific line that coats poison onto the sharp point the rest of her dormancy spiel establishes, excellent stuff. I can clearly see why you need to be in 'the zone' to write this stuff - there is a kind of passion to it that mustn't come easy.<br /> I really hope you took this from somewhere else instead of writing it up on the spot, no wonder your brain is mush, if so - and surprised if it isn't violently haemorrhaging . You should probably attend a physician if it is.<br /> -smile-<br /> Seriously, more great material. I appreciate the insight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, I mean someone more like Thane Krios from the <i>Mass Effect</i> franchise. Someone who kills people for a living, but oh look, he's so spiritual and philosophical about what he does, and he has a code of honor that governs him, etc...I dislike this trope immensely, and I view the novakillers thing as baseline audiences assigning traits to novas who don't deserve them. </div> </div> </div>Okay, does this extend to all protagonist killers? Or is it the ones who take the effort to justify themselves in this manner? i would guess the latter because of the 'spiritual' qualifier, but this is kind of splitting hairs too - a characteristic of many story tropes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah...that's going to difficult to explain. Apep is Ashnod's daughter, yes. That story is something better taken offline, as it's going to make no appreciable amount of sense here. </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds familiar. I also have characters who need to come with disclaimers, it's an unavoidable part of trying to reconcile the three settings on my part. I'll inquire after <i>your</i> excuse when it next confounds me.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the mostly worthy pursuit, yes. More to the point, I disagree with the Zurich Accord, and I'd disagree even more so were I erupted. </div> </div> </div>I think your excerpts of Ashnod above kind of make this crystal clear, no one on the other side of this argument is ever comparably close to her level of passion and logic in your writing. I'll leverage this to mention that this requires some balancing element, because Ashnod being right all the time is like Superman always winning: lacking in drama.<br /> Might sound harsh, but if you have a good character (like Ashnod) then this is a minor detail in the greater scope - after all, you only have to occasionally out-manoeuvre yourself believably to do this, although this is admittedly tough work in itself with mega-mental characters. Actually scratch the minor detail comment, that might require some thinking too.<br /> I don't know, what do you think? You have the better handle on the character and her limitations than i.<br /> As a side note, one day i hope to draw you out about the Null Manifesto, because i think you have one of the clearest understandings i've ever read of it's purported contents.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Violette &quot;V&quot; D'Aronique, a Utopian nova mentioned briefly, has a speech she gave on this after being released from Project Utopia. That's one of the unreleased parts of <i>Aberrant Nights</i>. </div> </div> </div>Remember what i said about your introductions?<br /> Stop teasing me with stuff i can't read.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The AEON Society had a big presence yes, and leaning more on the Proteus/dark Mercer future version of it.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Aberrant War was looming in the future.<br /> <br /> Thank you. Brain is mush now. Will tackle more later. </div> </div> </div><br /> Dark Mercer was my leaning too, apparently OPP have a new interpretation from what i've gathered. Interested to see what's planned for the mysterious Max Mercer and his society in general.<br /> Sorry for piling up the plate again, but you're bringing up some tasty good points. Just ignore this post and finish your tackle of the last if it's too much. If this goes on much longer i may have to start another thread in the vein of the one i did questioning CHILL, anyway.<br /> -points and nods forebodingly at Ashnod-<br /> Thanks heaps for the energy you've put in here - i hope i'm not eating away at time better spent elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Fixed a broken quote box and found a mis-worded statement. 04-18-2015, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T19:46:47-07:00","id":485025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=484950#post484950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm glad for that, the strong start of the Declaration article carrying into the second article built a feeling of connectivity that the whole would be weaker without. I feel silly to have lead with the cultural reference when there's actually a plot point in there too. I'm kind of frustrated to hear you have other writing that is set out of reach of my grubby little fingers (still in your head, no less), i can't speak for everyone, but i'd love to get a look at some more of your work on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't feel frustrated. That story is only partially written. I'm not keeping anything complete from you on that end.<br /> <br /> Ashnod and Sherazahde have a complicated history and complicated friendship. And that story isn't one that is meant for <i>Aberrant Nights</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ashnod might be objectively better than humans, but give our species a worthy voice in this conversation too. </div> </div> </div>That's the problem with being a nova with significant mega-socials who has <i>chrysalized. </i>If her mega-socials weren't enough to cow any worthy baseline voices, the eerie effect of her chrysalized taint magnifies this. Even if someone unerupted wanted to engage with her, they would likely find themselves unable to.<br /> <br /> But for Ashnod the goal isn't demonstrating that novakind is objectively better, it's getting novakind to recognize they aren't just baselines with <i>kewl powers</i>. That one can be sentient, intelligent, complex, and humane without being <i>human</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why did everything change when she met Wizard? </div> </div> </div>I can't lay claim to Wizard, but the simple explanation is that Wizard and Ashnod had a passionate romance. But that description sells their relationship short. If you have two temporal novas, both of whom can view the <i>possible</i> and not just the <i>probable</i>, their connection has the potential to reach beyond the immediate moment.<br /> <br /> It's difficult to describe what that did to Ashnod. She once described Wizard as someone who lived <i>within</i> the possible instead of merely one who observes it.<br /> <br /> Wizard was, for better or for worse, unconcerned with any nova who insisted on thinking of themselves as a human with kewl powers. Either they would come around or they would not, but she didn't feel it was her obligation to help them come around. Ashnod felt very differently when she initially met Wizard - she very much felt she had an obligation to do this.<br /> <br /> After some time, Ashnod began to understand Wizard's perspective on this. Not outright agree with it, but understand it. Why was she helping the Teragen, when half of the Teragen was squabbling for power within itself? Why was she arguing with novas who steadfastly defended the Zurich Accord in the face of their own experience?<br /> <br /> This is partially the dilemma of ascending to Quantum 6 and greater. Ashnod and Wizard were two beings who could touch the cosmic - and after a while it becomes more and more difficult to keep in mind that all those novas with Quantum 1 or 2 are on a much different strata of self-awareness and enlightenment. The things Ashnod has come to know are as alien to them as their experiences at being Q1 or Q2 are to baselines. This is a strata that Ashnod has never known. She entered the world of novas with both Temporal and Spatial manipulation (Quantum 5 abilities) when she was twenty years old - she has never known anything but power on a (for the era) very high scale. After pushing past Q5 into Q6, this gap just becomes wider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there some old forum where parts of this are preserved, so i can look it up myself rather than bother you with the details? Ian Watson, lead developer, has posted links to outside forums previously - so it isn't against the rules as far as i know. </div> </div> </div>I <i>think </i>so. I'll do some digging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you say Ashnod is loosely a Jim-Crow-like separatist when it comes to inter-species relations? I imagine she would give me an earful for relating her to humans, but apart from the prospect of re-integration, i'm (maybe ignorantly) not sure how it differs. </div> </div> </div>She's very much <i>not</i> Jim Crow-like. The only reason she's advocates separation is so that novakind stops thinking of itself as enhanced baselines and that baselines can stop being dependent upon novas to fix their messes. She doesn't think they are separate but equal, to borrow the phrase.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The introductions you give for the things you've wrote have all made me want to read what you were talking about - with no other frame of reference for this character (except the knowledge that your character writing is strong), i now want to read about her. I think i could learn a lot by watching how you do this. </div> </div> </div>Here's a bigger tease, then. Except from the Salamander piece:<br /> <br /> <i>I was taken to a local hospital while the authorities called in Utopia team to come visit me. In my hospital bed, between moments of accidentally setting things on fire without meaning to, I stared at my wrist. I had a little hospital bracelet fastened there. On it was the word novus. The nurse who put it on my arm told me they had purchased those bracelets years ago but I was the first to ever wear one. This stupid little meaningless, but tangible, acknowledgement that I was a nova meant the world to me right then. Physical proof that it had happened. The proof separating me as one who <b>was</b> from those who will <b>never</b> be.<br /> <br /> While I was there, I reflected back on the french nova Amelie Mauresmo. She erupted in 2007 while playing in the finals of the French Open, her home tournament and the one thing she wanted to win more than anything else in her career. While trying desperately to save match point, and stay alive in the match, she erupted and her physical qualities shot instantly into superhuman levels. She somehow got her racquet on the ball and hit an impossible winner, something absolutely impossible for a normal tennis player to do, and won the point. In that moment, with her life not in danger, she had become of those who are. But she cited it, for the longest time, as the worst thing that ever happened to her. She knew, at that moment, she'd never play competitive tennis again. She'd never be<b> allowed</b> to play competitive tennis again. She knew what had happened to her, and in the spirit of fair play, conceded the match rather than have to forfeit it at a referee's ruling.<br /> <br /> In the last two years, I've come to know that she wasn't upset at <b>becoming</b>, rather just mourning the loss of her tennis career, which had been her entire life up until that point. She's since made a happy life for herself with her quantum expression. Back then, in the hospital, I wasn't mature enough to understand that. I had just erupted, after all, and I was full of myself and my accomplishment.<br /> <br /> <b>What a fucking quantum accident</b>, I thought of her while looking at my novus hospital band. Whatever people would think about me, it didn't matter. My legs were already starting to heal. My anima was there illuminating the room. The nurses and hospital staff kept looking at me with wide, fascinated eyes. I could hear the halls filled with conversation about me and what had happened to me. How <b>jealous</b> they were of me, and how they wished they had been lucky enough to be one of <b>them</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>I was.</b></i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess i should have considered this, but hindsight is 20/20. Multiple games and formats - how very modern of you. It's only a matter of time for me at this stage...<br /> Thanks for the cheat-sheet. So you played Fracture, but who did you play first time, Ashnod? Meaning Sherazahde is someone else's character? You write the hell out of Sherazahde, what's the difference between her and Malu, that you write one but prefer not to write the other? </div> </div> </div>The very first nova character I played was Machina.<br /> The second was Ashnod.<br /> Sherazahde is mine, but she was like the 3rd or 4th nova character I played. I already knew her history, mind you, due to Ashnod's story, but I didn't actually play her as a character until much later.<br /> Fracture came after Sherazahde.<br /> <br /> Malu wasn't mine, though. Same with Apep. Both were characters of a friend. I feel awkward writing for either because they aren't mine I do not know them as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a human perspective she is a scary individual - mostly because of her ideas and the fear of where they would leave humanity. But who cares about <i>that</i> shit? I found Mal sympathetic in the same way, but that character burns up in a bizarre twist to the meta-plot of the series. </div> </div> </div>And she is supposed to be intimidating. As she was once quoted as saying, &quot;<i>It is not our fault if you are terrified of what we represent. We make no apologies for what we are.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, i'd like to see where you fall on the Lustral-Star interpretation in the Divis Mal thread (post #5, first page), but no rush there, just curious. </div> </div> </div>I'll look in on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sheeeit, Ashnod (referencing both character and poster)! Where was that voice in 1,001 Aberrant Nights? I can see why you think those pieces were failures, this Ashnod is much more concise and visceral. &quot;...This CAGE.&quot; is a terrific line that coats poison onto the sharp point the rest of her dormancy spiel establishes, excellent stuff. I can clearly see why you need to be in 'the zone' to write this stuff - there is a kind of passion to it that mustn't come easy.<br /> I really hope you took this from somewhere else instead of writing it up on the spot, no wonder your brain is mush, if so - and surprised if it isn't violently haemorrhaging . You should probably attend a physician if it is. Seriously, more great material. I appreciate the insight. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that was a copy pasta. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But reading over it...I could probably adapt much of that for <i>Aberrant Nights</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, does this extend to all protagonist killers? Or is it the ones who take the effort to justify themselves in this manner? i would guess the latter because of the 'spiritual' qualifier, but this is kind of splitting hairs too - a characteristic of many story tropes. </div> </div> </div>Not sure what you're asking here. Clarification?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think your excerpts of Ashnod above kind of make this crystal clear, no one on the other side of this argument is ever comparably close to her level of passion and logic in your writing. I'll leverage this to mention that this requires some balancing element, because Ashnod being right all the time is like Superman always winning: lacking in drama. </div> </div> </div>I'm not certain this a fault of Ashnod always being correct as much as it the setting for putting Utopia/AEON in the position that they were going to be more wrong than Mal or the Teragen. In the end, it doesn't matter how benevolent many of the people working within T2M or Utopia itself were: the organization was fully under the thumb of something corrupt that was doing terrible things, and the Zurich Accord represents the authority to do it.<br /> <br /> It's also very difficult for me to conceive of something similar to the Zurich Accord that would be less problematic. When you have one species that by their very nature alters the phenomena of the world, can control minds, be nigh-impervious to conventional weaponry, and literally fix the problems of the previous centuries in a handful of years; calling them the equals of baseline humanity is insulting. For someone like Ashnod, it very much was. She has no reason whatsoever to consider baseline humanity her peer. And while that doesn't mean she dislikes them, or would be antagonistic towards them, trying to pull her down legally and philosophically to their level just so they can feel comfortable with sharing the planet with her species is not on the table.<br /> <br /> Trying to combat her in a debate, on paper at least, is going to end up sounding like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PatrickStewartSpeech\" target=\"_blank\">a Patrick Stewart Speech</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a side note, one day i hope to draw you out about the Null Manifesto, because i think you have one of the clearest understandings i've ever read of it's purported contents. </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember what i said about your introductions?<br /> Stop teasing me with stuff i can't read. </div> </div> </div> Then I shall tease you again. (Working on getting this stuff online, promise) Excerpt from Violette's speech:<br /> <br /> <i>The first is whether or not I agree with the Null Manifesto, at least as far as novas being outside of baseline law. I'm of a mixed mind on this point. Yes, I do believe that novas should govern themselves, and I do believe if nothing else there should be a body of representation for novas if a full government isn't possible. I don't believe the &quot;every nova is a nation unto him or herself&quot; rhetoric, and I believe that if a nova decides to live within baseline society then he or she is responsible to obey the laws of the nation they call home.<br /> <br /> That generally leads to the next question, which is why I feel I can\u2019t simply live with the way things are. This is where the matter becomes significantly more complex. You see, as an American nova, I have a democratic view of the way government should be run. But my ideas aren\u2019t necessarily applicable to other nations because of the way their governments are arranged. Short of a complete restructuring and revision of the government to include equal representation by both species, which I\u2019d prefer, smaller changes could be enacted.<br /> <br /> Currently, I\u2019m not represented in the United States government. There are representatives for the state I live in, of course, but these are unerupted individuals who probably don\u2019t have the potential to erupt. There are novas in elected office, yes, but these novas, like my former teammates, believe that nova and baseline are the same. The legislation and decisions made by these elected officials are meant to govern baselines, and novas that live with the belief that they are just normal people who happen to have eyebeams.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I\u2019m concerned that one day legislation will pass that limits or affects the behavior of novas and I don\u2019t want this to be created solely by those who will never erupt, and those who continue to believe that they aren\u2019t different from the unerupted. While I\u2019m certain many of you will think me racist for saying this, I want you to keep in mind that we had a law passed in Florida that made it a crime for a nova to be within the city limits, prompting a quick and brutal response by the Teragen. Now, however ugly and illegal this law was, it was <b>passed</b> and it was <b>enforced</b>, and the organizations that performed the enforcing were my former employer and the local jurisdictions of the nation in which I live.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","user":"Ashnod","date":". 04-19-2015, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","name":"Ashnod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T23:51:26-07:00","id":485187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=485025#post485025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't feel frustrated. That story is only partially written. I'm not keeping anything complete from you on that end.<br /> <br /> Ashnod and Sherazahde have a complicated history and complicated friendship. And that story isn't one that is meant for <i>Aberrant Nights</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, the prospect of cosmic Ashnod being questioned on her stances by a young, earthy Sherazahde would have made for <i>spectacular</i> dialogue is all. Something to hope for in the future perhaps... Is it intimidating as a writer to approach something like that, the juxtoposition of two established characters?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the problem with being a nova with significant mega-socials who has <i>chrysalized. </i>If her mega-socials weren't enough to cow any worthy baseline voices, the eerie effect of her chrysalized taint magnifies this. Even if someone unerupted wanted to engage with her, they would likely find themselves unable to. </div> </div> </div>I was about to mention the material about overwhelming baselines with mega-social and there being ways to downplay the mega-social to avoid that. But, then i remembered that she was there to speak to an unerupted professor/speaker - she isn't there for discussion with humans in the first place. Rendering my suggestion moot.<br /> I hope you see where i'm coming from though - Ashnod's philosophies deserve an intellectual foil, if only for the sake of drama. A card carrying Utopian PR nova, if the human speaker isn't relevant/possible. Hell, use Divis Mal too - i feel you could probably approximate the character better than most and NPCs are there to be used. I'm sure we'll tell you if we think you are doing it wrong.<br /> -smile-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But for Ashnod the goal isn't demonstrating that novakind is objectively better, it's getting novakind to recognize they aren't just baselines with <i>kewl powers</i>. That one can be sentient, intelligent, complex, and humane without being <i>human</i>. </div> </div> </div>You're right, i'm just concerned that her dialogue is going completely unopposed in the narrative, if you were to attack her from an appropriately hostile opposing POV then it would help cement her as sympathetic to the reader - i know it's irrelevant to Ashnod, but to avoid the 'monologuing villain' approximation further; it could be a useful device.<br /> I'd be interested to know why that isn't the right mechanism - i may be over simplifying and maybe should, instead of replying, take another long look at 1,001 Aberrant Nights instead to seam up any more misunderstandings. But you're making it hard to not reply, with all the good content you're posting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't lay claim to Wizard, but the simple explanation is that Wizard and Ashnod had a passionate romance. But that description sells their relationship short. If you have two temporal novas, both of whom can view the <i>possible</i> and not just the <i>probable</i>, their connection has the potential to reach beyond the immediate moment.<br /> <br /> It's difficult to describe what that did to Ashnod. She once described Wizard as someone who lived <i>within</i> the possible instead of merely one who observes it.<br /> <br /> Wizard was, for better or for worse, unconcerned with any nova who insisted on thinking of themselves as a human with kewl powers. Either they would come around or they would not, but she didn't feel it was her obligation to help them come around. Ashnod felt very differently when she initially met Wizard - she very much felt she had an obligation to do this.<br /> <br /> After some time, Ashnod began to understand Wizard's perspective on this. Not outright agree with it, but understand it. Why was she helping the Teragen, when half of the Teragen was squabbling for power within itself? Why was she arguing with novas who steadfastly defended the Zurich Accord in the face of their own experience?<br /> <br /> This is partially the dilemma of ascending to Quantum 6 and greater. Ashnod and Wizard were two beings who could touch the cosmic - and after a while it becomes more and more difficult to keep in mind that all those novas with Quantum 1 or 2 are on a much different strata of self-awareness and enlightenment. The things Ashnod has come to know are as alien to them as their experiences at being Q1 or Q2 are to baselines. This is a strata that Ashnod has never known. She entered the world of novas with both Temporal and Spatial manipulation (Quantum 5 abilities) when she was twenty years old - she has never known anything but power on a (for the era) very high scale. After pushing past Q5 into Q6, this gap just becomes wider. </div> </div> </div>That not only makes sense, it's also a nice bit of character evolution. In your mind, how long is Ashnod trying to push the boulder uphill before this relationship visits her with paradigm shift? Months? Years? Decades? Just for a sense of how long the public aspect of Ashnod bounces around for. I understand that time is mixed up the way you played her - but you clearly have a notion of character progression there.<br /> Those higher quantum levels are seriously alienating for those possessing them - i only ever had one PC who breached that level by taking on taint and i folded the whole operation soon after due to balance issues. I never really explored non-combat specialized novas in that power level, especially not clear-headed and taint-free novas in their native setting of this level.<br /> Honestly some of the powers you've dropped for Ashnod would have made me very intimidated to write or play the character - mega-mental, primal-force senses and folding space - not to mention the temporal dimension. How on earth do you approach a mental monster like that? What is she like around her own kind, when she gets comfortable/relaxed? If she ever even gets that way...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I <i>think </i>so. I'll do some digging. </div> </div> </div>Thanks. But don't put any more effort into it than you want - i don't want to take up any more of your time than you would willingly part with. A forum name would suffice, i can run my own searches in your stead - to give you some of your time back.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She's very much <i>not</i> Jim Crow-like. The only reason she's advocates separation is so that novakind stops thinking of itself as enhanced baselines and that baselines can stop being dependent upon novas to fix their messes. She doesn't think they are separate but equal, to borrow the phrase. </div> </div> </div>I was secretly hoping you would disagree, but i'm still unclear as to the actual differences. The anti-miscegenation laws probably wouldn't have been focussed on at the start - because nova population is a fraction of a fraction of the human demographic. But the segregation of two societies occupying the same land can only look so many different ways - i am indeed suffering from a anthrocentric POV, but if i can't imagine something than i would have a damn hard time running it in game.<br /> Care to take a swing at how this would actually work? Or was it always intended as a pot of gold at the end of the rainbow in relations to Ashnod, never to be too deeply examined? Like Darkseids anti-life equation or something?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here's a bigger tease, then. Except from the Salamander piece:<br /> [...] </div> </div> </div>I'm running out of superlatives for you... Magnifico, i guess.<br /> -smile-<br /> That last paragraph is enough to give me goosebumps - you are right, this character's eruption has an entirely different approach than i had expected. Still in an incomplete state so i won't take to it with the hatchet, but it still makes for great food-for-thought.<br /> Can i assume this is prior to any final editing? Because i'm kind of interested to see the difference between the work as it is now and the edited work in the future, just to see if i can pick up any pointers in the process. The changes you make could be informative - it could be worthwhile for me to look at that in the interest of learning how you characterize these different actors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The very first nova character I played was Machina.<br /> The second was Ashnod.<br /> Sherazahde is mine, but she was like the 3rd or 4th nova character I played. I already knew her history, mind you, due to Ashnod's story, but I didn't actually play her as a character until much later.<br /> Fracture came after Sherazahde.<br /> <br /> Malu wasn't mine, though. Same with Apep. Both were characters of a friend. I feel awkward writing for either because they aren't mine I do not know them as well. </div> </div> </div>I apologize, you may need to tolerate a few more misunderstandings on my part before i get this all straight - in a way i suppose the complexity of the characters owe a little something to the complexity of their play history. I've never personally had a character that lasted longer than a single campaign - but i've been ST/GM/DM/whatever the majority of times we've played - so characters are a little interchangable for me. Give me a stat-block and i'm good to go.<br /> I've seen characters go from one campaign to the next a few times, but as far as i'm aware, i was those character's sole ST/GM/DM/whatever - they never played outside of a limited circle. I have no frame of reference of how a character might be forced to evolve when jumping between games like you describe.<br /> -shrug-<br /> I can entirely sympathize with writing for other player characters, also a call i hate to make. Even if i can approximate the player's portrayal, it still feels hollow to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And she is supposed to be intimidating. As she was once quoted as saying, &quot;<i>It is not our fault if you are terrified of what we represent. We make no apologies for what we are.&quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>I have no doubts she is meant to be intimidating, but since she is just a fictional construct to me, i can appreciate more nuanced aspects of her character. Trust me, i could be forced into the dreadful arms of Proteus if something like that was stalking about talking about a poorly defined (from my reading so far) segregated society where all the humans are on one side and all the quantum-powered gods on the other.<br /> I don't trust human legislators to speak plainly, how could i possibly trust self-interested superhumans to do so? I really don't see the aberrant war as any kind of stretch - if anything it was noble for them to hold off until 2049.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll look in on that. </div> </div> </div>Nice, interested to see if you have any input - like i said, your peculiar insight into the matter seems relevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, that was a copy pasta. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But reading over it...I could probably adapt much of that for <i>Aberrant Nights</i>. </div> </div> </div>Relieved to hear that.<br /> -smile-<br /> Again i would counsel breaking it into a dialogue, but you know what you're doing - i just can't help myself. I sometimes think i would question Shakespeare if he gave me a draft.<br /> -blush-<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure what you're asking here. Clarification? </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> So there is the unrepentant, grim-dark, mercenary type who just kills and makes no excuses - maybe even wallowing in gallows humour or bad-taste. Then you have the 'noble' killers, the Thane Krios', the Ezio Auditore da Firenzes, who in killing their prey have accomplished some philosophical or spiritual feat in their own paradigms - essentially alleviating them of any relevant guilt for murder.<br /> The first type doesn't care they are murderers, the second type might dispute that point with dogma and traditions that do nothing to undo their actions, but can serve as an excuse for both themselves and anyone with the appropriate inclination to believe them.<br /> I hope it makes sense this time, but if it's still unclear i'll link to the actual tropes involved - if i can find what i'm thinking of.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not certain this a fault of Ashnod always being correct as much as it the setting for putting Utopia/AEON in the position that they were going to be more wrong than Mal or the Teragen. In the end, it doesn't matter how benevolent many of the people working within T2M or Utopia itself were: the organization was fully under the thumb of something corrupt that doing terrible things, and the Zurich Accord represents the authority to do it.<br /> <br /> It's also very difficult for me to conceive of something similar to the Zurich Accord that would be less problematic. When you have one species that by their very nature alters the phenomena of the world, can control minds, be nigh-impervious to conventional weaponry, and literally fix the problems of the previous centuries in a handful of years; calling them the equals of baseline humanity is insulting. For someone like Ashnod, it very much was. She has no reason whatsoever to consider baseline humanity her peer. And while that doesn't mean she dislikes them, or would be antagonistic towards them, trying to pull her down legally and philosophically to their level just so they can feel comfortable with sharing the planet with her species is not on the table.<br /> <br /> Trying to combat her in a debate, on paper at least, is going to end up sounding like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PatrickStewartSpeech\" target=\"_blank\">a Patrick Stewart Speech</a>. </div> </div> </div>Yes, i mentioned before my issues with Proteus/Utopia being so wrong that i can't really stand up for them effectively - while in 2120 i can defend/lambast virtually anyone i see fit to and there is very little to prevent me from running it either way.<br /> The poor Zurich Accord is doomed to fail, but it's a great piece of setting drama - could you really say those responsible were motivated by envy or oppression? I would think it was done with the best of intentions, but with the limitations of human insight and short time in which to develop it. Perhaps a co-developed accord between the species could hit a sweeter note, but still it would be steeped in compromise on both sides. We all still have to share Earth and it simply may not be big enough.<br /> The Space Brigade ran Luna's Olympus colony for years, but there were humans up there too. They went to Mars before the war, and humans were right behind them, travelling on ships developed by paid Novas. All the while calling for the novas to dumb down their potential and be 'less scary'.<br /> Sorry, got on a space tangent there for a second. Nice reference at the end, there is no beating these kind of novas in a philosophical/moral debate - they just drop a sound bite that renders all your opinions invalid. But, dramatically that makes for a lack-lustre climax. Perhaps my suggestion above to debate with Mal instead or another nova might work - although by canon, Mal is <i>the</i> uber-quantum wielder and may be able to 'Patrick Stewart' (as a verb) Ashnod herself.<br /> Again, this takes the drama out of the discussion - but, i'm beating a dead horse here, aren't i? If you aren't going to do it, you probably have an excuse i'm not even seeing somehow. There are a lot of ideas competing in my head right now, thanks to your insight. Please forgive me if i stopped making sense at some point in this post...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thank you. </div> </div> </div>I mean that, if i was the one at the helm of the new edition, i'd be asking you to submit a draft for the thing. You are that convincing to me. So again, i'd like it if anyone who knows Aberrant better than i can point any weaknesses i'm not seeing here. Maybe i'll see them myself in my next reread or something, but for now i'd be really interested in how you would do a 'Null Manifesto'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then I shall tease you again. (Working on getting this stuff online, promise) Excerpt from Violette's speech:<br /> [...] </div> </div> </div>&quot;<i>Yes, let's all tease the Nihilist! Dangle desirable things in front of him to reach for, only to draw back when he gets close - this will be terribly good fun!</i>&quot;<br /> I swear, if there is some kind of secret agreement between you and Ian to wind me up for entertainment value...<br /> -grumble-<br /> This is frankly quite engrossing, i take a social approach to the Aberrant period - not as deeply as you, but close enough to be inspired by much of your examination of it. More on the details you are brushing on above would potentially be a captivating read - but i suppose it takes a great deal of thinking to run through the possibilities. The last major global deviation we took from democratic capitalism was the tragic fall of Marxist Communism into Stalinism into whatever the hell China is doing now. So coming up with a brand new variant of governance exclusively for a table-top role-playing game seems a little misguided and selfish, not to mention injuriously improbable.<br /> -smile-<br /> Just as a final consideration (i mentioned this above), if you really get a chance to revisit some characterization to edit it, i'd personally adore the opportunity to see what exactly you change - just for some (possible) insight on how you manufacture (or stumble upon) these wonderful characters and the idiosyncratic writing you differentiate them with. Not a demand, but it would sure be interesting to me.<br /> Thanks again for the wonderful conversation, Ashnod. You've rather made my day with all your clever thinking and magnificent posts - i feel like my brain may be contracting some mush too now, so forgive me if i start to wind down from here. (E.G. i can't even focus enough to properly check this entry for errors.)<br /> But, i make no promises if you make any more intruiging posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T23:54:04-07:00","id":489120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=483484#post483484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> . . .I don't know. I know my little writer's ego pictures Sherazahde's work being dug up or researched in the Trinity-era, something akin to Offred's accounting of what happened in the Republic of Gilead in <i>The Handmaid's Tail</i>. It's a record of what happened during the Aberrant years. Who some of the people were. What they could do. How they were changed and what it meant to be a nova, and not an <i>aberrant</i>.<br /> <br /> But again, that's my ego speaking, and not the truth. The truth is I honestly loved the setting, and I loved writing about different facets of what it mean to suddenly be a superhumanly powered person.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I really liked about <b>Aberrant Nights </b>was your ability to write convincing characters, who felt like members of this or that faction, without hardwiring them into the metaplot. For example, all of the &quot;official&quot; Terats (except maybe Swarm Queen) are written with an eye towards the Aberrant War, skewing heavily towards nova supremacists and violent wackos who didn't really seem to do anything other than get ready for the War. <br /> <br /> But not Ashnod. She still reads Terat, from her ideals to her agenda to her friends, but she's a Terat in the &quot;real world&quot;. And she showcases an alternate path forward, besides an apocalyptic war between mundanes and novas. Frankly, the setting needs <i>more</i> characters like her, characters who have lives outside of the war narrative. Even if the War is unavoidable, characters such as Ashnod give the world more depth and color.<br /> <br /> Same with Malu. Her dark night of the soul, over Fracture and the rumors of Bahrain, are the first real signs I've seen of Utopians having doubts about their organization and its actions. The official Utopians have all made their decision, to stand by the Project, or to side with Corbin's Aberrants. There just aren't any good examples of characters on the fence. <br /> <br /> The only thing I never really cared for was the backstory for Machina. Interesting character, and an interesting way to introduce her (via an interview with a bitter employee). The gene splicing, though, doesn't really feel <i>Aberrant</i> to me. <br /> <br /> One question, though - why didn't you ever post the pieces involving &quot;V&quot; or &quot;Salamander&quot;? I like both of them as is, and they've been done for years. So why not go ahead and make them available to everyone?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T14:51:51-07:00","id":489886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=489120#post489120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I really liked about <b>Aberrant Nights </b>was your ability to write convincing characters, who felt like members of this or that faction, without hardwiring them into the metaplot. For example, all of the &quot;official&quot; Terats (except maybe Swarm Queen) are written with an eye towards the Aberrant War, skewing heavily towards nova supremacists and violent wackos who didn't really seem to do anything other than get ready for the War. <br /> <br /> But not Ashnod. She still reads Terat, from her ideals to her agenda to her friends, but she's a Terat in the &quot;real world&quot;. And she showcases an alternate path forward, besides an apocalyptic war between mundanes and novas. Frankly, the setting needs <i>more</i> characters like her, characters who have lives outside of the war narrative. Even if the War is unavoidable, characters such as Ashnod give the world more depth and color.<br /> <br /> Same with Malu. Her dark night of the soul, over Fracture and the rumors of Bahrain, are the first real signs I've seen of Utopians having doubts about their organization and its actions. The official Utopians have all made their decision, to stand by the Project, or to side with Corbin's Aberrants. There just aren't any good examples of characters on the fence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only thing I never really cared for was the backstory for Machina. Interesting character, and an interesting way to introduce her (via an interview with a bitter employee). The gene splicing, though, doesn't really feel <i>Aberrant</i> to me. </div> </div> </div>And honestly, were I writing it again, I might not include that. The problem is all of that info is rumor mill material, but the writer didn't fact check it. Ramsey never spliced her genetic material. That is what Pinchot thinks he overheard . She injected herself with it to see how her nova immune system would react to it, yes, but that was all. The connection to the chrysalis is an assumption on the part of the baselines. The interview was never aired, IIRC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One question, though - why didn't you ever post the pieces involving &quot;V&quot; or &quot;Salamander&quot;? I like both of them as is, and they've been done for years. So why not go ahead and make them available to everyone? </div> </div> </div>Three reasons. <br /> <br /> 1: I am lazy.<br /> 2: the eXistenZialist columns were not written when you read them. <br /> 3: I am lazy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","name":"Ashnod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T20:09:31-07:00","id":490153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=489886#post489886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I never really cared for was the backstory for Machina. Interesting character, and an interesting way to introduce her (via an interview with a bitter employee). The gene splicing, though, doesn't really feel <i>Aberrant</i> to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> And honestly, were I writing it again, I might not include that. The problem is all of that info is rumor mill material, but the writer didn't fact check it. Ramsey never spliced her genetic material. That is what Pinchot thinks he overheard . She injected herself with it to see how her nova immune system would react to it, yes, but that was all. The connection to the chrysalis is an assumption on the part of the baselines. The interview was never aired, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah . . .gotcha. I picked up on his attitude, but didn't get that he'd misheard. Makes more sense now. Out of curiosity, though, just what did she inject herself with? An alien organism? Another nova's tissue? Something created in a lab?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/427250-post-publishing-and-fan-made-materials?p=489886#post489886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question, though - why didn't you ever post the pieces involving &quot;V&quot; or &quot;Salamander&quot;? I like both of them as is, and they've been done for years. So why not go ahead and make them available to everyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Three reasons.<br /> <br /> 1: I am lazy.<br /> 2: the eXistenZialist columns were not written when you read them.<br /> 3: I am lazy</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the irony of saying you're lazy . . . .twice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Wait, does that mean the eXistenZialist columns are finished now, too?!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T23:55:34-07:00","id":490270,"title":"","content":"I think i've made my stance pretty clear, but i'd just like to thank you again for bringing Ashnod to my attention, One Vorlon. Excellent point with Malu being a questioning Utopian too, not enough of that in the setting. These people are meant to be wannabe-heroes, yet they toe the company line without turmoil?<br /> Lots of good thinking and perspective to be found in the 1001 Aberrant Nights stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:36:53-07:00","id":887287,"title":"","content":"I have started writing Aberrant-related fiction again. Nothing world-shattering, or anything, just snippets here and there in the handful of minutes I can spare. Actually having the creative spark again is invigorating. Coincidentally, Nihilist, I've kind of accepted the fact that 1,001 Aberrant Nights will probably not be updated in the near future, so if you still want to read the two pieces I held back, send me a message.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5534-ashnod","name":"Ashnod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T21:18:55-07:00","id":903258,"title":"","content":"I wasn't sure if this has been mentioned yet, but the people who put together the Aberrant: New Flesh, Aberrant: Forceful Personalities as well as some other fan published material have released another fan made PDF; <a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/files/file/93-aberrant-nexus/\" target=\"_blank\">Aberrant: Nexus.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There is no good or evil. There is only instinct corrupted by intelligence.","edited":{"userid":5273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","user":"KingOfDreams","date":". 05-30-2016, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5273-kingofdreams","name":"KingOfDreams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T10:10:21-07:00","id":904237,"title":"","content":"I didn';t have anything to do with it but I can say that reading it has inspired me to once again imagine using Aberrant, so I consider it an awesome and totally cool thing to be created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T17:40:37-07:00","id":947346,"title":"","content":"I personally thought India Underground was pretty good ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12232-breearg","name":"Breearg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T06:22:53-08:00","id":1016514,"title":"","content":"oh, damn - i've had a lot less time to post of late - i'd love to ask you a few questions Breearg, if you are who i think you are and you are still checking in now and then. IU was a really ambitious fan supplement and i've always wondered where some of the ideas and notions were came from and were going - from the creators of the book.<br /> Thanks for posting Breearg, i hope i get a chance to speak with you about your contributions to the delightful post-publishing run of Aeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}